1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:03,738
♪ IN THE NOT-TOO-DISTANT
FUTURE ♪

2
00:00:03,772 --> 00:00:06,775
♪ WAY DOWN IN DEEP 13 ♪

3
00:00:06,808 --> 00:00:09,643
♪ DR. FORRESTER
AND TV'S FRANK ♪

4
00:00:09,677 --> 00:00:12,847
♪ WERE HATCHING
AN EVIL SCHEME ♪

5
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:15,917
♪ THEY HIRED A TEMP
BY THE NAME OF MIKE ♪

6
00:00:15,950 --> 00:00:19,053
♪ JUST A REGULAR JOE
THEY DIDN'T LIKE ♪

7
00:00:19,087 --> 00:00:22,157
♪ THEIR EXPERIMENT
NEEDED A GOOD TEST CASE ♪

8
00:00:22,190 --> 00:00:23,725
♪ SO THEY CONKED HIM
ON THE NOGGIN ♪

9
00:00:23,758 --> 00:00:25,827
♪ AND THEY SHOT HIM INTO SPACE ♪

10
00:00:25,860 --> 00:00:28,362
GET ME DOWN!

11
00:00:28,395 --> 00:00:31,698
♪ WE'LL SEND HIM
CHEESY MOVIES ♪

12
00:00:31,732 --> 00:00:34,668
- ♪ THE WORST WE CAN FIND ♪
- ♪ LA-LA-LA ♪

13
00:00:34,702 --> 00:00:37,672
♪ HE'LL HAVE TO SIT
AND WATCH THEM ALL ♪

14
00:00:37,705 --> 00:00:41,108
- ♪ AND WE'LL MONITOR HIS MIND ♪
- ♪ LA-LA-LA ♪

15
00:00:41,142 --> 00:00:44,045
♪ NOW, KEEP IN MIND
MIKE CAN'T CONTROL ♪

16
00:00:44,078 --> 00:00:47,115
- ♪ WHERE THE MOVIES
BEGIN OR END ♪
- ♪ LA-LA-LA ♪

17
00:00:47,148 --> 00:00:50,185
♪ HE'LL TRY
TO KEEP HIS SANITY ♪

18
00:00:50,218 --> 00:00:53,555
♪ WITH THE HELP
OF HIS ROBOT FRIENDS ♪

19
00:00:55,290 --> 00:00:56,825
♪ ROBOT ROLL CALL ♪

20
00:00:56,858 --> 00:00:58,192
- CAMBOT!
- SHOW YOURSELF.

21
00:00:58,225 --> 00:00:59,460
I'M NOT READY.

22
00:00:59,493 --> 00:01:01,328
HELLO THERE.

23
00:01:01,362 --> 00:01:02,763
THAT'S ONE "O".

24
00:01:02,797 --> 00:01:05,867
♪ IF YOU'RE WONDERING
HOW HE EATS AND BREATHES ♪

25
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:09,037
- ♪ AND OTHER SCIENCE FACTS ♪
- ♪ LA-LA-LA ♪

26
00:01:09,070 --> 00:01:12,073
♪ JUST REPEAT TO YOURSELF,
"IT'S JUST A SHOW ♪

27
00:01:12,107 --> 00:01:15,008
♪ "I SHOULD
REALLY JUST RELAX ♪

28
00:01:15,042 --> 00:01:19,880
♪ FOR MYSTERY SCIENCE
THEATER 3000" ♪

29
00:01:33,762 --> 00:01:35,730
HI, EVERYONE. WELCOME
TO THE SATELLITE OF LOVE.

30
00:01:35,763 --> 00:01:39,100
I'M MIKE. AND YOU'RE JUST
IN TIME FOR THE FINAL DRESS
AND TECH REHEARSAL

31
00:01:39,133 --> 00:01:41,568
FOR LOVE LETTERS,
STARTING CROW T. ROBOT--

32
00:01:41,602 --> 00:01:43,070
- HELLO.
- ...AND TOM SERVO.

33
00:01:43,103 --> 00:01:44,472
- HELLO.
- YOU KNOW, LOVE LETTERS

34
00:01:44,505 --> 00:01:46,407
IS A LOT LIKE
SAME TIME, NEXT YEAR,

35
00:01:46,440 --> 00:01:48,342
ONLY YOU DON'T HAVE TO
REMEMBER ANY LINES.

36
00:01:48,375 --> 00:01:50,110
- READY, GUYS?
- YES. READY.

37
00:01:50,143 --> 00:01:52,847
AND... ANYTIME.

38
00:01:54,915 --> 00:01:58,953
"DEAR MELISSA,
HI, HOW ARE YOU?
I AM FINE.

39
00:01:58,987 --> 00:02:02,023
"REMEMBER WHEN
WE MET AT COLLEGE LAST YEAR
AND FELL IN LOVE?

40
00:02:02,057 --> 00:02:04,025
SINCERELY, ANDREW."

41
00:02:04,058 --> 00:02:06,160
"DEAR ANDREW,
I READ YOUR LETTER TODAY

42
00:02:06,193 --> 00:02:08,495
"AND WAS OVERCOME
WITH LOVE FOR YOU.

43
00:02:08,528 --> 00:02:10,465
"BY THE WAY,
I HAVE MARRIED STEVEN,

44
00:02:10,498 --> 00:02:12,533
"BUT WE'LL PROBABLY GROW APART.

45
00:02:12,567 --> 00:02:14,635
MORE LATER, MELISSA."

46
00:02:14,668 --> 00:02:17,905
"DEAR MELISSA, THAT'S OKAY.
I GOT MARRIED TOO.

47
00:02:17,938 --> 00:02:20,408
BUT I TOTALLY LOVE YOU,
ANDREW."

48
00:02:20,442 --> 00:02:23,243
"DEAR ANDREW,
I'M HAVING STEVEN'S BABY,

49
00:02:23,277 --> 00:02:26,447
"BUT I WANTED TO LET YOU KNOW
THAT IT'S YOU THAT I LOVE.

50
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:28,282
TAKE CARE, MELISSA."

51
00:02:28,315 --> 00:02:30,985
"DEAR MELISSA,
I TURNED MIDDLE-AGED THIS WEEK.

52
00:02:31,018 --> 00:02:33,453
"I'M A RICH WASP,
AND I LOVE YOU.

53
00:02:33,487 --> 00:02:35,490
ALL MY BEST, ANDREW."

54
00:02:35,523 --> 00:02:37,792
"DEAR ANDREW,
I'M A GRANDMOTHER NOW.

55
00:02:37,825 --> 00:02:39,593
"STEVEN AND I
HAVE GROWN APART.

56
00:02:39,627 --> 00:02:42,063
"GO FIGURE.
I DO SO LOVE YOU.

57
00:02:42,097 --> 00:02:44,065
STAY WELL, MELISSA."

58
00:02:44,098 --> 00:02:47,168
"DEAR MELISSA, MY CHILDREN
HAVE REPRODUCED ALSO.

59
00:02:47,202 --> 00:02:49,603
"OUR LOVE ENDURES
THROUGH THE YEARS, HUH?

60
00:02:49,637 --> 00:02:52,373
BOY, DO YOU I LOVE YOU.
REGARDS, ANDREW."

61
00:02:52,407 --> 00:02:54,108
- [CLAPPING]
- THANK YOU.
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

62
00:02:54,142 --> 00:02:57,345
- THAT WAS FANTASTIC.
BRAVO AND BRAVA.
- REALLY?

63
00:02:57,378 --> 00:03:00,080
I SAW STEPHANIE ZIMBALIST, JR.
AND CHRIS LEMMON DO THAT,

64
00:03:00,113 --> 00:03:03,150
AND THEY DID NOT DO IT JUSTICE
COMPARED TO YOU TWO GENTLEMEN.

65
00:03:03,183 --> 00:03:06,520
- SERVO THERE
WAS SETTING THE LINE.
- NO, NO. IT'S CROW. CROW--

66
00:03:06,553 --> 00:03:10,292
WELL, THEATER IS A GROUP THING,
AND YOU WERE ABLE
TO HOLD MOMENTS--

67
00:03:10,325 --> 00:03:13,527
- MOMENT BY MOMENT IS WHAT
THEATER IS ALL ABOUT.
- THERE WAS A MOMENT.

68
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:16,497
IT WAS A VERY EPHEMERAL THING,
AND IT WAS ALMOST NOT THERE.

69
00:03:16,530 --> 00:03:18,532
BUT IT WAS THERE.

70
00:03:18,565 --> 00:03:20,935
MM. YOU KNOW, SERVO, CROW,

71
00:03:20,968 --> 00:03:24,038
I'M NOT JUST A FRIEND OF YOURS,
I'M A FAN.

72
00:03:24,072 --> 00:03:26,507
OH, HEY, RUTH GORDON
AND GARSON KANIN ARE CALLING.

73
00:03:26,540 --> 00:03:28,375
- OH.
- DON'T STOP TOUCHING ME.

74
00:03:28,408 --> 00:03:31,278
UH, WE'RE NOT READY.
YOU GO FIRST.

75
00:03:31,312 --> 00:03:33,715
HEY, NO PROBLEM.
OUR INVENTION IS YOU.

76
00:03:33,748 --> 00:03:37,185
- I'M DR. CLAYTON FORRESTER.
- AND I'M TV'S FRANK.

77
00:03:37,218 --> 00:03:39,653
- SEE?
- [SNICKERING]

78
00:03:39,687 --> 00:03:42,590
CUTE. BUT I DON'T
QUITE UNDERSTAND THE--

79
00:03:42,623 --> 00:03:46,293
I'M DR. CLAYTON FORRESTER,
THE ONE WITH THE WEAK CHIN.

80
00:03:46,327 --> 00:03:51,065
I'M GOING TO HIT TV'S FRANK
BECAUSE OF MY DEEP RESENTMENT
AT MY OWN LIMITATIONS.

81
00:03:51,098 --> 00:03:53,067
I'M TV'S FRANK,
AND I'M GOING TO TAKE IT,

82
00:03:53,100 --> 00:03:55,168
BECAUSE I HAVE
NO SELF-CONFIDENCE.

83
00:03:55,202 --> 00:03:58,205
- OW, OW, OW!
- [LAUGHTER]

84
00:04:00,842 --> 00:04:03,543
WELL, YOU DO HAVE
KIND OF A WEAK CHIN.

85
00:04:03,577 --> 00:04:06,480
FORGET THE CHIN, FRANK.
DON'T YOU SEE WHAT'S HAPPENING?

86
00:04:06,513 --> 00:04:09,883
WE'RE LOSING THEIR RESPECT.
IT'S ALL ON THE LINE HERE, MAN.

87
00:04:09,917 --> 00:04:12,420
WE'VE GOTTA DO SOMETHING,
AND FAST!

88
00:04:12,453 --> 00:04:14,822
HEY, WE'RE JUST FUNNING YA.

89
00:04:14,855 --> 00:04:17,125
SHALL I HIT YOU AGAIN,
TV'S FRANK?

90
00:04:17,158 --> 00:04:19,093
- OH, PLEASE DO.
- [LAUGHTER CONTINUES]

91
00:04:19,127 --> 00:04:22,463
OW! OH, NOT SO HARD!

92
00:04:22,497 --> 00:04:24,832
ALL RIGHT, FRANK.
LET THEM HAVE IT.

93
00:04:24,865 --> 00:04:26,533
[MUFFLED]
I'M TOM SERVO,

94
00:04:26,567 --> 00:04:29,670
AND I'M A CUTE LITTLE GUY
WITH A ROUND HEAD.

95
00:04:29,703 --> 00:04:34,075
[LAUGHING]
AND I'VE GOT THESE LITTLE
ADORABLE ARMS.

96
00:04:34,108 --> 00:04:36,077
AND I'M CROW T. ROBOT,

97
00:04:36,110 --> 00:04:39,047
AND I'M GOLD,
AND I'M TRAPPED IN SPACE.

98
00:04:39,080 --> 00:04:42,683
WHAT A STUPID COLOR GOLD IS.
[LAUGHING]

99
00:04:45,318 --> 00:04:47,822
WELL, I TRUST YOU CAN SEE

100
00:04:47,855 --> 00:04:50,157
THAT TWO CAN PLAY
AT THAT GAME, NELSON.

101
00:04:50,190 --> 00:04:52,560
ANYWAY, YOUR EXPERIMENT
THIS WEEK

102
00:04:52,593 --> 00:04:55,028
IS CALLED THE ATOMIC BRAIN.

103
00:04:55,062 --> 00:04:57,565
PLUS THERE'S A SHORT
ABOUT THE GOLDEN AGE

104
00:04:57,598 --> 00:05:00,468
OF JUVENILE DELINQUENCY.
[LAUGHS]

105
00:05:00,502 --> 00:05:03,670
OH, FRANK, THAT'S VERY GOOD.
YOU'VE ALMOST GOT TOM DOWN.

106
00:05:03,703 --> 00:05:06,307
KEEP FLAPPING THOSE ARMS.
[LAUGHS]

107
00:05:06,340 --> 00:05:08,943
UH, YOU KEEP PRACTICING.
I'LL GET THE BUTTON.

108
00:05:08,977 --> 00:05:11,778
I'M DR. CLAYTON FORRESTER,
AND I'VE GOT MY HEAD STUCK--

109
00:05:11,812 --> 00:05:13,613
- [ALARM BLARING]
- THE MOVIE'S STARTING!

110
00:05:13,647 --> 00:05:15,148
[ALL SHOUTING]

111
00:05:25,893 --> 00:05:28,830
- ♪♪ [DRAMATIC]
- ♪♪ [HUMMING]

112
00:05:28,863 --> 00:05:32,200
- HEY, SAM EAGLE PRESENTS--
- HEY, IT IS.

113
00:05:34,402 --> 00:05:35,870
"WHAT ABOUT
JUVENILE DELINQUENCY."

114
00:05:35,903 --> 00:05:38,272
THAT'S A VIABLE CAREER OPTION.

115
00:05:38,305 --> 00:05:40,608
SURE. YEP.

116
00:05:42,343 --> 00:05:45,780
PAST PRESIDENT DISBARRED
FOR DELINQUENCY.

117
00:05:47,582 --> 00:05:51,685
AND, OF COURSE, MUSIC BY
THE ROYAL DELINQUENT ORCHESTRA,
PHILIP GANNEL CONDUCTOR.

118
00:05:51,718 --> 00:05:54,422
CENTRON-- THE DAWNING
OF A NEW DAY.

119
00:05:56,190 --> 00:05:58,625
[LAUGHS]
THE BARTON MILLNER GANG.

120
00:05:58,658 --> 00:06:01,262
OH, THEY'RE SO KLANDINCTU.

121
00:06:01,295 --> 00:06:03,263
HERE HE COMES.

122
00:06:03,297 --> 00:06:06,200
- HERE'S MY DAD TO PICK US UP.
- [LAUGHS]

123
00:06:06,233 --> 00:06:09,403
- COME ON, GUYS.
LET'S GO STUDY.
- WHOO!

124
00:06:09,437 --> 00:06:11,572
- WHERE ARE WE HEADING?
- I'LL TELL YOU
WHEN WE PICK UP JAMIE.

125
00:06:11,605 --> 00:06:13,607
IN OTHER WORDS, YOU DON'T KNOW.

126
00:06:16,943 --> 00:06:18,412
HMM.

127
00:06:18,445 --> 00:06:20,848
I'M SURE GLAD
WE GOT THE CAR WASHED.

128
00:06:20,882 --> 00:06:22,183
[LAUGHS]

129
00:06:22,217 --> 00:06:26,487
CANNONBALL RUN.
WELL WITHIN THE SPEED LIMIT.

130
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:28,655
- WHAT'S THAT GUY WAITING FOR?
- GIVE HIM A BUMP.

131
00:06:28,688 --> 00:06:29,757
YEAH.

132
00:06:29,790 --> 00:06:31,858
- GORDON JUMP.
- HIT HIM AGAIN.

133
00:06:31,892 --> 00:06:33,862
AW, CUT IT OUT.
WE'LL GET IN A JAM.

134
00:06:33,895 --> 00:06:36,330
- [MOCKING GIBBERISH]
- WHAT'S THE MATTER?
YOU THINKING OF SOMETHING?

135
00:06:36,363 --> 00:06:39,233
- COME ON! MOVE IT!
- CARS WERE MADE
TO TAKE IT BACK THEN.

136
00:06:39,267 --> 00:06:41,602
WHAT DO YOU PUNKS THINK
YOU'RE DOING ANYWAY?

137
00:06:41,635 --> 00:06:43,603
OUR MAYTAG BROKE, SIR.

138
00:06:43,637 --> 00:06:45,740
WHAT WAS THAT YOU CALLED US?

139
00:06:45,773 --> 00:06:48,442
I JUST BOUGHT THAT CAR.
NOW LOOK.

140
00:06:48,475 --> 00:06:51,145
HE'S CHANGING INTO
THE INCREDIBLE HULK.

141
00:06:51,178 --> 00:06:54,148
WHEN GOOD-NATURED RIBBING
GOES TOO FAR.

142
00:06:54,182 --> 00:06:55,917
- HMM.
- ♪♪ [UPBEAT JAZZ]

143
00:06:55,950 --> 00:06:57,918
[GASPS]
THEY FLATTENED HIM! OH!

144
00:06:57,952 --> 00:06:59,920
- OH.
- WHOO.

145
00:06:59,953 --> 00:07:02,623
OH, WILLARD SCOTT,
I'LL GENTLY POLISH YOU.

146
00:07:02,657 --> 00:07:03,958
BZZ. WHOO.

147
00:07:03,992 --> 00:07:06,827
I HAVE JUST ENOUGH TIME
TO GET INTO MY BO PEEP OUTFIT.

148
00:07:06,860 --> 00:07:09,730
- ♪♪ [CONTINUES]
- WHAT, DOES SHE LIVE
AT SHAKEY'S?

149
00:07:09,763 --> 00:07:11,765
OH, MOM,
DUSTING IS SO BOURGEOIS.

150
00:07:11,798 --> 00:07:13,600
DO YOU HAVE ANY HOMEWORK, JAMIE?

151
00:07:13,633 --> 00:07:16,103
- AND QUIT PLAYING THAT RAGTIME.
- I TOLD YOU, NO.

152
00:07:16,137 --> 00:07:19,007
I'M GOING OUT
AS SOON AS THE GUYS COME BY
AND GET ME.

153
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:20,908
- GROOVIN' J.D. HAIR.
- WHAT TIME IS IT?

154
00:07:20,942 --> 00:07:22,910
- IT'S ALREADY AFTER 8:00.
- WHOO!

155
00:07:22,943 --> 00:07:25,112
I DON'T KNOW WHY YOU CAN'T
STAY HOME FOR ONE EVENING.

156
00:07:25,145 --> 00:07:28,282
- MA, I CAN SEE UP YOUR DRESS.
- YOUR FATHER WILL BE HOME
IN A LITTLE BIT.

157
00:07:28,315 --> 00:07:29,950
HE SHOULD BE HOME NOW.

158
00:07:29,983 --> 00:07:31,852
JUST WHERE IS IT YOU'RE GOING,
JAMIE?

159
00:07:31,885 --> 00:07:34,322
- CRACK HOUSE. WHY?
- IF I KNEW, I'D TELL YOU.

160
00:07:34,355 --> 00:07:37,258
- I DON'T KNOW.
- DON'T KILL YOUR FATHER.

161
00:07:37,292 --> 00:07:40,493
WELL, AT LEAST MY DRESS
MATCHES THE WALLPAPER.

162
00:07:40,527 --> 00:07:42,730
HUH?

163
00:07:42,763 --> 00:07:45,600
OOH, ALL THE DARK TEENS.

164
00:07:45,633 --> 00:07:48,168
♪ DARKNESS, DARKNESS ♪

165
00:07:48,202 --> 00:07:50,838
[MUTTERING]

166
00:07:50,872 --> 00:07:52,907
A DRY CLEANER!

167
00:07:52,940 --> 00:07:55,408
ONE HOUR, GUYS.
LET'S MARTINIZE.

168
00:07:55,442 --> 00:07:58,045
USE THE DOORS, PLEASE.
YOU START OUT
NOT USING THE DOORS,

169
00:07:58,078 --> 00:08:00,682
NEXT THING YOU KNOW,
YOU'RE BEATING UP GORDON JUMP.

170
00:08:00,715 --> 00:08:03,317
[ALL CHANTING]
NORM! NORM! NORM!

171
00:08:03,350 --> 00:08:07,722
- NORM! NORM!
- [LAUGHTER]

172
00:08:07,755 --> 00:08:09,890
- ALL RIGHT! BRIDGE CLUB!
- WHOO!

173
00:08:09,923 --> 00:08:12,393
WHAT'LL YOU HAVE, BOYS?
I'LL WRITE YOUR ORDERS
WITH MY NEW PENCIL.

174
00:08:12,427 --> 00:08:13,895
HEY, THOSE ARE GREAT.

175
00:08:13,928 --> 00:08:16,530
MY DAD'S GOT ONE JUST LIKE IT.
WHERE'D YOU GET IT?

176
00:08:16,563 --> 00:08:18,900
[LAUGHS]
SHOP 'N SAVE.

177
00:08:18,933 --> 00:08:22,570
WE JUST SWARMED ALL OVER A GUY.
FELL OUT OF HIS POCKET.

178
00:08:22,603 --> 00:08:25,873
- WHAT? WHEN DID THIS HAPPEN?
- JUST BEFORE WE PICKED YOU UP.

179
00:08:25,907 --> 00:08:28,542
WE BUMPED SOME GUY
IN A BIG BUICK, AND HE GETS OUT
AND STARTS GETTING SMART.

180
00:08:28,575 --> 00:08:30,778
- DUH, SMART, YEAH.
- BOY, DID WE GIVE IT TO HIM.

181
00:08:30,812 --> 00:08:32,813
WE SURE MESSED HIM UP.
YOU SHOULD'VE BEEN THERE, JAMIE.

182
00:08:32,847 --> 00:08:35,048
- WHO WAS HE?
- I DON'T KNOW.
SOME BIG BALD-HEADED GUY.

183
00:08:35,082 --> 00:08:37,385
DO YOU SMELL ONIONS?

184
00:08:37,418 --> 00:08:39,120
WHAT KIND OF A CAR
DID YOU SAY IT WAS?

185
00:08:39,153 --> 00:08:41,288
- OH, IT WAS A--
- UH, THE FORDILLAC.

186
00:08:41,322 --> 00:08:44,192
WHAT'S THE MATTER WITH YOU?

187
00:08:44,225 --> 00:08:46,460
I ASKED YOU WHAT KIND
OF A CAR IT WAS.

188
00:08:46,493 --> 00:08:48,795
I WANNA KNOW.

189
00:08:49,897 --> 00:08:52,633
IT WAS A YELLOW BUICK.
WHY?

190
00:08:52,667 --> 00:08:55,703
JUST TRYING TO DRAW YOU OUT.
YOU WANT SOME FRIES?

191
00:08:55,737 --> 00:08:57,438
A FISHER SPACE PEN.

192
00:08:59,407 --> 00:09:02,377
WHAT DO YOU WANNA
KNOW FOR, JAMIE?

193
00:09:02,410 --> 00:09:05,847
WHERE'S THE LITTLE
DELINQUENTS' ROOM?

194
00:09:05,880 --> 00:09:08,748
GET THIS THING OFF ME!
[GRUNTING]

195
00:09:08,782 --> 00:09:10,350
[HUFFS]

196
00:09:10,383 --> 00:09:13,553
YOU'RE GONNA MISS
THE SOUP OF THE DAY, JERK.

197
00:09:13,587 --> 00:09:15,055
- WHAT'S HIS TROUBLE?
- I DON'T KNOW,

198
00:09:15,088 --> 00:09:16,757
BUT THIS ISN'T THE PLACE
TO FIND OUT.

199
00:09:16,790 --> 00:09:18,960
- THE NO SHOULDER GANG.
- WE'LL SEE HIM IN THE MORNING
AT SCHOOL

200
00:09:18,993 --> 00:09:20,628
WHEN WE GIVE THIS TO HIM.

201
00:09:20,662 --> 00:09:22,663
WE GOTTA GET BETTER PATCHES.

202
00:09:23,998 --> 00:09:25,598
OOH! OW!

203
00:09:25,632 --> 00:09:29,103
- DEAR, IT'S JUST LEMON JUICE.
- OHH, OW!

204
00:09:29,137 --> 00:09:31,238
- JAMIE!
- HOW'S DAD?

205
00:09:31,272 --> 00:09:33,740
- HOW DID YOU KNOW?
- HE'S ALWAYS BEEN MY DAD.

206
00:09:33,773 --> 00:09:35,777
I HEARD IT OVER THE RADIO.

207
00:09:35,810 --> 00:09:37,778
HOW IS HE?

208
00:09:37,812 --> 00:09:40,347
- HE'LL BE ALL RIGHT.
- HE'S KIND OF RUBBERY.

209
00:09:40,380 --> 00:09:42,450
- HE'S RESTING NOW.
- OR HE'S DEAD.

210
00:09:42,483 --> 00:09:43,985
IT'S HARD TO TELL WITH HIM.

211
00:09:44,018 --> 00:09:46,453
HE WAS TERRIBLY SHAKEN UP
AND BRUISED, THOUGH.

212
00:09:46,487 --> 00:09:48,022
AND THEY TOOK HIS PENCIL POUCH.

213
00:09:48,055 --> 00:09:50,523
OH, IT MAKES ME SICK
TO THINK ABOUT IT.

214
00:09:50,557 --> 00:09:53,460
WHEN DID HIS NOSE
GET MILDEW?

215
00:09:53,493 --> 00:09:54,862
JAMIE...

216
00:09:54,895 --> 00:09:56,697
MASSAGE ME, WILL YOU?

217
00:09:56,730 --> 00:09:59,200
I'M SORRY, DAD.

218
00:09:59,233 --> 00:10:00,702
I'M SORRY.

219
00:10:00,735 --> 00:10:02,637
I'M SORRY I'M NOT
THE DAUGHTER YOU WANTED.

220
00:10:02,670 --> 00:10:07,073
IT'S NOTHING FOR YOU
TO BE SORRY ABOUT, SON.
WASN'T YOUR FAULT.

221
00:10:07,107 --> 00:10:11,212
EH, THE NEXT WEEKEND,
DAD'S GOLF BUDDIES COME
AND BEAT UP JAMIE.

222
00:10:11,245 --> 00:10:14,915
SON, YOU HAVE ANGEL-HAIR PASTA
ON YOUR SHIRT.

223
00:10:14,948 --> 00:10:17,818
I WONDER IF THIS
IS GONNA GET MELODRAMATIC.

224
00:10:17,852 --> 00:10:20,087
OKAY, COME ON.
I'LL TAKE YOU BOTH ON.

225
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:23,523
I'M ALL RIGHT NOW.
YOU'D BETTER GET UPSTAIRS
TO BED.

226
00:10:23,557 --> 00:10:25,993
- AND I'LL BE UP IN A MINUTE.
- ♪♪ [DRAMATIC]

227
00:10:26,027 --> 00:10:27,995
- I'M SORRY, DAD.
- NOW, AT THIS POINT HERE,

228
00:10:28,028 --> 00:10:29,930
THE MOOD SHIFTS
TO A LOVELY ADAGIO.

229
00:10:29,963 --> 00:10:33,933
- IT'S FANTASTIC.
- YOU EXPECTING A FLOOD, SON?

230
00:10:33,967 --> 00:10:37,438
IT'S JUST UPSTAIRS
AND TO THE LEFT, SON,
WHERE IT ALWAYS WAS.

231
00:10:39,807 --> 00:10:42,777
- WE'RE ALONE. LOVE ME!
- DARLING.

232
00:10:42,810 --> 00:10:44,312
HUH.

233
00:10:47,482 --> 00:10:49,883
♪ IT'S THE EYE OF THE T-- ♪
OH, BOY.

234
00:10:49,917 --> 00:10:52,853
WE BROUGHT YOUR TASTY SHAKE.

235
00:10:54,788 --> 00:10:56,890
♪♪ [WHISTLING THEME FROM
THE GOOD, THE BAD AND THE UGLY]

236
00:10:56,923 --> 00:10:58,858
[IMITATING SOUND
OF SPURS CLINKING]

237
00:10:58,892 --> 00:11:00,828
[IMITATING WOLF HOWLING
IN DISTANCE]

238
00:11:03,330 --> 00:11:06,300
IT'S A BELLBOY CONVENTION.

239
00:11:06,333 --> 00:11:09,403
- BETTER TAKE THIS BACK, JAMIE.
- WE DIDN'T KNOW
IT WAS YOUR DAD, JAMIE.

240
00:11:09,437 --> 00:11:11,605
- WE WOULDN'T HAVE DONE IT
IF WE'D KNOWN.
- LEAVE ME ALONE.

241
00:11:11,638 --> 00:11:13,540
- TAKE IT, JAMIE.
- YOU KEEP IT.

242
00:11:13,573 --> 00:11:14,942
WE'RE TRYING TO SAY WE'RE SORRY.

243
00:11:14,975 --> 00:11:16,510
I DON'T WANT ANYTHING MORE
TO DO WITH YOU.

244
00:11:16,543 --> 00:11:18,178
NOW, LOOK, JAMIE.
DON'T GET SMART.

245
00:11:18,212 --> 00:11:20,447
DON'T FORGET,
YOU COULD'VE BEEN ALONG
INSTEAD OF ONE OF US.

246
00:11:20,480 --> 00:11:23,450
- COULD'VE BEEN ONE OF OUR DADS.
- TELL YOU WHAT,
YOU CAN BEAT UP MY DAD.

247
00:11:23,483 --> 00:11:26,187
WOULDN'T SEE ME MOPING AROUND
IF IT HAD BEEN MY OLD MAN.

248
00:11:26,220 --> 00:11:28,755
DON'T WORRY.
I'M NOT FORGETTING A THING.

249
00:11:28,788 --> 00:11:30,958
JUST COUNT ME OUT FROM NOW ON.

250
00:11:30,992 --> 00:11:32,493
- [GIRL] THERE HE IS.
- MY BACKUP'S HERE.

251
00:11:32,527 --> 00:11:34,060
- WE WANNA TALK TO YOU.
- HE'S BUSY.

252
00:11:34,093 --> 00:11:36,163
- DID YOU HAVE AN APPOINTMENT?
- GIVE ME A STATEMENT.

253
00:11:36,197 --> 00:11:38,832
HAVE YOU READ ABOUT THE SPECIAL
SESSION OF THE CITY COUNCIL
THEY'RE HAVING THIS MORNING?

254
00:11:38,865 --> 00:11:40,367
AND ALL THE THINGS
THEY'RE TALKING ABOUT DOING--

255
00:11:40,400 --> 00:11:43,103
A CURFEW, UPPING THE AGE
OF DRIVER'S LICENSES,

256
00:11:43,137 --> 00:11:46,340
CANCELING THE FOOTBALL GAMES,
THE PARTIES, THE DANCES,
AND EVERYTHING ELSE.

257
00:11:46,373 --> 00:11:47,742
- AND THERE'S WITCHES.
- IT ISN'T FAIR.

258
00:11:47,775 --> 00:11:49,477
MOST OF THE HIGH SCHOOL STUDENTS

259
00:11:49,510 --> 00:11:51,878
HAVEN'T HAD ANYTHING TO DO
WITH THE THINGS
THAT HAVE BEEN HAPPENING.

260
00:11:51,912 --> 00:11:54,080
LIKE LAST NIGHT,
AND THE STATUE THAT WAS BROKEN,

261
00:11:54,113 --> 00:11:55,482
AND THE THEATER SEATS,
AND ALL THAT.

262
00:11:55,515 --> 00:11:56,817
AND THE SUEZ CANAL INCIDENT.

263
00:11:56,850 --> 00:11:58,385
BUT WE'RE ALL GOING
TO SUFFER FOR IT.

264
00:11:58,418 --> 00:12:00,187
I DIDN'T HAVE ANYTHING
TO DO WITH IT EITHER.

265
00:12:00,220 --> 00:12:02,890
- AND DON'T LOOK AT US.
- WE DIDN'T KICK OVER
ANY STATUES.

266
00:12:02,923 --> 00:12:06,027
- YOU'VE GOT TO HELP US, JAMIE.
- WHAT DO YOU EXPECT ME TO DO?

267
00:12:06,060 --> 00:12:08,062
[OVERLAPPING SHOUTING]

268
00:12:08,095 --> 00:12:11,032
[MOCK CRYING]

269
00:12:11,065 --> 00:12:14,067
MR. McPHERSON SAID WE COULD GO.
HE EXCUSED US FROM SCHOOL.

270
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:16,137
AND HE SAID
YOU COULD GO WITH US.

271
00:12:16,170 --> 00:12:19,140
LOOK, ALL OF YOU,
LEAVE ME OUT OF EVERYTHING
YOU'RE PLANNING.

272
00:12:19,173 --> 00:12:21,508
- ALL I WANNA DO
IS MIND MY OWN BUSINESS.
- YEAH, EVERYTHING.

273
00:12:21,542 --> 00:12:25,245
- BUT THIS IS YOUR BUSINESS.
- YOU HEARD HIM.
HE'S NOT GOING ANYWHERE.

274
00:12:25,278 --> 00:12:28,448
HE'S NO SAP.
WE'RE GOING TO THE CITY COUNCIL.

275
00:12:28,482 --> 00:12:30,583
- [LAUGHTER]
- [MOCK LAUGHTER]

276
00:12:30,617 --> 00:12:34,053
RIGHT NOW, YOU GUYS
ARE MORE AFRAID THAN WE ARE,
BUT YOU'RE NOT FOOLING US.

277
00:12:34,087 --> 00:12:36,590
- YOU THINK YOU CAN LAUGH
AT ANYBODY WHO STANDS UP TO YOU.
- OH!

278
00:12:36,623 --> 00:12:38,792
- PARTNER, WHOO.
- AND PRETTY SOON, EVERYONE
ELSE IS LAUGHING AT HIM.

279
00:12:38,825 --> 00:12:40,895
- AND YOU THINK YOU'VE WON?
- NEXT CARD, PLEASE.
THANK YOU.

280
00:12:40,928 --> 00:12:44,265
WELL, I DON'T CARE
IF YOU LAUGH OR NOT.
IT WON'T BE FUNNY

281
00:12:44,298 --> 00:12:46,533
- ...IF THE CITY COUNCIL DOES
WHAT THEY'RE TALKING ABOUT.
- WHEW!

282
00:12:46,567 --> 00:12:50,637
I WOULDN'T ADVISE ANY OF YOU
TO GO TO THAT MEETING,
IF I WERE YOU.

283
00:12:50,670 --> 00:12:53,307
- I'M WARNING YOU.
- ARE YOU GOING WITH US, JAMIE?

284
00:12:53,340 --> 00:12:55,308
- NO, HE'S NOT.
- I'M TALKING TO JAMIE.

285
00:12:55,342 --> 00:12:57,377
♪ TORN BETWEEN TWO PEER GROUPS ♪

286
00:12:57,410 --> 00:13:01,415
- WHAT DO YOU WANT ME TO DO?
- THEY'LL LISTEN TO YOU, JAMIE,
BECAUSE IT WAS YOUR DAD THAT...

287
00:13:01,448 --> 00:13:03,317
AWKWARD.

288
00:13:08,155 --> 00:13:11,558
- PERMIT ME TO SING SOMETHING
FROM MAN OF LA MANCHA.
- I'LL GO WITH YOU.

289
00:13:11,592 --> 00:13:14,093
- YOU'RE NOT GOING ANYWHERE.
- [FOOTSTEPS]

290
00:13:14,127 --> 00:13:17,063
- HMM?
- MARTHA GRAHAM! RUN!

291
00:13:17,097 --> 00:13:20,767
YOU BOYS HAVEN'T BEEN MOVING
THE STUFF VERY WELL.

292
00:13:22,135 --> 00:13:23,637
[QUIETLY]
I'M WATCHING YOU.

293
00:13:23,670 --> 00:13:25,605
THIS IS MY TURF NOW.

294
00:13:27,007 --> 00:13:28,842
[LAUGHING]

295
00:13:30,577 --> 00:13:32,045
♪♪ [IMITATING MOD SQUAD THEME]

296
00:13:32,078 --> 00:13:34,047
PETE, LINC, JULIE, AND...

297
00:13:34,080 --> 00:13:36,083
- STEVE?
- HUH?

298
00:13:37,250 --> 00:13:39,487
WHOA! BANANA PEEL!

299
00:13:39,520 --> 00:13:41,522
- I CALL SHOTGUN!
- [LAUGHS]

300
00:13:41,555 --> 00:13:43,690
- NO, NO, NO! WRONG WAY!
- WHOA!

301
00:13:43,723 --> 00:13:45,927
- BACK UP.
- THERE WE GO.

302
00:13:45,960 --> 00:13:49,997
ELIOT NESS AND HIS UNTOUCHABLES
WERE IN HOT PURSUIT.

303
00:13:50,030 --> 00:13:53,000
- GET TO THE HELICOPTER!
THE HELICOPTER!
- GET THE CAR!

304
00:13:54,502 --> 00:13:56,803
MEANWHILE,
BACK AT THE CONVENT...

305
00:13:56,837 --> 00:14:00,140
THIS IS 100% PURE DEMOCRACY.

306
00:14:01,908 --> 00:14:05,745
OKAY, EVERYBODY,
HURRY UP AND VOTE! COME ON!

307
00:14:05,778 --> 00:14:07,715
♪♪ [IMITATING SOUNDTRACK]

308
00:14:09,550 --> 00:14:12,118
WHOA. HOLD ON.
LET ME GET SOME LITERATURE.

309
00:14:12,152 --> 00:14:17,123
WHAT'S THE RUSH?
THERE'S GONNA BE THREE HOURS
OF ZONING STUFF FIRST.

310
00:14:17,157 --> 00:14:19,593
WE'RE NOT TALKING ABOUT PRANKS
AND LETTING OFF STEAM,

311
00:14:19,627 --> 00:14:21,695
WE'RE TALKING ABOUT
CRIMINAL ACTS FOR MILES!

312
00:14:21,728 --> 00:14:24,532
- WE'RE TALKING ABOUT TROUBLE
RIGHT HERE IN RIVER CITY!
- IF THESE KIDS WANNA GO AROUND

313
00:14:24,565 --> 00:14:27,367
BEATING UP PEOPLE
AND WRECKING THINGS
TO PROVE HOW TOUGH THEY ARE,

314
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:29,937
THEN IT'S TIME WE PROVE TO THEM
JUST HOW TOUGH WE ARE!

315
00:14:29,970 --> 00:14:32,138
- [MIMICKING, GIBBERISH]
- CAN WE SAY SOMETHING?

316
00:14:32,172 --> 00:14:33,840
- I'M SORRY--
- WHAT'S ALL THIS?

317
00:14:33,873 --> 00:14:36,710
DO YOU HAVE
SOME FACTS TO GIVE US
THAT WE DON'T ALREADY HAVE?

318
00:14:36,743 --> 00:14:38,712
I DON'T KNOW WHETHER
YOU'D CALL THEM FACTS OR NOT,

319
00:14:38,745 --> 00:14:41,248
BUT, WELL, EVERYBODY
KEEPS TALKING ABOUT TEENAGERS

320
00:14:41,282 --> 00:14:43,183
AS IF WE WERE A BUNCH OF FREAKS
OR SOMETHING.

321
00:14:43,217 --> 00:14:45,718
WE'RE JUST WASTING TIME.
WE'VE WASTED
TOO MUCH TIME ALREADY.

322
00:14:45,752 --> 00:14:47,722
- KILL THEM ALL!
- WE'VE INVITED
MR. McPHERSON HERE.

323
00:14:47,755 --> 00:14:49,055
HE'S PRINCIPAL
OF THE HIGH SCHOOL.

324
00:14:49,088 --> 00:14:51,358
AND HE CAN TELL US ANYTHING
THESE KIDS CAN TELL US.

325
00:14:51,392 --> 00:14:53,427
- NO, NO. I'M SORRY. I CAN'T.
- [OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

326
00:14:53,460 --> 00:14:56,963
- I'M TOO NOODILY.
- THAT'S WHY WHEN THESE STUDENTS
CAME TO ME TODAY,

327
00:14:56,997 --> 00:14:59,367
I ASKED THEM IF THEY'D
BE WILLING TO COME DOWN HERE

328
00:14:59,400 --> 00:15:01,168
AND PUT THEIR CASE BEFORE YOU.

329
00:15:01,202 --> 00:15:04,070
- IS THAT OKAY?
- AND I THINK YOU SHOULD HEAR
WHAT THEY HAVE TO SAY.

330
00:15:04,103 --> 00:15:06,573
- I GIVE YOU CHEETAH CHROME.
- THIS IS BILL STILLWELL,

331
00:15:06,607 --> 00:15:08,575
THE HEAD OF THE STUDENT COUNCIL,

332
00:15:08,608 --> 00:15:11,478
AND CHUCK LEEWOOD,
CAPTAIN OF OUR FOOTBALL TEAM.

333
00:15:11,512 --> 00:15:14,948
- HUT!
- AND SALLY LAWRENCE HERE,
THE SENIOR CLASS PRESIDENT.

334
00:15:14,982 --> 00:15:18,752
- SHE'S A GIRL.
- AND JAMIE. JAMIE'S DAD WAS
THE ONE WHO GOT HURT LAST NIGHT.

335
00:15:18,785 --> 00:15:20,053
- MR. MAYOR--
- I LOVE YOU.

336
00:15:20,087 --> 00:15:21,888
...I THINK
MR. McPHERSON'S RIGHT,

337
00:15:21,922 --> 00:15:24,525
AND I THINK THESE STUDENTS
ARE RIGHT TOO.

338
00:15:24,558 --> 00:15:26,627
TEENAGERS
AREN'T ALL DELINQUENTS.

339
00:15:26,660 --> 00:15:28,328
- ONLY A FEW ARE INVOLVED
- [WHISPERING]

340
00:15:28,362 --> 00:15:30,697
IN THESE CRIMINAL ACTS
THAT WE'RE ALL CONCERNED ABOUT.

341
00:15:30,730 --> 00:15:34,167
- IF THESE TEENAGERS,
WHO REPRESENT ALL OF THE REST--
- [WHISPERING] HEY.

342
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:35,902
- ...HAVE THE COURAGE
TO COME HERE,
- [CHUCKLING]

343
00:15:35,935 --> 00:15:38,405
THEN I THINK WE SHOULD
NOT ONLY LISTEN TO THEM,
BUT I THINK WE SHOULD--

344
00:15:38,438 --> 00:15:41,808
- OBEY THEM!
- ...INVITE THEM TO HELP US
STAMP OUT THIS VANDALISM.

345
00:15:41,842 --> 00:15:43,610
I SAY LET'S LET THEM TALK.

346
00:15:43,643 --> 00:15:46,113
- I SAY LET'S PUT THEM
THROUGH THE SPANKING MACHINE.
- ALL RIGHT.

347
00:15:46,147 --> 00:15:47,815
WHOO, YES.

348
00:15:47,848 --> 00:15:50,583
AND TONY BOUZA IS INTRODUCED.

349
00:15:50,617 --> 00:15:52,552
WE DON'T WANT TO PUNISH
ALL TEENAGERS

350
00:15:52,585 --> 00:15:54,220
FOR THE TROUBLE
A FEW ARE CAUSING--

351
00:15:54,253 --> 00:15:56,223
- JUST YOU.
- ...BUT SOMETHING
HAS TO BE DONE.

352
00:15:56,257 --> 00:16:00,860
YOU KNOW HOW SERIOUS
THE JUVENILE DELINQUENCY PROBLEM
HAS BECOME.

353
00:16:00,893 --> 00:16:04,598
WE HAVE TO TAKE SOME ACTION
TO PREVENT THIS SORT OF THING
FROM HAPPENING AGAIN.

354
00:16:04,632 --> 00:16:08,368
- WHY, HE'S QUITE GOOD.
- NOW, IF YOU HAVE SOME
SUGGESTIONS TO OFFER,

355
00:16:08,402 --> 00:16:10,603
- ...WE'RE WILLING
TO LISTEN TO YOU.
- AND THEN KILL YOU.

356
00:16:10,637 --> 00:16:14,408
WHAT CAN WE DO,
AND WHAT CAN YOU DO
TO PREVENT--

357
00:16:14,442 --> 00:16:16,477
- FOREST FIRES.
- ...JUVENILE DELINQUENCY?

358
00:16:16,510 --> 00:16:18,478
- YOU TELL US.
- YEAH?

359
00:16:18,512 --> 00:16:20,280
THEY CALLED OUR BLUFF.
WHAT DO WE DO?

360
00:16:20,313 --> 00:16:23,483
I THINK THEY'RE STILL TALKING
ABOUT ZONING STUFF.

361
00:16:24,885 --> 00:16:28,155
I OFFER MYSELF
AS A VIRGIN SACRIFICE.

362
00:16:29,757 --> 00:16:31,792
[NARRATOR]
WHAT WOULD YOU DO
IF YOU WERE JAMIE?

363
00:16:31,825 --> 00:16:33,793
- THAT'S PRINCE'S NEW NAME,
ISN'T IT?
- WHAT CAN WE DO--

364
00:16:33,827 --> 00:16:36,963
- NO, IT'S FRANK GORSHIN'S
NEW NAME.
- ...ABOUT JUVENILE DELINQUENCY?

365
00:16:36,997 --> 00:16:39,800
- WHAT WOULD YOU SAY?
- "WHAT WOULD YOU SAY?"

366
00:16:39,833 --> 00:16:41,768
- [LAUGHS]
- ♪ YOUNG AMERICAN ♪

367
00:16:41,802 --> 00:16:44,872
♪ YOUNG AMERICAN,
HE WAS A YOUNG AMERICAN ♪

368
00:16:44,905 --> 00:16:47,273
♪♪ [VOCALIZING]

369
00:16:53,880 --> 00:16:55,348
OH, HERE IT IS.

370
00:16:55,382 --> 00:16:57,017
[NARRATOR]
CAN DEATH BE OUTWITTED?

371
00:16:57,050 --> 00:16:58,785
LIKE SANDS
THROUGH THE HOURGLASS...

372
00:16:58,818 --> 00:17:02,790
IS THE SECRET OF ETERNAL LIFE
JUST AROUND THAT CORNER?

373
00:17:02,823 --> 00:17:05,825
TODAY, MEDICAL SCIENCE
PATCHES UP MUTILATED BODIES,

374
00:17:05,858 --> 00:17:07,762
TRANSPLANTING HUMAN SKIN,

375
00:17:07,795 --> 00:17:09,763
EYES, LIMBS,
EVEN VITAL ORGANS.

376
00:17:09,797 --> 00:17:11,498
GOLGI APPARATUS.

377
00:17:11,532 --> 00:17:14,367
IS THE NEXT STEP
THE TRANSPLANTATION
OF THE HUMAN BRAIN?

378
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:17,403
- THE PANTRY OF THE FUTURE.
- MANY SCIENTISTS ANSWER YES,

379
00:17:17,437 --> 00:17:19,272
BUT THEY PAUSE
AND ADD A GRIM WARNING.

380
00:17:19,305 --> 00:17:21,675
- OH, HEY, WE'RE OUT OF PAPER.
- FOR IN THE ANCIENT
FOLK LEGENDS,

381
00:17:21,708 --> 00:17:24,912
TALES ARE TOLD
OF BLOODSUCKING VAMPIRES

382
00:17:24,945 --> 00:17:28,282
CRAWLING OUT OF GRAVES
TO LIVE IN THE BODIES
OF HELPLESS VICTIMS.

383
00:17:28,315 --> 00:17:31,218
- BUT THAT'S ANOTHER MOVIE.
- IS MAN NOW DOOMED
TO PRODUCE A RACE

384
00:17:31,252 --> 00:17:33,220
OF EVER-LIVING MONSTROSITIES--

385
00:17:33,253 --> 00:17:35,488
- HUH?
- ...WORSE THAN THE VAMPIRES
OF LEGEND?

386
00:17:35,522 --> 00:17:37,490
- HEY, WAIT A MINUTE!
- WILL RUTHLESS MEN AND WOMEN--

387
00:17:37,523 --> 00:17:39,493
- SHE'S NUDE!
- LADY!

388
00:17:39,527 --> 00:17:43,163
...LEGALLY BUY OR STEAL
THE LIVING BODIES
OF THE YOUNG AND BEAUTIFUL

389
00:17:43,197 --> 00:17:46,133
SO THEIR BRAINS
MAY LIVE ON FOREVER?

390
00:17:46,167 --> 00:17:48,735
- SUCH QUESTIONS
MAY SEEM FANCIFUL--
- OR DOWNRIGHT STUPID.

391
00:17:48,768 --> 00:17:50,670
...BUT AT THIS VERY MOMENT,
SCIENTISTS ARE WORKING

392
00:17:50,703 --> 00:17:53,007
ON THE ANSWER
TO BRAIN TRANSPLANTATION--

393
00:17:53,040 --> 00:17:56,977
- THAT'S NOT ALL
THEY'RE WORKING ON.
- ...AND HUMAN BODIES ARE USED.

394
00:17:57,010 --> 00:17:58,478
BUT ENOUGH ABOUT ME.

395
00:17:58,512 --> 00:18:01,482
THIS GIRL WAS BURIED
IN A NEARBY CEMETERY YESTERDAY.

396
00:18:01,515 --> 00:18:05,285
- THAT'S NOT A GIRL.
- ONLY A FEW HOURS AGO,
HER BODY WAS STOLEN--

397
00:18:05,318 --> 00:18:06,920
NOW, THAT'S A GIRL.

398
00:18:06,953 --> 00:18:09,155
...BY DR. OTTO FRANK

399
00:18:09,188 --> 00:18:11,858
- ...AND BROUGHT TO
THIS HIDDEN LABORATORY.
- SHOULD WE BE LOOKING AT THIS?

400
00:18:11,892 --> 00:18:13,860
HE HAS GRAFTED
A LIVING ANIMAL'S BRAIN

401
00:18:13,893 --> 00:18:15,562
INTO THIS NEWLY DEAD BODY.

402
00:18:15,595 --> 00:18:18,798
- WHAT A KNUCKLE-KNOB.
- IF THE EXPERIMENT WORKS,

403
00:18:18,832 --> 00:18:22,235
THE NEXT STEP WILL BE
THE TRANSPLANTATION
OF A HUMAN BRAIN.

404
00:18:22,268 --> 00:18:24,237
AND IF IT DOESN'T WORK,
IT'S THE COMPOST HEAP.

405
00:18:24,270 --> 00:18:26,038
THE BRAIN CELLS
ARE BEING REACTIVATED

406
00:18:26,072 --> 00:18:28,975
BY AN ATOMIC FISSION
PRODUCED IN THE CYCLOTRON.

407
00:18:29,008 --> 00:18:31,645
ISN'T THAT A RIDE
AT THE STATE FAIR?

408
00:18:31,678 --> 00:18:34,047
[WHISPERS]
CYCLONE.

409
00:18:34,080 --> 00:18:36,048
[IMITATING LIQUID BUBBLING]

410
00:18:36,082 --> 00:18:38,485
AND THE TIME'S UP.
HOW MUCH HAVE YOU RISKED?

411
00:18:38,518 --> 00:18:40,653
ALL OF IT? OOH.

412
00:18:40,687 --> 00:18:44,290
DO NOT ADJUST YOUR DRYER.
WE CONTROL YOUR AIR FLUFF.

413
00:18:44,323 --> 00:18:45,492
[CHUCKLING]

414
00:18:45,525 --> 00:18:47,827
HAS HE FOUND THE WAY
TO OUTWIT DEATH?

415
00:18:47,860 --> 00:18:51,865
- WHO, DURK PEARSON?
- OR HAS HE CREATED
ANOTHER MONSTROS--

416
00:18:51,898 --> 00:18:55,202
- WHAT? ANOTHER WHAT?
- I MISSED IT.

417
00:18:55,235 --> 00:18:57,770
[RAPPING]
♪ I'M A DOCTOR, YEAH,
MY NAME IS JED ♪

418
00:18:57,803 --> 00:19:00,273
- ♪♪ [BEATBOXING]
- ♪ I LIKE TO WEAR
THIS STUPID HAT ♪

419
00:19:00,307 --> 00:19:03,577
- HUH? OH.
- YOU KNOW, GUYS, PEOPLE ARE
JUST DYING TO GET IN THERE.

420
00:19:03,610 --> 00:19:05,978
- DOH!
- KNOW HOW MANY PEOPLE
ARE BURIED IN THERE?

421
00:19:06,012 --> 00:19:07,480
- ALL OF THEM!
- [LAUGHS]

422
00:19:07,513 --> 00:19:09,482
- THANK YOU.
- [LAUGHS]

423
00:19:09,515 --> 00:19:11,685
LOOKS LIKE JOE ORTON
WOULD MEET SOMEONE THERE.

424
00:19:11,718 --> 00:19:13,153
[CHUCKLES]

425
00:19:16,857 --> 00:19:19,492
HEY, KEEP IT QUIET IN THERE.
HAH! JUST KIDDING.

426
00:19:19,525 --> 00:19:21,127
LOVE THAT ONE.

427
00:19:23,097 --> 00:19:24,998
IT'S BARNEY MOONLIGHTING.

428
00:19:25,032 --> 00:19:26,600
♪♪ [WHISTLING]

429
00:19:26,633 --> 00:19:29,202
[IMITATING BARNEY FIFE]
YEAH, I THOUGHT I'D TAKE
THELMA LOU

430
00:19:29,235 --> 00:19:32,505
OVER TO MY PILOT
FOR A PICTURE SHOW.

431
00:19:32,538 --> 00:19:35,042
- DEEP BELOW, DR. FRANK
TAKES THE CHANCE--
- AAH!

432
00:19:35,075 --> 00:19:37,377
...OF SMASHING HIS WAY
INTO A NEWLY SEALED VAULT.

433
00:19:37,410 --> 00:19:40,080
HIS EXPERIMENTS CANNOT CONTINUE
WITHOUT ANOTHER BODY.

434
00:19:40,113 --> 00:19:42,448
- IT'S CHRISTMAS AT THE VAULT.
- OH, NICE.

435
00:19:44,785 --> 00:19:47,487
- IT'S A GARY COLEMAN MEMORIAL.
- [LAUGHS]

436
00:19:50,690 --> 00:19:52,692
- WHOA, WHOA.
- HEY, HEY, HEY, HEY, HEY.

437
00:19:52,725 --> 00:19:55,728
THE WATCHMAN'S MIND
WAS NOT ON BODY SNATCHERS--

438
00:19:55,762 --> 00:19:58,198
- STARSKY AND--
- ...JUST HIS USUAL NIP.

439
00:19:58,232 --> 00:19:59,700
[LAUGHS]
YEAH.

440
00:19:59,733 --> 00:20:01,302
[IMITATING GUZZLING]

441
00:20:02,902 --> 00:20:06,773
- OH, GOD,
THAT'S GOOD EXPECTORANT.
- MM.

442
00:20:06,807 --> 00:20:09,175
WELL, BACK TO READING
THE BRIDGES OF MADISON C--

443
00:20:09,208 --> 00:20:11,845
- WHAT THE-- HEY.
- ♪♪ [CLARINET]

444
00:20:11,878 --> 00:20:15,615
WHERE THE HECK IS THAT CLARINET
COMING FROM?

445
00:20:15,648 --> 00:20:19,318
HEY, WE'RE, UH, RENOVATING
THE CRYPT HERE, AND...

446
00:20:19,352 --> 00:20:21,288
[HAMMERING CONTINUES]

447
00:20:24,123 --> 00:20:26,960
- STEPHEN STILLS!
- [SCREAMS]

448
00:20:26,993 --> 00:20:29,095
THAT'S WHAT HE'S ALWAYS
WANTED TO DO TO DAVID CROSBY.

449
00:20:29,128 --> 00:20:30,663
- [LAUGHING]
- I SEE.

450
00:20:30,697 --> 00:20:31,998
♪♪ [FLUTES]

451
00:20:32,032 --> 00:20:34,000
IT'S THE DELIGHTFULLY
WHIMSICAL MURDER.

452
00:20:34,033 --> 00:20:35,668
- [LAUGHS]
- INSIDE THE VAULT,

453
00:20:35,702 --> 00:20:37,170
A BODY WAITS.

454
00:20:37,203 --> 00:20:39,372
[SINGSONG VOICE]
I'M WAITING!

455
00:20:42,142 --> 00:20:45,045
- HE'S GOT A COCONUT HEAD ON.
- [LAUGHS]

456
00:20:45,078 --> 00:20:46,513
♪♪ [FLUTES CONTINUE]

457
00:20:46,547 --> 00:20:48,282
GALWAY, RAMPAL.

458
00:20:48,315 --> 00:20:50,283
THEY'RE FLUTE POLICE.

459
00:20:50,317 --> 00:20:53,587
GALWAY, YOU STARTED THE TRILL
IN THE UPPER NOTE!

460
00:20:54,955 --> 00:20:58,492
SOMEONE GET A DOCTOR!
WHA-- WAIT. I AM A DOCTOR.

461
00:20:58,525 --> 00:21:00,493
DOES IT HURT WHEN I DO THIS?

462
00:21:00,527 --> 00:21:03,397
THIS IS ONE OF
THE DOCTOR'S MISTAKES--
A MONSTROSITY.

463
00:21:03,430 --> 00:21:06,333
AN ANIMAL'S BRAIN
GRAFTED TO A HUMAN BODY.

464
00:21:06,367 --> 00:21:08,502
- IN RETROSPECT,
AN OBVIOUS MISTAKE.
- LEAVING THE DEAD WATCHMAN,

465
00:21:08,535 --> 00:21:11,438
THE MONSTROSITY CARRIED
THE GIRL'S BODY
OUT OF THE VAULT.

466
00:21:11,472 --> 00:21:13,507
IT FEARS AND OBEYS ONE MASTER:

467
00:21:13,540 --> 00:21:15,508
- TONY ORLANDO.
- ...DR. FRANK.

468
00:21:15,542 --> 00:21:17,510
ENSTEIN.

469
00:21:17,543 --> 00:21:19,445
WE GOTTA GET SOME LIGHT
IN HERE, BOSS.

470
00:21:19,478 --> 00:21:21,882
SOMEONE COULD GET HURT.

471
00:21:21,915 --> 00:21:24,050
- THEY SEEM REAL ORGANIZED.
- YEAH.

472
00:21:27,153 --> 00:21:28,822
TAXI!

473
00:21:30,590 --> 00:21:32,825
BOSS, WAS I REALLY A MISTAKE
LIKE THE MAN SAID?

474
00:21:32,858 --> 00:21:35,195
- OH, NO, YOU WERE
A LITTLE MIRACLE.
- OKAY.

475
00:21:35,228 --> 00:21:38,465
AND SO THE LITTLE FELLOW
CARTED THE CORPSE AWAY.

476
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:43,403
THAT'S RATHER A CASUAL LOOK
FOR A GRAVE ROBBER.

477
00:21:43,437 --> 00:21:46,407
- NICE.
- HE PROBABLY HAS ESPADRILLES ON
OR A NICE LOAFER.

478
00:21:46,440 --> 00:21:48,042
YEAH.

479
00:21:51,678 --> 00:21:54,247
[TOM SERVO]
WEEKEND AT BERNIE'S:
THE ARMAGEDDON.

480
00:21:54,280 --> 00:21:57,983
ARE THOSE MY GOOD SHEETS?
THOSE ARE MY
300-PER-COUNT PERCALES.

481
00:22:02,055 --> 00:22:04,357
NOW IT'S MISSISSIPPI BURNING.

482
00:22:06,025 --> 00:22:08,495
[SIGHS]
I MISS THE VOICE-OVER GUY.

483
00:22:09,562 --> 00:22:11,363
WELL, WHAT ARE YOU HUNGRY FOR?

484
00:22:11,397 --> 00:22:14,567
ANYPLACE
THAT'S GOT CURLY FRIES.

485
00:22:14,600 --> 00:22:17,570
WELL, IT'S A QUIET NIGHT
HERE ON LAKE WOEBEGONE.

486
00:22:17,603 --> 00:22:19,272
[WHISTLING]

487
00:22:22,442 --> 00:22:25,212
THEY'RE ARRIVING
AT JIM DINE'S HOUSE.

488
00:22:26,847 --> 00:22:28,982
- OHH!
- SPECIAL DUAL-ACTION GLOVE BOX.

489
00:22:29,015 --> 00:22:31,183
YEAH.

490
00:22:31,217 --> 00:22:34,187
NO. I'M SORRY. I'M SORRY.
WE DON'T BUY THIS.

491
00:22:36,623 --> 00:22:38,592
♪♪ [HUMMING ADDAMS FAMILY THEME]

492
00:22:38,625 --> 00:22:41,728
COMING THIS CHRISTMAS.

493
00:22:41,762 --> 00:22:45,365
- SELZNICK INTERNATIONAL
PICTURES.
- [CHUCKLING]

494
00:22:45,398 --> 00:22:47,600
OH, THEY'RE SNEAKING MARILYN
INTO THE WHITE HOUSE.

495
00:22:47,633 --> 00:22:49,837
- OHH!
- SHH!

496
00:22:49,870 --> 00:22:51,872
THAT CAR'S GOT BAD RINGS
OR SOMETHING.

497
00:22:51,905 --> 00:22:53,440
BAD PICKUP.
I DON'T KNOW.

498
00:22:53,473 --> 00:22:55,342
[IMITATING ENGINE SPUTTERING]

499
00:22:58,145 --> 00:23:00,380
AH, CRIPES, THE WARDEN'S UP.

500
00:23:00,413 --> 00:23:03,617
MUST BE WATCHING CHEVY CHASE
OR SOMETHING.

501
00:23:03,650 --> 00:23:06,252
WELL, I'VE HAD
A REALLY NICE TIME TONIGHT.

502
00:23:06,285 --> 00:23:07,820
I HOPE WE CAN DO IT
AGAIN SOMETIME.

503
00:23:07,853 --> 00:23:11,057
- [GROWLING]
- WOLFIE, HONEY...

504
00:23:11,090 --> 00:23:13,058
HERE BENEATH THE OLD MANSION,

505
00:23:13,092 --> 00:23:15,062
THE DOCTOR CAREFULLY PREPARED
FOR ANOTHER TRANSPLANT.

506
00:23:15,095 --> 00:23:17,863
- A POT ROAST!
- THIS BODY HAD BEEN IN
THE VAULT FOR ONLY A FEW HOURS.

507
00:23:17,897 --> 00:23:19,867
CHANCES SEEMED BETTER
THIS TIME.

508
00:23:19,900 --> 00:23:21,802
STILL, DR. FRANK WAS DOUBTFUL.

509
00:23:21,835 --> 00:23:24,703
TISSUE IN DEAD BODIES
DETERIORATES RAPIDLY.

510
00:23:24,737 --> 00:23:27,307
WHERE WERE THE LIVE,
FRESH BODIES
HE'D BEEN PROMISED?

511
00:23:27,340 --> 00:23:30,043
WHY, STRAIGHT FROM
YOUR GROCER'S FREEZER.

512
00:23:30,077 --> 00:23:31,712
HE BITTERLY RESENTS
THAT EVERY STEP FORWARD

513
00:23:31,745 --> 00:23:33,747
DEPENDS ON THE WHIM
OF A MISER, THE OLD WOMAN,

514
00:23:33,780 --> 00:23:35,915
BROODING UPSTAIRS
IN HER BEDROOM.

515
00:23:35,948 --> 00:23:37,250
- [IMITATING GUZZLING]
- CHUG IT!

516
00:23:37,283 --> 00:23:39,085
FINISH IT!
ALL THE WAY!

517
00:23:39,118 --> 00:23:41,120
AND HETTY MARCH WONDERS.

518
00:23:41,153 --> 00:23:44,490
HAS SHE BEEN A FOOL,
SQUANDERING MONEY
ON THIS STRANGE EXPERIMENT?

519
00:23:44,523 --> 00:23:47,160
- [MOCK COUGHING]
- MONEY HOARDED THROUGH A LONG,
GREEDY LIFETIME.

520
00:23:47,193 --> 00:23:51,397
EACH DAY, MORE MONEY.
EACH DAY, DEATH GETTING CLOSER.

521
00:23:51,430 --> 00:23:54,567
- AH, BUT TO START LIFE AGAIN
IN A BRAND-NEW BODY.
- [COUGHS] NEED A LEMON.

522
00:23:54,600 --> 00:23:56,335
- BEAUTIFUL AND YOUNG.
- KITTY.

523
00:23:56,368 --> 00:23:58,003
NO PRICE CAN BE
TOO HIGH FOR THAT.

524
00:23:58,037 --> 00:24:00,007
- I'M DRUNK TOO. MEOW.
- CAN SHE REALLY
TRUST THE DOCTOR?

525
00:24:00,040 --> 00:24:02,375
CAN SHE REALLY TRUST ANYONE?
HASN'T EVERYONE TRIED
TO CHEAT HER?

526
00:24:02,408 --> 00:24:04,077
I CAN'T EVEN TRUST
THOSE BLINDS.

527
00:24:04,110 --> 00:24:06,378
WANTING HER MONEY
WHILE THEY SMILED
AT HER UGLINESS.

528
00:24:06,412 --> 00:24:08,215
BUT THEY NEVER GOT A PENNY.

529
00:24:08,248 --> 00:24:10,083
OH, HOW SHE MADE THEM SWEAT.

530
00:24:10,117 --> 00:24:12,752
- IN THOSE SATIN, TIGHT PANTS.
- ESPECIALLY THIS OLD FOOL,

531
00:24:12,785 --> 00:24:14,855
COMPANION AND GIGOLO.

532
00:24:14,888 --> 00:24:18,057
HOW MANY YEARS SHE'S KEPT HIM
DANGLING ON PROMISES.

533
00:24:18,090 --> 00:24:20,627
WELL, SOMETIMES IT'S CONVENIENT
TO HAVE A MAN,

534
00:24:20,660 --> 00:24:22,695
ESPECIALLY WHEN HE COMES
CHEAPER THAN SERVANTS.

535
00:24:22,728 --> 00:24:24,597
[MIKE]
THE STRANGE LOVES
OF MARTHA WASHINGTON.

536
00:24:24,630 --> 00:24:26,533
THE AUSTRIAN GIRL?

537
00:24:26,567 --> 00:24:29,068
"NINA RHODES, 18, NO FAMILY,

538
00:24:29,102 --> 00:24:31,070
PLEASING PERSONALITY."

539
00:24:31,103 --> 00:24:33,072
WHATEVER THAT MIGHT MEAN.

540
00:24:33,105 --> 00:24:36,408
HMPH! THICK ANKLES,
PIMPLY FACE,

541
00:24:36,442 --> 00:24:39,545
BUT SHE ALWAYS SMILES
WHEN SHE'S SPOKEN TO.

542
00:24:39,578 --> 00:24:41,882
- WOW.
- WELL, APPLICATION FORMS
FOR A SERVANT GIRL

543
00:24:41,915 --> 00:24:44,417
DON'T USUALLY INCLUDE BUST,
WAIST, AND HIP MEASUREMENTS.

544
00:24:44,450 --> 00:24:46,385
- EXCEPT AT HOOTERS.
- OOH.

545
00:24:46,418 --> 00:24:49,688
[MAN]
ALL THREE WILL BE HERE TOMORROW,
AND THEN YOU CAN CHOOSE.

546
00:24:49,722 --> 00:24:51,558
[MAN ON RADIO]
AT GREEN HAVEN CEMETERY,

547
00:24:51,592 --> 00:24:54,460
THE BODY SNATCHERS
BRUTALLY MURDERED
NIGHT WATCHMAN ROBERT HANES,

548
00:24:54,493 --> 00:24:57,597
- HEY. SHH. THIS IS US.
- ...62, WHO EVIDENTLY
INTERRUPTED HIS KILLERS

549
00:24:57,630 --> 00:24:59,165
DURING THEIR GHOULISH TASK.

550
00:24:59,198 --> 00:25:00,933
HIS NECK WAS BROKEN.
THE IMPRINT

551
00:25:00,967 --> 00:25:03,303
OF A HUGE PAIR OF HANDS
WAS FOUND ON HIS THROAT.

552
00:25:03,337 --> 00:25:06,538
- IT'S THE OPINION
OF THE POLICE--
- GOD, I HATE MICHAEL FELDMAN.

553
00:25:06,572 --> 00:25:08,742
- WHAT DO YA KNOW? I KNOW THIS.
- RING FOR DR. FRANK.

554
00:25:08,775 --> 00:25:10,777
[BUZZES]

555
00:25:10,810 --> 00:25:12,445
SO THAT'S WHAT HE WAS DOING.

556
00:25:23,623 --> 00:25:25,592
SO, THEN, WITH JUST
THIS LITTLE WEATHER KIT,

557
00:25:25,625 --> 00:25:27,527
YOU'VE TRANSFORMED
YOURSELF INTO--

558
00:25:27,560 --> 00:25:29,662
- WHAT WAS IT AGAIN?
- WEATHER SERVO 9,

559
00:25:29,695 --> 00:25:32,765
FIRST TO BRING
THE SATELLITE OF LOVE
VITAL WEATHER INFORMATION

560
00:25:32,798 --> 00:25:34,867
THAT AFFECTS YOU!
♪♪ [HUMMING]

561
00:25:34,900 --> 00:25:37,503
WELL, I APPRECIATE THAT,
BUT THERE'S VERY LITTLE
WEATHER IN SPACE.

562
00:25:37,537 --> 00:25:39,805
AND BESIDES, WE HAVE INSTRUMENTS
THAT HANDLE ALL THAT.

563
00:25:39,838 --> 00:25:41,875
SERVO, YOU'RE GONNA
DIE IN SPACE.

564
00:25:41,908 --> 00:25:43,877
- CROW! HE MIGHT NOT.
- HEY.

565
00:25:43,910 --> 00:25:47,213
THAT'S RIGHT, CROW.
NOW RAISE WEATHER SERVO 9
INTO SPACE,

566
00:25:47,247 --> 00:25:50,117
AND I'LL REPORT THE WEATHER
AS IT HAPPENS TO YOU!

567
00:25:50,150 --> 00:25:51,483
- ♪♪ [HUMMING]
- NOTHING HAPPENS TO US.

568
00:25:51,517 --> 00:25:52,985
WE'RE PROTECTED BY A SATELLITE.

569
00:25:53,018 --> 00:25:55,222
I KNOW. JUST SEND
THE POOR DOPE OUT TO SPACE.

570
00:25:55,255 --> 00:25:56,890
DON'T DIE!

571
00:25:56,923 --> 00:25:58,892
UP-TO-THE-MINUTE FORECAST
FROM WEATHER SERVO--

572
00:25:58,925 --> 00:26:02,628
- [HATCH CLOSES]
- [TOM SERVO OVER RADIO]
BOY, IT'S COLD OUT HERE.

573
00:26:02,662 --> 00:26:04,697
IS IT SUPPOSED TO BE THIS COLD?

574
00:26:04,730 --> 00:26:07,700
AW, DON'T BE AFRAID.
[MOCKINGLY]
YOU'RE WEATHER SERVO 9.

575
00:26:07,733 --> 00:26:10,670
SERVO, JUST MAKE YOUR REPORT
AND THEN GET BACK IN HERE, OKAY?

576
00:26:10,703 --> 00:26:12,905
WELL, BEFORE I
GET ON WITH THE WEATHER,

577
00:26:12,938 --> 00:26:14,740
I'VE GOT A COUPLE OF BIRTHDAYS
TO ANNOUNCE.

578
00:26:14,773 --> 00:26:17,110
- [LAUGHS] I'M JUST KIDDING,
OF COURSE.
- OH, BOY.

579
00:26:17,143 --> 00:26:19,445
- MAN, IS IT COLD OUT HERE!
- HE'S DEAD MEAT.

580
00:26:19,478 --> 00:26:22,348
- YEP.
- I GUESS THE BIG NEWS
IS THE COLD WEATHER.

581
00:26:22,382 --> 00:26:25,352
YOU MIGHT WANNA TAKE A JACKET.
[LAUGHS]

582
00:26:25,385 --> 00:26:27,187
IT'S COLD.

583
00:26:27,220 --> 00:26:28,688
OH, WHAT'S THIS?

584
00:26:28,722 --> 00:26:30,857
LOOKS LIKE A METEOR SHOWER'S
GONNA BE COMING BY.

585
00:26:30,890 --> 00:26:33,427
IT MIGHT WARM THINGS UP A BIT.
[LAUGHS]

586
00:26:33,460 --> 00:26:36,730
[GASPING]
IT'LL PROBABLY PASS
JUST TO THE NORTH OF US,

587
00:26:36,763 --> 00:26:39,665
BUT YOU MIGHT WANNA...
[SCREAMING]

588
00:26:39,698 --> 00:26:42,268
SERVO!
LOOKS LIKE IT'S NOT WORKING.

589
00:26:42,302 --> 00:26:44,303
CAMBOT, YOU BETTER SHOW ME
ROCKET NUMBER 9.

590
00:26:44,337 --> 00:26:47,340
[SCREAMING CONTINUES]

591
00:26:47,373 --> 00:26:49,008
[MUTTERING]

592
00:26:49,042 --> 00:26:50,510
WELL, THAT'LL HAPPEN.

593
00:26:50,543 --> 00:26:52,278
SERVO, ARE YOU ALL RIGHT?

594
00:26:52,312 --> 00:26:54,080
SERVO, BUDDY,
SPEAK TO ME.

595
00:26:54,113 --> 00:26:55,248
WELL,
[COUGHS]

596
00:26:55,282 --> 00:26:57,150
I'M NOT COLD ANYMORE.

597
00:26:57,183 --> 00:26:58,985
I BETTER START FIXING YOU UP.

598
00:26:59,018 --> 00:27:00,753
- WOW. YOU LOOK SO COOL, SERVO.
- [SIZZLES]

599
00:27:00,787 --> 00:27:03,490
- HEY, MIKE, CAN I DO THAT?
- NO, YOU CANNOT DO THAT.

600
00:27:03,523 --> 00:27:06,292
- WE'LL BE RIGHT BACK.
- WEATHER [COUGHS] STATION...

601
00:27:06,325 --> 00:27:08,795
HELP.
[LAUGHS]
HEAD HAPPENS TO BE ON FIRE.

602
00:27:08,828 --> 00:27:10,463
MIGHT WANNA...
[LAUGHS]

603
00:27:10,497 --> 00:27:12,498
♪♪ [HUMMING]

604
00:27:16,368 --> 00:27:17,770
[EQUIPMENT WHIRRING]

605
00:27:17,803 --> 00:27:19,272
- HMM.
- ♪♪ [HUMMING]

606
00:27:19,305 --> 00:27:21,540
HOPE YOU'RE OKAY.
[CLEARS THROAT]

607
00:27:21,573 --> 00:27:23,443
THIS JUST IN...

608
00:27:25,212 --> 00:27:26,913
HAH! IT'S JERZY KOSINSKI.

609
00:27:26,947 --> 00:27:28,415
[CHUCKLING]

610
00:27:31,752 --> 00:27:34,653
[MUTTERING]

611
00:27:35,722 --> 00:27:39,125
ROMPER, STOMPER, BOMPER BOO.

612
00:27:39,158 --> 00:27:42,462
WELL, MIKE, YOU KNOW,
PUBLIC ACCESS TV
JUST IS NOT VERY GOOD.

613
00:27:42,495 --> 00:27:44,963
MM-MM. MM-MM.

614
00:27:44,997 --> 00:27:46,332
MMM.

615
00:27:48,668 --> 00:27:49,968
WHOA.

616
00:27:52,272 --> 00:27:54,740
HEY, THERE'S A NAKED LADY
IN THIS MOVIE,

617
00:27:54,773 --> 00:27:57,310
AND SHE'S NUDE
WITH NO CLOTHES ON.

618
00:27:57,343 --> 00:27:58,645
[WHIRRING CONTINUES]

619
00:27:58,678 --> 00:28:01,380
SOUNDS LIKE THE PRINTER'S STUCK.

620
00:28:01,413 --> 00:28:04,317
OH, DARN!
I NEED ANOTHER QUARTER.

621
00:28:06,318 --> 00:28:10,423
OH, WHENEVER I PUT THIS SUIT ON,
I GOTTA TINKLE.

622
00:28:10,457 --> 00:28:14,393
OH, I GOTTA START
THOSE NEW POTATOES.

623
00:28:14,427 --> 00:28:16,797
ANN-MARGROCK.

624
00:28:16,830 --> 00:28:19,532
YOU KNOW,
JAME GUMB ONLY DREAMED

625
00:28:19,565 --> 00:28:22,968
OF ACHIEVING
WHAT THIS GUY HAS.

626
00:28:23,002 --> 00:28:25,070
OH, WHO DIED IN HERE?

627
00:28:25,103 --> 00:28:27,040
[TOM SERVO]
POINT OF LAW.

628
00:28:28,608 --> 00:28:30,577
MISS MARPLE ARRIVES.

629
00:28:30,610 --> 00:28:33,513
[CROW]
MURDER, MOST GOOFY.

630
00:28:33,547 --> 00:28:36,282
HE'S GOT ANOTHER NUDEY
ON THE SLAB.

631
00:28:36,315 --> 00:28:39,752
MORE OF THIS HOCUS-POCUS, HETTY?

632
00:28:39,785 --> 00:28:42,288
THE DOCTOR TRANSPLANTED
THE BRAIN

633
00:28:42,322 --> 00:28:44,990
FROM A LIVE DOG
TO A DEAD HUMAN BODY.

634
00:28:45,023 --> 00:28:49,595
- CAN YOU STAND IT?
- YOU SAW THE CREATURE WALK OUT
OF THAT CYLINDER ALIVE.

635
00:28:49,628 --> 00:28:52,432
- HOW MANY FAILURES SINCE THEN?
- OH.

636
00:28:52,465 --> 00:28:54,633
WELL, IT'S YOUR MONEY.

637
00:28:56,735 --> 00:28:59,638
OH, HI.
DIDN'T HEAR THE BELL.

638
00:28:59,672 --> 00:29:01,573
OKAY, CAN WE GET A LEVEL,
PLEASE?

639
00:29:01,607 --> 00:29:04,443
- THIS SPECIMEN IS EXCELLENT.
- AND THE POLICE ARE LOOKING
FOR THE BODY SNATCHERS.

640
00:29:04,477 --> 00:29:06,880
- MA, DON'T HIT, PLEASE.
- WHY THE LOCAL CEMETERY,
DOCTOR?

641
00:29:06,913 --> 00:29:10,015
ARE YOU TRYING
TO BLAZE A TRAIL TO OUR DOOR?

642
00:29:10,048 --> 00:29:12,652
THE FINAL TEST WAS ESSENTIAL
FOR YOUR PROTECTION.

643
00:29:12,685 --> 00:29:14,620
AS FOR THE POLICE,
IF THEY COME HERE,

644
00:29:14,653 --> 00:29:17,423
I HIT THIS SWITCH,
AND A NUCLEAR REACTION
IS SET OFF.

645
00:29:17,457 --> 00:29:20,393
- OH, WELL, THAT MA-- WHAT?
- CLOSE THE CIRCUIT BREAKER,

646
00:29:20,427 --> 00:29:22,328
AND IN A MATTER OF MINUTES,

647
00:29:22,362 --> 00:29:24,597
THIS HOUSE AND ANY EVIDENCE
IT MIGHT CONTAIN

648
00:29:24,630 --> 00:29:26,532
BECOMES A RADIOACTIVE HOLE
IN THE GROUND.

649
00:29:26,565 --> 00:29:30,370
- BE CAREFUL.
- IS THERE A WAY WE COULD LIVE
AND STILL EVADE THE POLICE?

650
00:29:30,403 --> 00:29:32,705
WELL, NOTHING MUST GO WRONG.

651
00:29:32,738 --> 00:29:34,907
JEEZ, SHE'S THE BATTLE-AX
POTEMKIN.

652
00:29:34,940 --> 00:29:37,243
YEAH.

653
00:29:37,277 --> 00:29:39,912
THERE'S NO SIGN OF LIFE.

654
00:29:39,945 --> 00:29:41,948
- YEAH? LOOK WHO'S TALKING.
- WATCH.

655
00:29:47,353 --> 00:29:49,022
WHAT?

656
00:29:49,055 --> 00:29:52,892
I CAN'T WAIT TILL I'M HER.

657
00:29:52,925 --> 00:29:56,462
NOW, DON'T LOOK AT HER
CHESTOCOLOGICAL REGION.

658
00:29:56,495 --> 00:29:58,263
DID I GET
REALLY DEAD LAST NIGHT?

659
00:30:01,902 --> 00:30:04,837
SHE'S SORT OF ALIVE!

660
00:30:04,870 --> 00:30:08,007
OH, JUST RADIATE
THE WHOLE ROOM, PLEASE.

661
00:30:13,278 --> 00:30:15,315
THE JOSHUA LIGHT SHOW.

662
00:30:17,183 --> 00:30:20,587
- SHE LACKS BUT ONE THING.
- BIG, HUNKY ME.

663
00:30:20,620 --> 00:30:22,655
- A BRAIN.
- MAN, HE'S PICKY.

664
00:30:22,688 --> 00:30:25,858
HANS WAS STILL LIVING
WHEN HE WAS DRAGGED
FROM THAT WRECKED CAR.

665
00:30:25,892 --> 00:30:28,027
THAT'S WHY WE SUCCEEDED
WITH THE TRANSPLANT.

666
00:30:28,060 --> 00:30:30,028
LET'S SEE.
WHAT ELSE CAN I DO AROUND HERE?

667
00:30:30,062 --> 00:30:33,432
- SHE SEEMS ALIVE.
- SHE IS, TO A LIMITED EXTENT.

668
00:30:33,465 --> 00:30:35,435
SHE'LL BE ABLE TO MOVE AROUND,

669
00:30:35,468 --> 00:30:39,105
BUT THE BRAIN DETERIORATION
IS TOO EXTENSIVE
FOR THOUGHT PROCESSES.

670
00:30:41,540 --> 00:30:43,910
HEY. HEY, DON'T TEASE
THE CORPSE.

671
00:30:43,943 --> 00:30:45,478
[TAPPING CONTINUES]

672
00:30:45,512 --> 00:30:47,947
I AM TRYING TO SLEEP.

673
00:30:51,917 --> 00:30:54,887
♪ FLEW IN FROM
MIAMI BEACH B.O.A.C. ♪

674
00:30:54,920 --> 00:30:56,888
♪ COULDN'T GET TO BED
LAST NIGHT ♪

675
00:30:56,922 --> 00:30:59,192
- ♪♪ [HUMMING]
- THE BOEING 707,

676
00:30:59,225 --> 00:31:02,295
THE PACK MULE
OF THE AMERICAN SKIES.

677
00:31:03,697 --> 00:31:06,098
SHEEP-LIKE PASSENGERS
TOO STUPID TO APPRECIATE

678
00:31:06,132 --> 00:31:09,268
TECHNOLOGIES INHERITED
FROM LONG-RANGE BOMBERS.

679
00:31:09,302 --> 00:31:12,538
BYE, GRANDMA.
HOPE YOU ENJOY THE SEX CHANGE.

680
00:31:12,572 --> 00:31:15,442
- SCANDINAVIAN AIRLINES.
- I SEE.

681
00:31:15,475 --> 00:31:17,877
♪♪ [IMITATING SOUNDTRACK MUSIC]

682
00:31:17,910 --> 00:31:20,447
WILMA!

683
00:31:20,480 --> 00:31:22,982
ATOMIC BUTT.
[CHUCKLES]

684
00:31:25,250 --> 00:31:28,220
♪♪ [UPBEAT]

685
00:31:28,253 --> 00:31:31,390
MRS. WIGGINS!

686
00:31:31,423 --> 00:31:34,393
♪♪ [ALL IMITATING
SOUNDTRACK MUSIC]

687
00:31:36,228 --> 00:31:38,230
OOH, THIS THING NEEDS A REST.

688
00:31:40,533 --> 00:31:42,502
[FOREIGN ACCENT]
SAY, PARDON ME,

689
00:31:42,535 --> 00:31:44,670
BUT HOW FAR IS HOLLYWOOD
FROM HERE?

690
00:31:44,703 --> 00:31:47,907
AND COULD YOU TELL ME WHERE
MY ACCENT IS FROM?

691
00:31:50,343 --> 00:31:52,512
COME ON, COME ON!

692
00:31:53,612 --> 00:31:55,582
ALL RIGHT. LET'S SEE.

693
00:31:55,615 --> 00:31:58,283
OOH-HOO!
THE SCHLOSSEN CUTOFF!

694
00:31:58,317 --> 00:32:00,052
- OOH-HOO-HOO!
- IT'S ABOUT TEN MILES.

695
00:32:00,085 --> 00:32:01,887
WHICH WAY?

696
00:32:01,920 --> 00:32:03,657
THAT WAY.

697
00:32:03,690 --> 00:32:05,257
HMM? OH.

698
00:32:05,290 --> 00:32:07,193
[WOMAN]
ARE YOU GOING TO HOLLYWOOD?

699
00:32:07,227 --> 00:32:11,297
NO SUCH LUCK.
I'M WHAT'S KNOWN
AS A FOREIGN DOMESTIC.

700
00:32:11,330 --> 00:32:15,300
FOR THE NEXT 12 MONTHS,
I'LL BE SCRUBBING FLOORS
AND MAKING BEDS.

701
00:32:15,333 --> 00:32:18,170
BUT WHEN MY TIME'S UP,
HOLLYWOOD, LOOK OUT.

702
00:32:18,203 --> 00:32:20,540
- ALL RIGHT. WE'RE WARNED.
- THAT'S STRANGE.

703
00:32:20,573 --> 00:32:23,710
A FOREIGN DOMESTIC AGENCY
PAID MY PASSAGE TOO.

704
00:32:23,743 --> 00:32:25,778
- I'M FROM VIENNA, AUSTRIA.
- UH-HUH.

705
00:32:25,812 --> 00:32:27,313
- OH, REALLY?
- MM-HMM.

706
00:32:27,347 --> 00:32:29,615
- I'M FROM ENGLAND.
- NO!

707
00:32:29,648 --> 00:32:32,118
- IS THIS YOUR FIRST TRIP?
- WE HAVE AN OFFICIAL BEVY.

708
00:32:32,152 --> 00:32:34,120
YES. I'M AWFUL EXCITED.

709
00:32:34,153 --> 00:32:36,355
- POR FAVOR.
- YEAH! [LAUGHS]

710
00:32:36,388 --> 00:32:38,323
- PLEASE!
- I NO SPEAK INGLéS VERY GOOD.

711
00:32:38,357 --> 00:32:41,560
YOU'RE ALL FROM NEBRASKA.
CUT IT OUT.

712
00:32:41,593 --> 00:32:43,963
"HAND OVER YOUR
WALLET PROMPTLY."

713
00:32:43,997 --> 00:32:45,998
WELL, I BETTER DO IT.

714
00:32:46,032 --> 00:32:48,433
YOUR MISSION, MR. PHELPS,
SHOULD YOU DECIDE TO ACCEPT IT,

715
00:32:48,467 --> 00:32:50,370
IS TO PICK UP
THESE THREE FOREIGN WOMEN

716
00:32:50,403 --> 00:32:52,372
AT THE L.A.
INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT.

717
00:32:52,405 --> 00:32:54,973
- SHOULD YOU OR ANY OF YOUR--
- YEAH, YEAH.
IT GOES ON LIKE THAT.

718
00:32:55,007 --> 00:32:57,077
- WE KNOW.
- SORRY.

719
00:32:58,812 --> 00:33:01,680
ARE YOU GOING TO WORK
FOR MRS. MARCH TOO?

720
00:33:01,713 --> 00:33:05,985
- YES-- I MEAN, Sí.
- THIS SOUNDS LIKE A SISTER ACT.

721
00:33:06,018 --> 00:33:10,088
- HMM? "MRS. BAT GUANO,"
IF IT REALLY IS YOUR NAME.
- YOU TOO?

722
00:33:10,122 --> 00:33:12,358
- NINA RHODES?
- YO!

723
00:33:12,392 --> 00:33:14,393
YES, SIR.

724
00:33:14,427 --> 00:33:17,330
ANITA GON-- GONZALEZ?

725
00:33:17,363 --> 00:33:22,135
- RIGHT AT YA!
- KIRBY PUCKETT!

726
00:33:22,168 --> 00:33:25,070
- BEATRICE MULLINS HERE?
- THAT'S RIGHT.

727
00:33:25,103 --> 00:33:27,073
ARE YOU MR. MARCH?

728
00:33:27,107 --> 00:33:29,775
NO. I WORK FOR MRS. MARCH.

729
00:33:29,808 --> 00:33:33,913
- COME ALONG.
- IT'S ALEXANDER'S RAGTIME BAND.

730
00:33:33,947 --> 00:33:37,783
[NARRATOR]
THREE NEW BODIES--
FRESH, LIVE, YOUNG, BODIES.

731
00:33:37,817 --> 00:33:40,953
- THIS FALL ON NBC.
- NO FAMILIES OR FRIENDS
WITHIN THOUSANDS OF MILES,

732
00:33:40,987 --> 00:33:43,455
NO ONE TO ASK
EMBARRASSING QUESTIONS
WHEN THEY DISAPPEAR.

733
00:33:43,488 --> 00:33:45,525
[MIKE]
THE FACTS OF LIFE
GO TO EUROPE.

734
00:33:45,558 --> 00:33:47,527
NOT THAT I'VE SEEN IT.

735
00:33:47,560 --> 00:33:50,963
THEY'RE OFF TO A MURDER
IN SUNNY CALIFORNIA.

736
00:33:52,565 --> 00:33:55,267
♪ L.A. IS A GREAT BIG FREEWAY ♪

737
00:33:55,300 --> 00:33:57,270
♪♪ [HUMMING ALONG]

738
00:33:57,303 --> 00:33:59,572
[NARRATOR]
VICTOR WONDERED WHICH ONE
MRS. MARCH WOULD PICK--

739
00:33:59,605 --> 00:34:03,108
THE LITTLE MEXICAN,
THE GIRL FROM VIENNA,
OR THE BUXOM BLONDE.

740
00:34:03,142 --> 00:34:07,045
- OR THE...
- VICTOR KNEW HIS PICK,
BUT HE STILL FELT UNEASY.

741
00:34:07,078 --> 00:34:08,782
MAKING LOVE
TO AN 80-YEAR-OLD WOMAN

742
00:34:08,815 --> 00:34:11,617
IN THE BODY
OF A 20-YEAR-OLD GIRL
IS INSANITY.

743
00:34:11,650 --> 00:34:14,053
- OH, THEY DO IT
EVERY DAY IN L.A.
- STILL, HETTY'S PLAN

744
00:34:14,087 --> 00:34:16,888
TO TRANSFER HER FORTUNE
TO THE NEW BODY
HAD BEEN BRILLIANT.

745
00:34:16,922 --> 00:34:19,192
UNPLEASANT TO THINK ABOUT
WHAT'S GOING TO HAPPEN
TO THESE GIRLS,

746
00:34:19,225 --> 00:34:21,427
BUT A MAN HAS TO CONSIDER
HIS OWN FUTURE.

747
00:34:21,460 --> 00:34:23,428
- HEY, YOU'RE RATIONALIZING.
- WHAT WOULD HAPPEN TO HIM

748
00:34:23,462 --> 00:34:26,265
IF HETTY WERE TO CAST HIM OFF
AFTER ALL THESE YEARS?

749
00:34:26,298 --> 00:34:27,767
BLANCHE, NO!
[IMITATES TIRES SCREECHING]

750
00:34:27,800 --> 00:34:29,168
[IMITATES THUDDING]

751
00:34:31,503 --> 00:34:35,273
- I AM NOT SHARING A ROOM
WITH BETH, AM I?
- [BEATRICE MUTTERS]

752
00:34:35,307 --> 00:34:37,477
WELL, THERE'S YOUR NEW HOME,
GIRLS.

753
00:34:37,510 --> 00:34:39,245
THE PYGMALION SISTERS.

754
00:34:39,278 --> 00:34:42,448
[BEATRICE SIGHS]
GIVES ME THE SHIVERS.

755
00:34:42,482 --> 00:34:44,450
- AREN'T THERE ANY NEIGHBORS?
- NO.

756
00:34:44,483 --> 00:34:46,785
WHEN YOU GET CLOSE TO AN ACCENT,
LET US KNOW.

757
00:34:46,818 --> 00:34:48,620
ARE THERE ANY OTHER SERVANTS?

758
00:34:48,653 --> 00:34:52,358
NO, BUT I DON'T THINK
YOU'RE GOING TO FIND IT BORING.

759
00:34:52,392 --> 00:34:55,193
THAT'S THREE DOWN
AND SEVEN TO GO.
BENNETT CERF.

760
00:34:57,230 --> 00:35:00,533
[GASPS]
TRUMPY, YOU CAN DO MAGIC!

761
00:35:00,567 --> 00:35:02,835
♪♪ [HUMMING]

762
00:35:12,845 --> 00:35:16,148
♪ AND THERE'S A ROSE
IN A FISTED GLOVE ♪

763
00:35:23,622 --> 00:35:25,525
MM. BOY, A LONG DAY, HUH?

764
00:35:25,558 --> 00:35:27,327
I'M JUST GONNA CLIMB INTO
A NICE HOT BATH.

765
00:35:27,360 --> 00:35:28,493
YEAH.

766
00:35:28,527 --> 00:35:31,430
CLARA PELLER IN REAR WINDOW.

767
00:35:31,463 --> 00:35:35,033
WEIRD WINDOW.

768
00:35:35,067 --> 00:35:39,438
- WHOA-OA-OA-OA!
[IMITATING CRASHING]
- [LAUGHING]

769
00:35:41,140 --> 00:35:44,177
I'LL GET IT!
GOTTA DO EVERYTHING AROUND HERE.

770
00:35:44,210 --> 00:35:46,878
MEOW.

771
00:35:46,912 --> 00:35:48,813
[SNIFFS]

772
00:35:48,847 --> 00:35:50,917
YOU HAVE CATS, DON'T YOU?

773
00:35:50,950 --> 00:35:52,852
WHAT A JOLLY LITTLE PLACE
THIS IS.

774
00:35:52,885 --> 00:35:54,853
[ENGLISH ACCENT]
I SAID "PLACE,"
'CAUSE I'M ENGLISH.

775
00:35:54,887 --> 00:35:58,390
DICK VAN DYKE HAD
A BETTER ENGLISH ACCENT.

776
00:35:58,423 --> 00:36:00,793
OH, HI. HOW YA DOIN'?

777
00:36:00,827 --> 00:36:03,795
- [SCREAMS]
- THAT'S SPANISH FOR "AAHH!"

778
00:36:03,828 --> 00:36:06,165
NOW, HURRY ALONG.

779
00:36:06,198 --> 00:36:08,333
HURRY UP. NOW GO.

780
00:36:08,367 --> 00:36:10,770
IT'S A 20-YEAR
CHARLIE'S ANGELS REUNION.

781
00:36:13,472 --> 00:36:16,508
OH, I SHOULD'VE PLEDGED
LAMBDA CHI OMEGA.

782
00:36:20,378 --> 00:36:24,717
AND THIS IS THE ROOM
WHERE PRESIDENT KENNEDY AND I

783
00:36:24,750 --> 00:36:27,887
HAD THE BALL
FOR THE SPANISH AMBASSADOR.

784
00:36:29,922 --> 00:36:33,358
THE ONE I HAD TO MEET YOU THERE.

785
00:36:33,392 --> 00:36:37,330
OH, THEY'RE GOING TO PAY
THEIR RESPECTS TO THE PRE-DEAD.

786
00:36:37,363 --> 00:36:39,665
♪♪ [IMITATING SOUNDTRACK MUSIC]

787
00:36:41,133 --> 00:36:42,602
[ELDERLY FEMALE VOICE]
NORMAN!

788
00:36:42,635 --> 00:36:45,137
- OH.
- I KNOW YOU'RE LOOKING
AT MY JEWELRY.

789
00:36:45,170 --> 00:36:47,072
PUT DOWN YOUR LUGGAGE.

790
00:36:47,105 --> 00:36:49,742
TONIGHT ON A VERY SPECIAL
GRANDMA IRONSIDE...

791
00:36:51,443 --> 00:36:52,812
[IMITATING WHEELS SQUEAKING]

792
00:36:52,845 --> 00:36:55,648
OKAY, WHO'S BUNKING WITH ME?

793
00:36:59,152 --> 00:37:01,653
UH, YOU WANNA SEE
MY RESUMé MAYBE?

794
00:37:01,687 --> 00:37:03,422
WHAT ARE YOU, MRS. PENGUIN?

795
00:37:03,455 --> 00:37:05,523
GET THAT THING AWAY FROM ME.

796
00:37:08,060 --> 00:37:09,528
TURN AROUND.

797
00:37:09,562 --> 00:37:11,863
- OH, WOW.
- SLOWLY.

798
00:37:11,897 --> 00:37:14,400
GET THE DOCTOR.

799
00:37:14,433 --> 00:37:17,603
- GET THE DOCTOR!
- I COULD BE THE DOCTOR!
I'LL BE THE DOCTOR!

800
00:37:20,138 --> 00:37:21,740
BLIMEY.

801
00:37:23,375 --> 00:37:24,343
[KNOCKING]

802
00:37:24,377 --> 00:37:25,912
HEY.

803
00:37:25,945 --> 00:37:28,413
YEAH, LET'S GIVE SOMEBODY ELSE
A CRACK AT THAT BOWL, HUH?

804
00:37:30,148 --> 00:37:33,852
OH, RIGHT IN THE MIDDLE
OF SPLICING RECOMBINANT DNA!

805
00:37:33,885 --> 00:37:35,353
I'M NEVER GONNA...

806
00:37:35,387 --> 00:37:37,323
♪♪ [WHISTLING]

807
00:37:37,357 --> 00:37:39,958
HUH. MESSY.

808
00:37:39,992 --> 00:37:42,562
WELL, I WOULDN'T LIVE HERE.
WELL...

809
00:37:42,595 --> 00:37:44,630
HEY, HE'S GOT ONE OF THOSE.
HUH.

810
00:37:46,098 --> 00:37:48,333
AS WITH THE OTHER BODIES
STOLEN FROM CEMETERIES,

811
00:37:48,367 --> 00:37:51,803
THE NERVE ENDINGS OF THE BRAIN
WERE TOO FAR GONE
TO RECEIVE A PROPER TRANSPLANT.

812
00:37:51,837 --> 00:37:54,173
- WELL, LIVE AND LEARN.
- THE EXPERIMENT FAILED
TO PRODUCE ANYTHING MORE

813
00:37:54,207 --> 00:37:56,842
THAN A WALKING, BREATHING,
ZOMBIE-LIKE CREATURE.

814
00:37:56,875 --> 00:37:59,645
- HEY.
- BUT THE DOCTOR PERMITTED HER
TO WANDER ABOUT THE LABORATORY.

815
00:37:59,678 --> 00:38:02,682
- SHE WAS QUITE HARMLESS
AND, AT TIMES--
- NUDE.

816
00:38:02,715 --> 00:38:04,583
- ...EVEN AMUSING.
- WOW.

817
00:38:04,617 --> 00:38:07,453
[DR. FRANK]
CHARMING, ISN'T SHE?

818
00:38:07,487 --> 00:38:09,822
- DID YOU WANT SOMETHING?
- [MIKE] UM, HER.

819
00:38:09,855 --> 00:38:12,057
[VICTOR]
UH, MRS. MARCH
IS WAITING FOR YOU.

820
00:38:12,090 --> 00:38:15,127
- THREE GIRLS HAVE ARRIVED.
- AND I'LL STAY HERE
AND SUPERVISE THE ZOMBIE.

821
00:38:15,160 --> 00:38:17,228
[VICTOR]
SHE DOESN'T HAVE A BRAIN?

822
00:38:17,262 --> 00:38:18,863
SHE'D MAKE A GOOD NEWS ANCHOR.

823
00:38:18,897 --> 00:38:20,365
[VICTOR]
MIGHT BE ADVANTAGES.

824
00:38:20,398 --> 00:38:22,535
OH, THANK YOU, ORRIN HATCH.

825
00:38:23,602 --> 00:38:25,738
THE OLD BAT SMELLS LIKE--
OH, HI!

826
00:38:25,772 --> 00:38:27,172
[CHUCKLES]

827
00:38:28,573 --> 00:38:31,043
I WANT THEM EXAMINED
IMMEDIATELY.

828
00:38:31,077 --> 00:38:33,445
VERY WELL. THIS WAY.

829
00:38:33,478 --> 00:38:35,715
WOULD YOU GO OVER
OUR JOB DESCRIPTION AGAIN?

830
00:38:35,748 --> 00:38:38,017
I'M FOGGY ON THAT.

831
00:38:38,050 --> 00:38:40,887
- COME HERE. I FEEL FRISKY.
- LOOK HERE.
THE DOCTOR CAN CONDUCT

832
00:38:40,920 --> 00:38:42,855
THE EXAMINATION PERFECTLY.

833
00:38:42,888 --> 00:38:44,523
[CHUCKLING]

834
00:38:44,557 --> 00:38:47,192
WHAT AN OLD SPOILSPORT I AM.

835
00:38:47,225 --> 00:38:49,195
THAT WOMAN DIAPERED
ROSE KENNEDY.

836
00:38:49,228 --> 00:38:51,197
HAVE YOU DISCONNECTED
THE PHONE?

837
00:38:51,230 --> 00:38:53,665
CAN'T I DEPEND ON YOU
FOR ANYTHING?

838
00:38:53,698 --> 00:38:57,570
WON'T IT BE NICE
WHEN THOSE GIRLS
START CALLING POLICE,

839
00:38:57,603 --> 00:39:01,107
EMPLOYMENT AGENCIES,
IMMIGRATION AUTHORITIES,
COUNSELORS?

840
00:39:01,140 --> 00:39:04,110
- THERE WILL BE NO PHONE CALLS.
- WE HAVE A WINNER.

841
00:39:06,012 --> 00:39:08,613
LOOK. LOOKIT HERE.
THERE WAS A ZIT,
BUT I SQUEEZED IT.

842
00:39:08,647 --> 00:39:10,950
- OHH!
- WEST VIRGINIA?

843
00:39:10,983 --> 00:39:13,952
HIDEOUS. SHE'S USELESS.

844
00:39:13,985 --> 00:39:15,888
THERE IS ONE MORE TEST
I SHOULD MAKE.

845
00:39:15,922 --> 00:39:17,957
DO ANYTHING YOU WANT WITH HER.

846
00:39:17,990 --> 00:39:20,292
- THE OTHER TWO?
- PERFECT MEDICAL SPECIMENS.

847
00:39:20,325 --> 00:39:21,660
- WOW.
- [WHISTLES]

848
00:39:21,693 --> 00:39:23,795
ALL RIGHT, ANITA.
GET DRESSED NOW

849
00:39:23,828 --> 00:39:25,730
AND WAIT FOR THE OTHERS.

850
00:39:25,763 --> 00:39:28,433
- Sí.
- [CREATURE HOWLING]

851
00:39:28,467 --> 00:39:29,468
I'M SCARED.

852
00:39:29,502 --> 00:39:34,640
♪ SO WE CHANGE PARTNERS ♪

853
00:39:34,673 --> 00:39:38,410
- IT'S MAGGIE THE CAT AUDITIONS.
- MRS. MARCH, I AM NOW
GIVING YOU NOTICE.

854
00:39:38,443 --> 00:39:41,147
I DO NOT CARE TO WORK
IN THIS HOUSE ANY LONGER.

855
00:39:41,180 --> 00:39:43,848
- I DEMAND THAT--
- YOU HAVE SIGNED AN AGREEMENT.

856
00:39:43,882 --> 00:39:48,020
IF YOU HAVE ANY OBJECTION,
YOU WILL DISCUSS THEM WITH
THE IMMIGRATION AUTHORITIES

857
00:39:48,053 --> 00:39:50,355
AS PROVIDED FOR IN YOUR PAPERS.

858
00:39:50,388 --> 00:39:52,190
- BUT, MRS. MARCH--
- LATER!

859
00:39:52,223 --> 00:39:54,927
WILLARD SCOTT'S GONNA
READ MY NAME ON TV.

860
00:39:54,960 --> 00:39:56,828
STAND UP, MY DEAR.

861
00:39:56,862 --> 00:40:00,198
I'VE GOT THE SAME MEASUREMENTS
AS MARILYN MONROE.

862
00:40:00,232 --> 00:40:01,700
- [CHUCKLING]
- [CHUCKLES]

863
00:40:01,733 --> 00:40:05,470
- SEE? THERE'S THE HICKEY
FROM BOBBY KENNEDY.
- YEAH.

864
00:40:05,503 --> 00:40:07,473
RAOUL WALLENBERG.

865
00:40:07,507 --> 00:40:11,643
- SHE HAD A MAY-DECEMBER ROMANCE
WITH EUBIE BLAKE.
- [CLEARS THROAT]

866
00:40:11,677 --> 00:40:13,312
[LAUGHS]

867
00:40:13,345 --> 00:40:16,015
- THE LUCKY GIRL?
- YES.

868
00:40:16,048 --> 00:40:18,950
ALLOW ME TO BE THE FIRST
TO OFFER CONGRATULATIONS.

869
00:40:18,983 --> 00:40:21,487
YOU'VE BEEN FONDLED
BY MILDRED NATWICK.

870
00:40:21,520 --> 00:40:23,855
- TO BOTH OF YOU.
- [LAUGHS]

871
00:40:23,888 --> 00:40:26,192
I DON'T GET IT.

872
00:40:29,495 --> 00:40:32,330
- FOR ME?
- WALLS AND EVERYTHING?

873
00:40:33,698 --> 00:40:35,935
WOW! YOU SHOULDN'T HAVE.

874
00:40:35,968 --> 00:40:38,137
YOU GOT ME IN MOTEL 6. AW.

875
00:40:38,170 --> 00:40:39,805
- ♪♪ [BOUNCY SOUNDTRACK MUSIC]
- HUH?

876
00:40:39,838 --> 00:40:42,842
- WHAT THE--
- THERE'S A XYLOPHONE BUILT
IN THAT BED.

877
00:40:44,210 --> 00:40:45,610
- OW!
- OOH!

878
00:40:45,643 --> 00:40:48,213
- DOH!
- OOH, NICE RECOVERY.

879
00:40:48,247 --> 00:40:51,750
YOU TWO GET
THE "NOT AS HOT AS HER" SUITE.

880
00:40:51,783 --> 00:40:54,620
COME ON. COME ON.

881
00:40:54,653 --> 00:40:56,588
NOW LISTEN CAREFULLY,
RUNNERS-UP,

882
00:40:56,622 --> 00:40:59,192
IN THE EVENT
THAT THE BLONDE WOMAN
IS UNABLE TO FULFILL HER DUTIES

883
00:40:59,225 --> 00:41:01,293
AS THE OLD WOMAN'S NEW BODY,
THE FIRST RUNNER-UP

884
00:41:01,327 --> 00:41:03,628
WILL BE ASKED TO CONTINUE ON
IN THOSE DUTIES.

885
00:41:03,662 --> 00:41:06,265
NOW UP TO KATHIE LEE.
[CHUCKLES]

886
00:41:08,300 --> 00:41:10,002
YOUR ROOM IS IN THE BASEMENT,
ANITA.

887
00:41:10,035 --> 00:41:13,138
NINA, YOUR ROOM IS UPSTAIRS,
RIGHT ACROSS FROM THE TOP
OF THE STAIRS.

888
00:41:13,172 --> 00:41:16,142
THERE'S A CONTINENTAL BREAKFAST
AT 8:00, AND IF YOU
HEAR SCREAMING, DON'T LISTEN.

889
00:41:16,175 --> 00:41:18,010
GOOD NIGHT.

890
00:41:18,043 --> 00:41:19,978
I'LL HAVE TO SHOW YOU.

891
00:41:22,513 --> 00:41:24,950
HEY, HERVé VILLECHAIZE'S ROOM.

892
00:41:24,983 --> 00:41:26,218
SEE?

893
00:41:26,252 --> 00:41:27,987
- [MUTTERING]
- YEAH. GOT IT.

894
00:41:28,020 --> 00:41:29,788
OH, THIS IS THE DOOR
TO THE OPTICAL TRACK.

895
00:41:29,822 --> 00:41:32,323
[IMITATING SPEAKING UNDERWATER]

896
00:41:34,860 --> 00:41:38,097
- IMPETIGO.
- NO. I THINK
YOU MEAN "VERTIGO."

897
00:41:38,130 --> 00:41:40,432
UH, EXCUSE ME.
THERE'S A DOG BRAIN
IN MY TOILET.

898
00:41:40,465 --> 00:41:42,500
ESCHER.

899
00:41:42,533 --> 00:41:45,570
ARE YOU RUTH UNDERWOOD?

900
00:41:45,603 --> 00:41:48,107
[ANITA]
I THINK IT WILL BE LONESOME
DOWN THERE.

901
00:41:48,140 --> 00:41:50,375
[VICTOR]
NONSENSE. YOU'LL BE ALL RIGHT.
GO ON.

902
00:41:55,982 --> 00:41:58,950
[HOCKS]

903
00:41:58,983 --> 00:42:03,588
IT MIGHT SMELL A LITTLE DAMP,
AND DON'T MIND THE SILVERFISH.

904
00:42:05,757 --> 00:42:08,293
I'M GONNA ORDER
THE BIG-FOOT BASH.

905
00:42:08,327 --> 00:42:11,097
WATSON, I'M STILL HERE.
WATSON, I NEED YOU.

906
00:42:14,433 --> 00:42:16,435
THIS CLOCK DOESN'T WORK.

907
00:42:19,237 --> 00:42:21,173
- TA-DA.
- GRACIAS.

908
00:42:22,642 --> 00:42:25,177
- THERE YOU GO.
- THANK YOU.

909
00:42:25,210 --> 00:42:26,678
♪ JUST A GIGOLO ♪

910
00:42:26,712 --> 00:42:28,580
♪♪ [HUMMING]

911
00:42:30,182 --> 00:42:33,518
BUT YOU'RE NOT USING AT&T.

912
00:42:33,552 --> 00:42:35,553
OH, THE ELECTROMAGNET
HAS BEEN DESTROYED,

913
00:42:35,587 --> 00:42:37,923
RENDERING THE CARBON GRAINS
AND TRANSMITTER USELESS.

914
00:42:37,957 --> 00:42:39,358
POOPY.

915
00:42:40,425 --> 00:42:42,027
MM.

916
00:42:42,060 --> 00:42:44,963
I KNOW.
I'LL WRITE FOR HELP.

917
00:42:44,997 --> 00:42:48,900
I WAS RIGHT.
IT REALLY IS LONELY DOWN HERE.

918
00:42:48,933 --> 00:42:50,768
- [WHIRRING]
- HUH?

919
00:42:52,037 --> 00:42:55,707
THE MICROBREWERY THING
IS REALLY CATCHING ON.

920
00:42:56,975 --> 00:43:00,045
♪ DA-DA-DA-DA ♪
IMPERIAL MARGARINE.

921
00:43:00,078 --> 00:43:01,180
[WHIRRING STOPS]

922
00:43:03,248 --> 00:43:05,483
ALL RIGHT.
AN HOUR OFF FOR RENEGADE,

923
00:43:05,517 --> 00:43:08,020
AND THEN BACK AT IT.

924
00:43:09,755 --> 00:43:11,123
♪ IT'S TIME WE STOPPED ♪

925
00:43:11,157 --> 00:43:12,792
♪ HEY, WHAT'S THAT SOUND ♪

926
00:43:12,825 --> 00:43:14,827
♪ EVERYBODY LOOK
WHAT'S GOIN'-- ♪

927
00:43:14,860 --> 00:43:16,828
TAKE OVER, CHEWIE.

928
00:43:16,862 --> 00:43:19,398
- HUH?
- CHEWIE. CHEWBACCA.

929
00:43:19,432 --> 00:43:21,533
COMPLETELY FORGOT
WHAT I CAME UP HERE FOR.

930
00:43:21,567 --> 00:43:23,835
[CHUCKLING]

931
00:43:23,868 --> 00:43:26,772
[KNOCKING ON DOOR SLOWLY]

932
00:43:26,805 --> 00:43:29,875
[TOM SERVO: DEEP, SLOW VOICE]
HOUSEKEEPING.

933
00:43:29,908 --> 00:43:31,910
- ¿QUIéN ES?
- "BIKINIS"?

934
00:43:31,943 --> 00:43:32,912
HMM?

935
00:43:32,945 --> 00:43:35,280
DID SHE SAY "BIKINIS"?

936
00:43:35,313 --> 00:43:36,682
WHO IS IT?

937
00:43:36,715 --> 00:43:38,050
IT'S THE PLUMBER.

938
00:43:38,083 --> 00:43:40,052
I'VE COME TO FIX YOUR SINK.

939
00:43:40,085 --> 00:43:43,188
[ROBOTS LAUGHING]

940
00:43:43,222 --> 00:43:45,490
ISN'T SHE SUPPOSED TO BE
WEARING SOMETHING TIGHTER

941
00:43:45,523 --> 00:43:48,093
OR FLIMSIER OR MORE REVEALING?

942
00:43:48,127 --> 00:43:50,762
WELL, I MEAN,
THAT'S THE PREFERRED ROUTE,

943
00:43:50,795 --> 00:43:53,232
- ...BUT THAT'S
NOT NECESSARILY--
- WELL, YEAH.

944
00:43:56,068 --> 00:43:57,368
[SCREAMS]

945
00:44:03,342 --> 00:44:05,743
COME ON. I CAN'T BELIEVE
YOU'VE NEVER HEARD
OF A CHIN PUPPET.

946
00:44:05,777 --> 00:44:08,547
- NO. NOT ME.
- ALL RIGHT. WELL, I'LL DO
THE WHOLE DEMO FOR YOU, OKAY?

947
00:44:08,580 --> 00:44:10,315
- OF A CHIN PUPPET?
- RIGHT. A CHIN PUPPET.

948
00:44:10,348 --> 00:44:12,117
HEY, WHY DON'T YOU SCRAMBLE
AROUND FRONT THERE,

949
00:44:12,150 --> 00:44:14,853
AND I'LL DO THE WHOLE STAGE SHOW
FOR YOU, ALL RIGHT?

950
00:44:14,887 --> 00:44:17,122
- YOU GUYS ARE GONNA LOVE THIS.
- MIKE, WHAT ARE YOU DOING
THERE, HONEY?

951
00:44:17,155 --> 00:44:18,623
- HONEY? DEAR?
- WHOA.

952
00:44:18,657 --> 00:44:20,858
♪ HEY, HOW ARE YOU DOING
AND WHAT DO YOU KNOW ♪

953
00:44:20,892 --> 00:44:23,162
♪ I'M GLAD YOU COULD BE HERE
TO SEE MY SHOW, YEAH ♪

954
00:44:23,195 --> 00:44:26,865
- OH, MY GOD!
- I DON'T GET IT.
WHY ARE YOU UPSIDE DOWN?

955
00:44:26,898 --> 00:44:28,767
WHAT'S NOT TO GET?
I'M A CHIN PUPPET.

956
00:44:28,800 --> 00:44:31,370
SO, ON EARTH, DID YOU JUST GO
AHEAD AND DO THIS FOR PEOPLE?

957
00:44:31,403 --> 00:44:32,972
- YEAH.
- AND THEY LAUGHED?

958
00:44:33,005 --> 00:44:34,773
WELL, SURE. IT'S FUNNY.
HEY, YOU'RE A GREAT CROWD.

959
00:44:34,807 --> 00:44:36,975
- DID YOU EVER GO
ON A DATE LIKE THAT?
- OF COURSE NOT.

960
00:44:37,008 --> 00:44:38,943
HEY, COME ON.
YOU GUYS WANTED TO SEE THIS.
GET INTO IT.

961
00:44:38,977 --> 00:44:41,947
I KNOW,
BUT IN OUR WILDEST DREAMS,
WE NEVER IMAGINED THIS!

962
00:44:41,980 --> 00:44:44,783
- COME ON. IT'S WHIMSICAL.
- IT'S ODD AND DISTURBING, MIKE.

963
00:44:44,817 --> 00:44:47,652
WHAT WOULD POSSESS
A PERSON TO DO THAT?
I JUST DON'T UNDERSTAND THIS.

964
00:44:47,685 --> 00:44:50,022
APPARENTLY YOU'RE NOT SUITED
TO CHIN PUPPETS.

965
00:44:50,055 --> 00:44:51,890
- LET'S JUST CALL
THE WHOLE THING OFF.
- [OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

966
00:44:51,923 --> 00:44:53,725
[ROBOTS LAUGHING]

967
00:44:53,758 --> 00:44:55,060
NOW, THAT'S FUNNY!
LOOK AT THAT!

968
00:44:55,093 --> 00:44:56,762
HE'S GOT AN UPSIDE-DOWN FACE
ON HIS CHIN!

969
00:44:56,795 --> 00:44:59,598
- NOW I GET IT. IT'S HILARIOUS.
- [LAUGHING CONTINUES]

970
00:44:59,632 --> 00:45:02,567
- [ALARM BLARING]
- [ALL SHOUTING]

971
00:45:14,947 --> 00:45:17,482
GEE, YOU'RE A HEAVY LITTLE GUY.
[GRUNTS]

972
00:45:17,515 --> 00:45:19,552
- ARE YOU OKAY?
- THAT WASN'T VERY NICE.

973
00:45:19,585 --> 00:45:21,320
ARE YOU SURE
SHE'S NOT IN HER ROOM?

974
00:45:21,353 --> 00:45:23,188
YES.

975
00:45:23,222 --> 00:45:25,157
VICTOR LEFT
A LITTLE WHILE AGO.

976
00:45:25,190 --> 00:45:27,092
MAYBE SHE WENT WITH HIM.

977
00:45:27,125 --> 00:45:29,227
[ENGLISH ACCENT]
LOOK AT THOSE LITTLE
NO-NECK MONSTERS.

978
00:45:29,260 --> 00:45:32,130
SHE DIDN'T GET OUT OF
THIS PRISON WITHOUT PERMISSION,
THAT'S FOR SURE.

979
00:45:32,163 --> 00:45:34,132
YEAH.

980
00:45:34,165 --> 00:45:37,202
BUT SHE WOULD'VE SAID GOOD-BYE.

981
00:45:37,235 --> 00:45:39,938
WHY SHOULD SHE?
WE ONLY MET HER YESTERDAY.

982
00:45:39,972 --> 00:45:42,173
OH, RIGHT. WHY CARE ABOUT
THE WELFARE OF OTHERS?

983
00:45:42,207 --> 00:45:44,408
I DON'T BLAME HER
FOR NOT WANTING TO SLEEP
IN THE "BICEMENT."

984
00:45:44,442 --> 00:45:45,910
THAT'S BRITISH FOR "BASEMENT."

985
00:45:45,943 --> 00:45:47,980
WHY, THERE'S A CHUNK
OF CREAMED SPINACH HERE.

986
00:45:48,013 --> 00:45:49,915
IT'S FUNNY, THOUGH.

987
00:45:49,948 --> 00:45:54,720
MRS. MARCH WOULDN'T EVEN LISTEN
WHEN I ASKED TO BE DISMISSED.

988
00:45:54,753 --> 00:45:58,423
AND THEN SHE KISSED ME
FULL ON THE LIPS.
I DON'T KNOW WHY.

989
00:45:58,457 --> 00:46:01,960
WHAT THE HELL IS THIS?
I MEAN, IT'S BAKED ON.

990
00:46:04,095 --> 00:46:06,898
SHE DOESN'T EVEN HAVE
ANY UNIFORMS FOR US.

991
00:46:06,932 --> 00:46:09,267
WHAT IN THE WORLD
DO YOU THINK YOU'RE DOING?

992
00:46:09,300 --> 00:46:11,570
YOU TOLD US LAST NIGHT
TO CLEAN AND POLISH IN HERE.

993
00:46:11,603 --> 00:46:15,473
BUT YOUR HANDS.
THAT WILL LEAVE A STAIN ON THEM.

994
00:46:15,507 --> 00:46:18,643
- NOW DON'T ARGUE. GO IN
AND WASH THEM IMMEDIATELY.
- RELAX.

995
00:46:18,677 --> 00:46:22,680
- SPEAKING OF STAINED...
- YOU CAN PUT THE THINGS AWAY
AFTER NINA CLEANS THEM.

996
00:46:22,713 --> 00:46:24,415
OH, JAM IT, AUNT MAY.

997
00:46:24,448 --> 00:46:27,518
MRS. MARCH, WHERE IS ANITA?

998
00:46:27,552 --> 00:46:30,355
- ANITA? OH.
- THE DEAD ONE?

999
00:46:30,388 --> 00:46:34,192
- SHE ACCIDENTALLY DROPPED
HER BRAIN ON THE FLOOR.
- SHE LEFT LAST NIGHT.

1000
00:46:34,225 --> 00:46:36,795
I WOULD LIKE TO GIVE NOTICE TOO.

1001
00:46:36,828 --> 00:46:40,098
- I WILL DISCUSS IT WITH YOU--
- AT THE STAFF MEETING.

1002
00:46:40,132 --> 00:46:43,702
- ...ANOTHER TIME.
- ♪♪ [HUMMING]

1003
00:46:45,403 --> 00:46:48,240
I WOULD GIVE ANYTHING
FOR THAT FIGURE.

1004
00:46:48,273 --> 00:46:49,742
[WHIRRING]

1005
00:46:49,775 --> 00:46:51,677
YES, IT'S DISCO NIGHT
AT GLAM SLAM.

1006
00:46:51,710 --> 00:46:55,147
- COME ON DOWN.
- ♪♪ [HUMMING]

1007
00:46:55,180 --> 00:46:58,617
- LASERIUM.
- [IMITATING WHIRRING]

1008
00:46:58,650 --> 00:47:01,920
A HOT TUB IS NOT RELAXING
WITH ALL THOSE LIGHTS.

1009
00:47:01,953 --> 00:47:03,988
NO. NEVER.

1010
00:47:04,022 --> 00:47:06,090
- HEY, GANDALF'S DOWN THERE.
- HUH?

1011
00:47:06,123 --> 00:47:08,793
- WITH THE SMOKE RINGS
AND ALL THAT.
- OH, BROTHER.

1012
00:47:08,827 --> 00:47:10,828
- THIS GUY.
- [LAUGHS]

1013
00:47:12,730 --> 00:47:14,933
- WELL. YEAH.
- I THINK THEY'RE DONE.

1014
00:47:14,967 --> 00:47:17,835
- NINA! NINA!
- QUIT LISTENING TO THAT STUFF!

1015
00:47:17,868 --> 00:47:19,938
COME HERE THIS INSTANT!

1016
00:47:19,972 --> 00:47:22,040
OH, IF ONLY RICHARD WIDMARK
WERE HERE.

1017
00:47:22,073 --> 00:47:24,910
- OH, MAN.
- I'M GONNA DO IT.
I'M GONNA GET AIRBORNE.

1018
00:47:24,943 --> 00:47:27,078
100% PURE ADRENALINE.

1019
00:47:27,112 --> 00:47:30,482
- YES, MRS. MARCH?
- YOUR NAME ISN'T NINA.

1020
00:47:30,515 --> 00:47:33,685
BUT, MRS. MARCH, SHE'S GOT
POLISH ALL OVER HER HANDS,
AND I'M NOT DOING ANYTHING.

1021
00:47:33,718 --> 00:47:37,088
I DON'T WANT YOU RUNNING
UP AND DOWN STAIRS.

1022
00:47:37,122 --> 00:47:40,258
THOSE PRETTY LEGS OF YOURS
WILL GET UGLY MUSCLES.

1023
00:47:40,292 --> 00:47:42,660
- SHE LIKES BIG PIANO LEGS
ON A WOMAN.
- SEND NINA TO ME.

1024
00:47:42,693 --> 00:47:45,097
- WHO DOESN'T?
- YES, MA'AM.

1025
00:47:45,130 --> 00:47:48,533
[MRS. MARCH]
I'LL BE IN MY ROOM.

1026
00:47:48,567 --> 00:47:51,770
♪ HERE'S CATHY WHO'S LIVED
MOST EVERYWHERE ♪

1027
00:47:51,803 --> 00:47:53,205
[LAUGHS]

1028
00:47:53,238 --> 00:47:54,538
[SIGHS]

1029
00:47:54,572 --> 00:47:56,040
BEA, COME WITH ME.

1030
00:47:56,073 --> 00:47:57,775
WHAT WILL WE BECOME?

1031
00:47:57,808 --> 00:47:59,343
I DON'T THINK THAT'S WHAT...

1032
00:48:02,647 --> 00:48:04,783
[IMITATING STAIRS CREAKING]

1033
00:48:04,817 --> 00:48:08,287
THERE. YOU SEE?
THERE ARE SIGNS OF SEEPAGE
DOWN HERE.

1034
00:48:11,657 --> 00:48:13,625
I WANT TO SHOW YOU SOMETHING.

1035
00:48:13,658 --> 00:48:17,295
THEY KEEP THEIR CHRISTMAS
DECORATIONS DOWN HERE.
IT'S AMAZING.

1036
00:48:17,328 --> 00:48:20,832
LOOK AT ALL THE AMENITIES
THAT ANITA GOT.

1037
00:48:23,168 --> 00:48:24,502
HMM.

1038
00:48:26,303 --> 00:48:28,440
ANITA WOULDN'T LEAVE
WITHOUT TAKING HER CLOTHES.

1039
00:48:28,473 --> 00:48:31,577
- HAVE YOU SEEN HER CLOTHES?
- I THINK WE'D BETTER
GET OUT OF HERE, FAST.

1040
00:48:31,610 --> 00:48:34,078
BEA, I'D HATE TO GO
IF SHE'S STILL HERE.

1041
00:48:34,112 --> 00:48:35,880
YOU'LL GO NOW
IF YOU GO WITH "MAY."

1042
00:48:35,913 --> 00:48:38,183
- "MAY"? NOW, WHO'S MAY?
- I DON'T UNDERSTAND.

1043
00:48:38,217 --> 00:48:40,118
DON'T KNOW.

1044
00:48:40,152 --> 00:48:42,487
MAN, SHE'S BOSSY.

1045
00:48:46,057 --> 00:48:48,727
IT'S TRIXIE BELDEN AND HONEY.

1046
00:48:53,132 --> 00:48:55,167
HERE. I WANNA SHOW YOU
THE TOMATOES THEY PUT UP

1047
00:48:55,200 --> 00:48:57,002
AND SOME WATERMELON
RIND PICKLES.

1048
00:48:57,035 --> 00:48:58,837
OH, THAT SOUNDS GOOD.

1049
00:48:58,870 --> 00:49:00,505
- THIS HINGE IS LOOSE.
- HMM.

1050
00:49:00,538 --> 00:49:03,375
HELP ME.

1051
00:49:03,408 --> 00:49:04,877
♪♪ [DRAMATIC FLOURISH]

1052
00:49:04,910 --> 00:49:07,512
♪♪ [HUMMING "THEME FROM
MISSION: IMPOSSIBLE]

1053
00:49:11,148 --> 00:49:12,617
♪♪ [HUMMING]

1054
00:49:12,650 --> 00:49:15,320
- NOW, WHERE DID YOU GET THAT?
- I FOUND IT UP THERE.

1055
00:49:15,353 --> 00:49:17,288
WELL, PUT THAT BACK.

1056
00:49:17,322 --> 00:49:18,957
[HIGH-PITCHED GIBBERISH]

1057
00:49:18,990 --> 00:49:20,892
OH, CRIPE.

1058
00:49:20,925 --> 00:49:22,227
IT'S OPEN!

1059
00:49:22,260 --> 00:49:24,228
HE'S THE ATOMIC VET.

1060
00:49:25,530 --> 00:49:27,165
HUH?

1061
00:49:28,900 --> 00:49:30,768
KITTY...
[MUTTERS]

1062
00:49:32,803 --> 00:49:35,240
GOD, I'M LUMPY TODAY.

1063
00:49:35,273 --> 00:49:37,475
[IMITATING GIRLS WHISPERING,
SHUSHING]

1064
00:49:37,508 --> 00:49:39,310
HMM?

1065
00:49:43,615 --> 00:49:46,618
ONE LAST EXPERIMENT BEFORE
DR. FRANK WOULD BE READY.

1066
00:49:46,652 --> 00:49:49,053
BUT THIS WAS THE MOST CRITICAL
OF ALL THE EXPERIMENTS.

1067
00:49:49,087 --> 00:49:51,255
FOR THE FIRST TIME,
THE GRAFTING OPERATION

1068
00:49:51,288 --> 00:49:53,925
WOULD BE PERFORMED
ON A LIVING HUMAN BODY,

1069
00:49:53,958 --> 00:49:57,728
AND THE BRAIN WOULD COME
FROM THE DOCTOR'S FAVORITE CAT.

1070
00:49:57,762 --> 00:49:59,630
JEEZ, IMAGINE THE SIZE
OF THE LITTER BOX.

1071
00:49:59,663 --> 00:50:01,967
- ANITA WAS READY.
- HUH?

1072
00:50:02,000 --> 00:50:06,270
JEAN SHEPHERD'S VOICE-OVERS
HAVE GOTTEN WEIRD.

1073
00:50:06,303 --> 00:50:08,373
IT'S THE STRANGEST
BED AND BREAKFAST
I'VE EVER BEEN TO.

1074
00:50:08,407 --> 00:50:09,875
[KNOCK ON DOOR]

1075
00:50:13,712 --> 00:50:15,980
- IT'S ME, NINA.
- OH.

1076
00:50:16,013 --> 00:50:18,217
WHAT ABOUT YOUR CLOTHES?

1077
00:50:19,717 --> 00:50:22,620
- NEVER MIND. LET'S GO.
- HERE. GET IN.

1078
00:50:23,822 --> 00:50:25,857
DID I HEAR SOMEONE PACKING?

1079
00:50:25,890 --> 00:50:28,227
I THOUGHT PACKING
WOULD FULFILL ME,

1080
00:50:28,260 --> 00:50:30,595
BUT NOW I JUST FEEL EMPTY.

1081
00:50:30,628 --> 00:50:32,230
OH.

1082
00:50:32,263 --> 00:50:35,533
♪♪ [OBOE]

1083
00:50:35,567 --> 00:50:39,603
THE OBOE REPRESENTS THE TENSION
AS THEY SNEAK AWAY.

1084
00:50:42,040 --> 00:50:44,108
CASPER?
[CHUCKLES]

1085
00:50:44,142 --> 00:50:46,578
♪ ROLLIN', ROLLIN', ROLLIN' ♪

1086
00:50:46,612 --> 00:50:48,547
SHE'S SPINNING DONUTS
ON THE DEEP PILE.

1087
00:50:48,580 --> 00:50:49,613
WOW.

1088
00:50:49,647 --> 00:50:52,050
BEA, SHE ALMOST SAW US.

1089
00:50:53,618 --> 00:50:56,755
LET'S WAIT AWHILE TO MAKE SURE
WE WON'T RUN INTO HER.

1090
00:50:58,088 --> 00:51:00,292
[GERMAN ACCENT]
MEIN FüHRER, I CAN WALK!

1091
00:51:01,893 --> 00:51:03,228
AH, AH, AAHH!

1092
00:51:03,262 --> 00:51:06,063
DR. FRANK, QUIT LEAVING
YOUR SKATEBOARD ON THE STAIRS!

1093
00:51:06,097 --> 00:51:08,233
[IMITATING BODY
THUDDING DOWN STAIRS]

1094
00:51:08,267 --> 00:51:11,168
[TO SOUNDTRACK MUSIC,
MRS. MARSH'S THEME]
♪ SHE'S OLD, SHE'S OLD ♪

1095
00:51:11,202 --> 00:51:14,538
♪ SHE'S OLD, SO OLD, OLD ♪

1096
00:51:14,572 --> 00:51:16,775
DID PROKOFIEV DO
THE MUSIC FOR THIS?

1097
00:51:16,808 --> 00:51:20,078
- UH, YES. ERNIE PROKOFIEV.
- ♪ LOOK OUT, SHE'S OLD ♪

1098
00:51:20,112 --> 00:51:22,547
♪ SHE CREAKS AND POPS ♪

1099
00:51:22,580 --> 00:51:26,283
LET'S FOLLOW THE WHIMSICAL
ADVENTURES OF GRANNY.
[LAUGHS]

1100
00:51:26,317 --> 00:51:28,287
- ♪♪ [LADIES' THEME]
- ♪ THEY'RE YOUNG ♪

1101
00:51:28,320 --> 00:51:31,957
♪ THEY'RE SCARED ♪

1102
00:51:31,990 --> 00:51:35,293
♪ YOUNG AND SCARED ♪

1103
00:51:35,327 --> 00:51:37,028
♪ YOUNG ♪

1104
00:51:37,062 --> 00:51:39,330
- ♪♪ [MRS. MARCH'S THEME]
- ♪ SHE-- SHE'S OLD ♪

1105
00:51:39,363 --> 00:51:42,000
♪ LOOK AT HOW OLD SHE IS ♪

1106
00:51:42,033 --> 00:51:44,402
♪ SHE CREAKS,
SHE'S SO DANG OLD ♪

1107
00:51:44,435 --> 00:51:46,538
[WHISPERS]
LET'S GO HAVE
SOME FISH AND CHIPS.

1108
00:51:46,572 --> 00:51:48,507
- ♪♪ [LADIES' THEME]
- ♪ SCARED ♪

1109
00:51:50,542 --> 00:51:53,678
♪ THEY'RE YOUNG ♪

1110
00:51:53,712 --> 00:51:56,648
- I NEVER KNEW I HAD A BASEMENT.
- ♪♪ [MRS. MARCH'S THEME]

1111
00:51:56,682 --> 00:51:58,983
♪ SHE'S OLD,
SHE'S IN THE BASEMENT ♪

1112
00:52:01,485 --> 00:52:04,488
LET'S SLIDE DOWN THE BANNISTER.
IT'S FUN.
[LAUGHS]

1113
00:52:04,522 --> 00:52:07,492
- ♪♪ [LADIES' THEME]
- ♪ YOUNG, SCARED ♪

1114
00:52:07,525 --> 00:52:11,328
♪ YOUNG STEWARDESSES ♪

1115
00:52:11,362 --> 00:52:13,532
♪ SCARED ♪

1116
00:52:13,565 --> 00:52:15,600
♪ DING ♪

1117
00:52:15,633 --> 00:52:17,902
- ♪ YOUNG ♪
- ♪ THING ♪

1118
00:52:17,935 --> 00:52:20,905
HEY, THAT LADY MADE SANDWICHES
FOR THE MEN WORKING
ON THE SPHINX.

1119
00:52:20,938 --> 00:52:21,907
[LAUGHTER]

1120
00:52:21,940 --> 00:52:25,077
OH, HEAVENS.
MY PACEMAKER. OH, DAMN.

1121
00:52:26,143 --> 00:52:29,247
THE SNOOP NIECES.
[CHUCKLES]

1122
00:52:29,280 --> 00:52:31,683
- ♪♪ [LADIES' THEME]
- ♪ WE'RE YOUNG ♪

1123
00:52:31,717 --> 00:52:34,185
♪ YOUNG, SCARED ♪

1124
00:52:34,218 --> 00:52:36,487
AAH! DOROTHY DAY!

1125
00:52:36,520 --> 00:52:37,955
SHE'S A NICE LADY.

1126
00:52:40,325 --> 00:52:42,127
- ♪♪ [MRS. MARCH'S THEME]
- ♪ NOW COME ON ♪

1127
00:52:42,160 --> 00:52:43,895
♪ LET'S GO UPSTAIRS ♪

1128
00:52:43,928 --> 00:52:45,430
♪ WE'RE SCARED, WE'RE YOUNG ♪

1129
00:52:45,463 --> 00:52:48,165
- BEA!
- A DOOBIE.

1130
00:52:49,800 --> 00:52:52,003
THIS IS GONNA BE
SOME CHASE SCENE.

1131
00:52:52,037 --> 00:52:53,070
MM.

1132
00:52:53,103 --> 00:52:55,073
♪ SHE'S OLD, SHE'S OLD ♪

1133
00:52:55,107 --> 00:52:56,675
♪ SHE CREAKS,
SHE GOES ♪

1134
00:52:56,708 --> 00:52:58,208
- BEA!
- ♪ UPSTAIRS ♪

1135
00:52:58,242 --> 00:53:00,078
[MIKE]
BEA!

1136
00:53:00,112 --> 00:53:01,880
[WHIRRING]

1137
00:53:01,913 --> 00:53:03,782
AH, GOOD RENEGADE TONIGHT.

1138
00:53:03,815 --> 00:53:05,117
WELL, BACK AT IT.

1139
00:53:05,150 --> 00:53:08,687
♪ DUM DE-DUM DE-DUM DE-DUM ♪

1140
00:53:08,720 --> 00:53:10,788
OH. THAT THING.

1141
00:53:10,822 --> 00:53:12,323
WOW.

1142
00:53:12,357 --> 00:53:15,727
OH, I JUST LOVE
THESE MONDAY KLAN MEETINGS.

1143
00:53:17,795 --> 00:53:20,865
- DO I SMELL BACON?
- [THUNDERCLAP]

1144
00:53:23,668 --> 00:53:27,505
- SEE? THE LIGHTNING
OPENED THE DOOR.
- HMM.

1145
00:53:27,538 --> 00:53:30,208
THAT'S A REAL COMPLICATED
PORTA-POTTY, ISN'T IT?

1146
00:53:30,242 --> 00:53:32,277
- I WOULDN'T WANT ONE.
- MM-MM.

1147
00:53:32,310 --> 00:53:35,813
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN,
MISS NETHERWORLD!
[IMITATING CROWD CHEERING]

1148
00:53:36,982 --> 00:53:40,118
HEY, NO SHOES, NO BRAIN,
NO SERVICE, LADY.

1149
00:53:40,152 --> 00:53:42,853
LOOKS LIKE, UH, ULTRAVIOLET.

1150
00:53:42,887 --> 00:53:45,590
- WHAT, WITH THE FROWNS AND...
- [CHUCKLES]

1151
00:53:48,827 --> 00:53:52,730
[SLOWLY]
ANYONE WANT ANYTHING?

1152
00:53:52,763 --> 00:53:54,532
BEA!

1153
00:53:54,565 --> 00:53:56,533
I-N-G-O.

1154
00:53:56,567 --> 00:53:59,937
- BEA, WHERE ARE YOU?
- B-34. BINGO.

1155
00:53:59,970 --> 00:54:01,607
ANSWER ME!

1156
00:54:04,042 --> 00:54:06,812
♪♪ [HUMMING]

1157
00:54:11,783 --> 00:54:13,885
[GASPS]
SHAVE AND A HAIRCUT!
WHAT DO WE DO?

1158
00:54:13,918 --> 00:54:17,055
I'M HERE, MRS. MARCH.

1159
00:54:17,088 --> 00:54:20,092
LET'S SEE.
THAT'S MY HARLEY KEY.

1160
00:54:20,125 --> 00:54:23,528
OH, THERE IT IS.
[MUTTERING]

1161
00:54:23,562 --> 00:54:25,563
SHE'S LOCKED US IN.

1162
00:54:25,597 --> 00:54:28,198
DIALOGUE REPLACEMENT PLAYHOUSE.

1163
00:54:28,232 --> 00:54:30,235
[NINA]
OPEN IT! I SAID OPEN IT!

1164
00:54:30,268 --> 00:54:32,103
- ♪ NO, I'VE GOT ♪
- MRS. MARCH!

1165
00:54:32,137 --> 00:54:33,938
♪ THE KEYS DOWN HERE ♪

1166
00:54:33,972 --> 00:54:34,972
WAIT.

1167
00:54:35,005 --> 00:54:37,042
SELZNICK INTERNATIONAL
PRESENTS...

1168
00:54:37,075 --> 00:54:38,543
[CHUCKLES]
THAT'S NICE.

1169
00:54:38,577 --> 00:54:40,278
I LOVE THAT ONE.

1170
00:54:43,615 --> 00:54:46,117
WELL, IT SEEMS OUR OPTIONS
ARE LIMITED.

1171
00:54:46,150 --> 00:54:48,185
ARE YOU FAMILIAR
WITH RITA MAE BROWN?

1172
00:54:48,218 --> 00:54:50,255
WOW.

1173
00:54:50,288 --> 00:54:52,790
HERE.
LET ME ADJUST YOUR AURA.

1174
00:54:54,292 --> 00:54:55,960
ERRR...

1175
00:54:55,993 --> 00:54:58,028
VICTOR!

1176
00:54:58,062 --> 00:54:59,530
GET AN INTERCOM.

1177
00:54:59,563 --> 00:55:02,033
VICTOR!

1178
00:55:02,067 --> 00:55:05,137
IN A MINUTE.
♪♪ [HUMMING]

1179
00:55:11,608 --> 00:55:13,578
- WHAT?
- WELL, YOU TOOK LONG ENOUGH.

1180
00:55:13,612 --> 00:55:16,447
- YOU CRUMPLED OLD BINT.
- THE LAWYER WILL SEE YOU
IN THE MORNING.

1181
00:55:16,480 --> 00:55:19,383
I TOLD HIM YOU WERE
GOING TO CHANGE YOUR WILL.

1182
00:55:19,417 --> 00:55:21,252
HERE.
CAREFUL OF THIS STEP HERE!
[GRUNTS]

1183
00:55:21,285 --> 00:55:24,588
[ALL IMITATING BODY
THUDDING DOWN STAIRS]

1184
00:55:24,622 --> 00:55:27,392
YOU'LL HAVE TO CHECK
THE BASEMENT DOOR.
IT BROKE LOOSE.

1185
00:55:27,425 --> 00:55:31,162
OH, MY LIFE IS GETTING
MORE INTERESTING BY THE MINUTE.

1186
00:55:31,195 --> 00:55:34,132
TALIA SHIRE IS SQUEAKY FROMME.

1187
00:55:34,165 --> 00:55:37,035
[PANTING]
IT'S EVIL HERE. RUN!

1188
00:55:39,637 --> 00:55:43,073
OH, HI.
YOUR RECEPTIONIST LET US IN.

1189
00:55:43,107 --> 00:55:44,542
HI.

1190
00:55:46,443 --> 00:55:48,580
YOU'VE FAILED.

1191
00:55:50,715 --> 00:55:53,317
OH, YOU GOT ONE OF THOSE, HUH?

1192
00:55:53,350 --> 00:55:55,487
OH, MEOW.

1193
00:55:55,520 --> 00:55:57,955
[CHUCKLES]

1194
00:55:57,988 --> 00:56:00,592
OH, ISN'T IT CUTE?
YES, IT IS.

1195
00:56:00,625 --> 00:56:02,427
- [MEOWS]
- HELLO. YES.

1196
00:56:02,460 --> 00:56:06,463
- IT'S LIZZ WINSTEAD.
- SHE THINKS SHE'S A CAT!

1197
00:56:06,497 --> 00:56:09,300
AND I JUST BOUGHT NEW FURNITURE!

1198
00:56:09,333 --> 00:56:11,702
NICE KITTY.

1199
00:56:11,735 --> 00:56:14,472
PICK HER UP BY THE NAPE.

1200
00:56:16,808 --> 00:56:19,743
- EW.
- [SNARLING]

1201
00:56:19,777 --> 00:56:22,880
GREAT. SHE'S A SIAMESE TOO.

1202
00:56:22,913 --> 00:56:25,183
CLEAN MY LITTER BOX.

1203
00:56:25,217 --> 00:56:27,785
- [HISSES]
- OH! JUMP-STARTED GRANDMA.

1204
00:56:27,818 --> 00:56:31,088
WELL, I SEE YOU STILL RESENT
THE WAY MRS. MARCH TREATS YOU.

1205
00:56:31,122 --> 00:56:33,057
- I CAN'T SAY THAT I BLAME YOU.
- [CHUCKLES]

1206
00:56:33,090 --> 00:56:36,160
KITTY'S ALWAYS BEEN
VERY FOND OF ME. DON'T YOU?

1207
00:56:36,193 --> 00:56:38,763
- [PURRING]
- EW, SHE'S GOT EAR MITES.

1208
00:56:38,797 --> 00:56:41,232
DOES SHE HAVE ALL THE INSTINCTS
OF A CAT?

1209
00:56:41,265 --> 00:56:43,568
- WITH HALF THE CALORIES.
- WATCH.

1210
00:56:44,702 --> 00:56:47,305
SHE HAD HER SHOTS?

1211
00:56:49,807 --> 00:56:53,478
THIS MOUSE HAS THE BRAIN
OF NEWT GINGRICH. NOW EAT!

1212
00:56:56,147 --> 00:56:58,282
RUNNERS, TAKE YOUR MARKS.

1213
00:56:58,315 --> 00:56:59,683
[SNARLING]

1214
00:56:59,717 --> 00:57:02,520
SOMEBODY HELP ME!
OH, GOD!

1215
00:57:02,553 --> 00:57:04,688
- [SNARLING CONTINUES]
- OW! OOH! [MUTTERS]

1216
00:57:06,190 --> 00:57:08,560
[MUFFLED SHOUTING]

1217
00:57:09,627 --> 00:57:11,562
TASTE IT ALL.

1218
00:57:13,030 --> 00:57:16,167
- SHE ATE IT.
- I WANTED IT.

1219
00:57:16,200 --> 00:57:19,937
[IMITATING CHEWING, GULPS]

1220
00:57:19,970 --> 00:57:22,107
OH.

1221
00:57:22,140 --> 00:57:24,608
- HEY, IT'S
NORMA DESMOND'S HOUSE.
- OH.

1222
00:57:24,642 --> 00:57:27,145
♪♪ [FLUTE]

1223
00:57:27,178 --> 00:57:31,148
PRELUDE TO THE AFTERNOON
OF A SEXUALLY AROUSED GAS MASK.

1224
00:57:33,183 --> 00:57:37,422
I DON'T FEEL DEAD.
ACTUALLY, I FEEL PRETTY GOOD.

1225
00:57:37,455 --> 00:57:40,492
I SORT OF THINK,
THEREFORE I SORT OF AM.

1226
00:57:40,525 --> 00:57:44,162
DIVORCED,
HARASSED BY CREDITORS.

1227
00:57:44,195 --> 00:57:47,932
- BEA.
- LORNA LUFT GAZES
OUT THE WINDOW.

1228
00:57:47,965 --> 00:57:50,802
- IS THAT ANITA?
- THE REAL ANITA HILL?

1229
00:57:50,835 --> 00:57:53,437
- WHERE? OH, I DON'T THINK SO.
- SORRY.

1230
00:57:55,440 --> 00:57:58,475
I'M LOOKING
FOR THE MANOS SET.

1231
00:57:58,508 --> 00:58:01,980
[IMITATING GRUNTING]

1232
00:58:02,013 --> 00:58:04,548
GOING UPHILL IS HARD
WHEN YOU'RE DEAD.

1233
00:58:04,582 --> 00:58:05,717
[GRUNTING]

1234
00:58:05,750 --> 00:58:07,752
THINK SHE'S DEAD ON HER FEET.

1235
00:58:07,785 --> 00:58:09,853
- [LAUGHING]
- OHH.

1236
00:58:09,887 --> 00:58:11,455
SORRY.

1237
00:58:13,357 --> 00:58:15,660
HMM?

1238
00:58:15,693 --> 00:58:17,962
♪ UH, JUMP THE ONE YOU'RE WITH,
OH, YEAH ♪

1239
00:58:17,995 --> 00:58:19,130
[BEA]
LOOK OUT!

1240
00:58:19,163 --> 00:58:20,197
[SCREAMS]

1241
00:58:20,230 --> 00:58:21,198
[GASPS]

1242
00:58:21,232 --> 00:58:23,333
SOMEBODY HELP HER!

1243
00:58:23,367 --> 00:58:25,237
I'LL SAVE YOU, NELL!

1244
00:58:25,270 --> 00:58:28,072
- ♪♪ [HUMMING]
- [CREATURE GROWLING]

1245
00:58:28,105 --> 00:58:30,007
WHAT-- ALF, NO!

1246
00:58:30,040 --> 00:58:33,010
[LAUGHING]
ALF.

1247
00:58:33,043 --> 00:58:36,882
OH, GET THE HOSE! OH, JEEZ,
I SHOULD'VE HAD HIM FIXED.

1248
00:58:38,015 --> 00:58:39,517
[DR. FRANK]
BACK, HANS! BACK!

1249
00:58:39,550 --> 00:58:41,085
- HMM?
- PERSONA.

1250
00:58:41,118 --> 00:58:42,987
- INTERIORS.
- SAME THING.

1251
00:58:43,020 --> 00:58:44,388
[GROWLING]

1252
00:58:44,422 --> 00:58:46,857
I'M VISIBLY REACTING.

1253
00:58:46,890 --> 00:58:48,558
[GROWLING CONTINUES]

1254
00:58:48,592 --> 00:58:52,230
COME ON. BACK IT UP, BUDDY.
LET'S SEE SOME I.D.

1255
00:58:52,263 --> 00:58:54,732
IT'S SO WEIRD WHEN PEOPLE
DRESS UP THEIR DOGS.

1256
00:58:54,765 --> 00:58:57,435
- [CHUCKLES]
- HANS. HANS!

1257
00:58:57,468 --> 00:59:01,205
HE'S SPEAKING IN TONGUES.
[LAUGHS]

1258
00:59:01,238 --> 00:59:03,908
HMM, I'D LIKE A DOG.

1259
00:59:06,443 --> 00:59:09,513
[LAUGHS]
LOOK AT HIS FEET.
HE'S STILL A PUPPY.

1260
00:59:09,547 --> 00:59:13,350
- [MUTTERS]
- ♪ SO WE CHANGE PARTNERS ♪

1261
00:59:13,383 --> 00:59:15,320
HUH?

1262
00:59:15,353 --> 00:59:17,622
GEE, DO YOU THINK HE'LL CHEW
HIS OWN HEAD OFF?

1263
00:59:17,655 --> 00:59:20,592
I STILL THINK
YOU SHOULD'VE LOCKED THEM UP.

1264
00:59:20,625 --> 00:59:23,493
THEY'RE NOT ABOUT
TO LEAVE THIS HOUSE
AFTER WHAT THEY'VE WITNESSED.

1265
00:59:23,527 --> 00:59:25,663
THEY KNOW HANS IS OUTSIDE THERE.

1266
00:59:25,697 --> 00:59:27,665
PASS THE CARAMELIZED ONIONS.

1267
00:59:27,698 --> 00:59:29,367
[SMACKS LIPS]

1268
00:59:29,400 --> 00:59:31,402
SO, MORE BLOOD?

1269
00:59:35,205 --> 00:59:38,242
I HOPE THERE'S NO SPOTS
ON THE WINE GLASSES.

1270
00:59:38,275 --> 00:59:40,912
EVEN IF WE COULD GET PAST
THAT CREATURE OUTSIDE,

1271
00:59:40,945 --> 00:59:42,780
THERE'S STILL
THE ELECTRIC FENCE.

1272
00:59:42,813 --> 00:59:46,717
- OOH.
- THE PHONE'S DEAD.
CAN'T GET HELP THAT WAY.

1273
00:59:46,750 --> 00:59:49,220
- THIS IS THE FEMALE PAPILLON.
- PAPIETTE.

1274
00:59:49,253 --> 00:59:52,990
- IF WE COULD GET THE CAR--
- WE COULD GO FOR A DRIVE.

1275
00:59:53,023 --> 00:59:55,327
THAT'S IT! VICTOR!

1276
00:59:55,360 --> 00:59:57,462
VICTOR?

1277
00:59:57,495 --> 00:59:59,963
HE LIKES ME, I GUESS.

1278
00:59:59,997 --> 01:00:01,965
BUT I'M SEEING CLAUS VON BüLOW.

1279
01:00:01,998 --> 01:00:03,902
IF YOU COULD GET
THE KEYS FROM HIM...

1280
01:00:03,935 --> 01:00:06,070
[WHISPERING GIBBERISH]

1281
01:00:06,103 --> 01:00:08,372
- OH, ROCHESTER!
- [WHISPERS] AAHHH.

1282
01:00:08,405 --> 01:00:11,475
- HEY.
- HELLO, MARY.

1283
01:00:11,508 --> 01:00:13,477
I WAS HAVING
A LITTLE NIGHTCAP.

1284
01:00:13,510 --> 01:00:16,113
AND IT GOT OUT OF HAND.

1285
01:00:16,147 --> 01:00:18,548
WHOA, SHE'S GONNA PULL
A GROIN MUSCLE.

1286
01:00:18,582 --> 01:00:20,918
WHO DO YOU THINK YOU ARE,
PINCHING ME?

1287
01:00:20,952 --> 01:00:22,920
WELL...
[LAUGHS]

1288
01:00:22,953 --> 01:00:24,922
[LAUGHS]
THAT MAGOO.
YOU'VE DONE IT AGAIN.

1289
01:00:24,955 --> 01:00:26,990
MAYBE YOU'D LIKE SOME COMPANY.
SOMEONE LIKE ME?

1290
01:00:27,023 --> 01:00:28,625
WHOA. HOW'S THE TUMBLER
OF SCOTCH?

1291
01:00:28,658 --> 01:00:30,127
- YEAH.
- [WHISTLES]

1292
01:00:30,160 --> 01:00:32,030
THAT'S MORE LIKE IT.

1293
01:00:32,063 --> 01:00:36,100
OH, I HAVEN'T MADE LOVE
TO A WOMAN WITH TEETH
IN SO LONG.

1294
01:00:36,133 --> 01:00:37,902
DON'T YOU LIKE ME, VICTOR?

1295
01:00:37,935 --> 01:00:40,872
OH, IF YOU WERE ONLY 80.
[CHUCKLES, MUTTERS]

1296
01:00:42,140 --> 01:00:45,610
OH, THERE'S NOTHING LIKE
THE FEEL OF A REAL HIP.

1297
01:00:45,643 --> 01:00:48,545
MMM, YOU TASTE
LIKE A WOOLWORTH'S COUNTER.

1298
01:00:49,613 --> 01:00:51,248
WAIT.

1299
01:00:51,282 --> 01:00:52,950
I WANT YOU TO DRESS
IN LEDERHOSEN.

1300
01:00:52,983 --> 01:00:55,920
OHHH.

1301
01:00:55,953 --> 01:00:59,090
[IMITATING CRICKETS CHIRPING]

1302
01:01:01,692 --> 01:01:02,860
HMM.

1303
01:01:02,893 --> 01:01:04,862
HANS IS CHAINED.

1304
01:01:04,895 --> 01:01:07,198
- LET'S GO OUTSIDE.
- OUTSIDE?

1305
01:01:07,232 --> 01:01:09,200
LET'S PLAY SOME SHUFFLEBOARD.

1306
01:01:09,233 --> 01:01:10,902
I THINK I'D LIKE THAT.

1307
01:01:10,935 --> 01:01:14,872
AND THEN WE CAN TAKE
A REAL LONG TIME
TO WRITE A CHECK SOMEWHERE.

1308
01:01:22,247 --> 01:01:25,550
♪♪

1309
01:01:25,583 --> 01:01:28,352
OH, GOD, THEY'RE GONNA SING!

1310
01:01:28,385 --> 01:01:30,822
MR. AND MRS. BRIDGE.

1311
01:01:32,157 --> 01:01:34,858
WAS IT MY RIPPLING GLUTEALS
THAT DID IT TO YOU?

1312
01:01:34,892 --> 01:01:36,260
[CHUCKLES]

1313
01:01:39,097 --> 01:01:41,998
THE JOB ISN'T SO BAD
IF YOU KNOW HOW TO HANDLE IT.

1314
01:01:42,032 --> 01:01:45,737
KNOCK BACK A FEW,
CLOSE MY EYES,
AND THINK OF ENGLAND.

1315
01:01:50,307 --> 01:01:52,277
[MRS. MARSH]
VICTOR! VICTOR!

1316
01:01:52,310 --> 01:01:55,045
AW, CRIPES,
MISS HAVISHAM NEEDS ME.

1317
01:01:55,078 --> 01:01:57,615
I GOTTA GO SERVICE GRANDMA.

1318
01:01:57,648 --> 01:01:59,083
OH!

1319
01:02:01,685 --> 01:02:04,488
♪♪ [HUMMING]

1320
01:02:04,522 --> 01:02:06,490
BLIMEY, I HOPE I DON'T
GET ATTACKED OUT HERE

1321
01:02:06,523 --> 01:02:09,427
WHEN I'M ALL ALONE,
WEARING MY SPIKE HEELS.

1322
01:02:09,460 --> 01:02:11,095
WALKING THROUGH
ALL THIS TALL GRASS

1323
01:02:11,128 --> 01:02:12,763
WOULD MAKE ME
PARTICULARLY UNSTABLE

1324
01:02:12,797 --> 01:02:14,765
SHOULD ANYTHING HAPPEN,
LIKE I'M ATTACKED.

1325
01:02:14,798 --> 01:02:18,302
I ONLY ASSUME THERE ISN'T SOME
KIND OF MUTILATED HELL BEAST
RUNNING AROUND

1326
01:02:18,335 --> 01:02:21,905
THAT MAYBE COULD
SHRED ME PITILESSLY.
[CHUCKLES]

1327
01:02:21,938 --> 01:02:24,142
[GROWLING SOFTLY]

1328
01:02:26,643 --> 01:02:30,147
AH, HERE'S SOMETHING
THAT CAN CAUSE ME
IRREPARABLE DAMAGE.

1329
01:02:30,180 --> 01:02:32,150
- [HISSES]
- WHAT ARE YOU DOING UP THERE?

1330
01:02:32,183 --> 01:02:35,385
ANITA, WHAT'S THE MATTER
WITH YOU?

1331
01:02:35,418 --> 01:02:37,288
DON'T YOU KNOW ME?

1332
01:02:37,322 --> 01:02:39,890
ANITA, LISTEN TO ME. IT'S--
[SCREAMING]

1333
01:02:41,358 --> 01:02:43,360
- WELL, THE HECK WITH YOU, THEN.
- [HISSES]

1334
01:02:43,393 --> 01:02:45,428
OOH.

1335
01:02:45,462 --> 01:02:50,100
MM, I WISH I WAS
HARRY CONNICK'S GIRLFRIEND.

1336
01:02:50,133 --> 01:02:53,137
I'LL NEVER GET TO THE PYRENEES.

1337
01:02:53,170 --> 01:02:56,107
[HANS GROWLING]

1338
01:02:56,140 --> 01:02:58,675
I HEAR WILLIAM CONRAD.

1339
01:03:00,377 --> 01:03:02,680
I THINK IT'S THE DOBERMAN GANG.

1340
01:03:04,215 --> 01:03:06,617
- STELLA! WOOF, WOOF.
- [GROWLING CONTINUES]

1341
01:03:06,650 --> 01:03:08,285
STELLA!

1342
01:03:12,857 --> 01:03:14,158
HMM?

1343
01:03:14,192 --> 01:03:15,960
ANITA!

1344
01:03:17,462 --> 01:03:19,830
WE GOT CATS.

1345
01:03:19,863 --> 01:03:22,400
STAY RIGHT THERE.
DON'T MOVE.

1346
01:03:22,433 --> 01:03:24,602
I'M COMING.

1347
01:03:24,635 --> 01:03:26,303
♪♪ [IMITATING SOUNDTRACK MUSIC]

1348
01:03:30,708 --> 01:03:32,843
OH, BOY, OH, BOY!
I'VE ALWAYS WANTED A PET.

1349
01:03:32,877 --> 01:03:35,680
SHE'S TRAINED,
AND SHE WEARS MY SIZE.
[LAUGHS]

1350
01:03:35,713 --> 01:03:37,382
♪♪ [UPBEAT]

1351
01:03:37,415 --> 01:03:40,217
♪ THERE'S A GIRL ON THE ROOF,
AND SHE THINKS SHE'S A CAT ♪

1352
01:03:40,250 --> 01:03:42,253
♪ SHE THINKS SHE'S A CAT,
BUT SHE'S NOT, NO, SHE'S NOT ♪

1353
01:03:42,287 --> 01:03:44,422
♪ THERE'S A GIRL ON THE ROOF,
AND SHE THINKS SHE'S A CAT ♪

1354
01:03:44,455 --> 01:03:46,257
♪ BUT SHE AIN'T NO CAT,
NO, SHE AIN'T NO CAT ♪

1355
01:03:46,290 --> 01:03:48,725
♪ ARE YOU SURE, ARE YOU SURE,
ARE YOU SURE, ARE YOU SURE? ♪

1356
01:03:48,758 --> 01:03:52,263
- ♪ SHE IS NOT A CAT, YOU KNOW ♪
- ♪ SHE IS NOT A CAT ♪

1357
01:03:52,297 --> 01:03:55,933
♪ SHE IS JUST FROM MEXICO ♪

1358
01:03:55,967 --> 01:03:59,270
- ♪ MEXICO ♪
- ♪ SHE'S NOT A CAT ♪

1359
01:03:59,303 --> 01:04:02,038
♪ AND THAT IS THAT ♪

1360
01:04:02,072 --> 01:04:03,773
♪ SHE'S NOT A... ♪

1361
01:04:03,807 --> 01:04:07,177
THE "CAT SUITE" FROM CAROUSEL.

1362
01:04:10,848 --> 01:04:12,450
[SNARLING]

1363
01:04:12,483 --> 01:04:15,452
ANITA, IF I CALL
THE FIRE DEPARTMENT AGAIN,
THEY'LL START LAUGHING.

1364
01:04:15,485 --> 01:04:16,953
ANITA.

1365
01:04:16,987 --> 01:04:18,923
[CROW]
WHERE EAGLES DARE.

1366
01:04:18,957 --> 01:04:22,058
[SNARLING CONTINUES]

1367
01:04:22,092 --> 01:04:25,095
HMM? OH, IT'S JOEY RAMONE!
[CHUCKLES]

1368
01:04:25,128 --> 01:04:27,532
WELL, WHAT DO YOU KNOW?

1369
01:04:27,565 --> 01:04:29,300
[NINA]
ANITA, LET ME HELP YOU.

1370
01:04:29,333 --> 01:04:30,868
[MIKE]
I KNOW A VET IN TOWN.

1371
01:04:30,902 --> 01:04:33,370
SHE'S A CAT WHO BITES HER NAILS.

1372
01:04:37,608 --> 01:04:39,910
[HISSES]

1373
01:04:39,943 --> 01:04:42,112
♪♪ [WHISTLING]

1374
01:04:44,182 --> 01:04:47,250
- [GROWLING]
- ♪♪ [CONTINUES]

1375
01:04:47,283 --> 01:04:50,587
- THAT IS INDIGESTION.
- ANITA, WAIT.

1376
01:04:50,620 --> 01:04:52,523
TO CATCH A CAT.

1377
01:04:52,557 --> 01:04:54,758
[SNARLING]

1378
01:04:54,792 --> 01:04:56,960
I'LL CATCH YOU.
[CHUCKLES]

1379
01:04:56,993 --> 01:04:59,063
I'LL CATCH YOU. WOOF.

1380
01:04:59,097 --> 01:05:01,065
[SNORTS]

1381
01:05:01,098 --> 01:05:03,100
- [GROWLING]
- TAKE MY HAND.

1382
01:05:03,133 --> 01:05:05,803
I'M A STRANGER IN PARADISE.

1383
01:05:05,837 --> 01:05:08,205
SO, DID THEY PUT STUFFING
AROUND THE CAT BRAIN

1384
01:05:08,238 --> 01:05:10,007
SO IT WOULDN'T RATTLE AROUND
INSIDE HER SKULL?

1385
01:05:10,040 --> 01:05:15,045
GOTTA GO WALKIES,
FOR CRYING OUT LOUD! WALKIES!

1386
01:05:15,078 --> 01:05:16,547
[GROWLING]

1387
01:05:16,580 --> 01:05:18,915
THIS IS NO GOOD.
WE'RE ON TOP OF THE MONUMENT.

1388
01:05:18,948 --> 01:05:22,152
- ♪♪ [HUMMING]
- ANITA.

1389
01:05:22,185 --> 01:05:24,222
- [HISSES]
- ANITA!

1390
01:05:24,255 --> 01:05:25,723
- [SCREAMS]
- [CHUCKLES]

1391
01:05:25,757 --> 01:05:27,358
AND SHE FLOATS GENTLY
TO HER DEATH.

1392
01:05:27,392 --> 01:05:29,093
- AH.
- EW.

1393
01:05:29,127 --> 01:05:32,062
WELL, SO MUCH FOR THE "LANDING
ON YOUR FEET" THEORY.

1394
01:05:34,532 --> 01:05:37,167
OOH, THAT'S A NICE BATHROBE
SHE'S GOT THERE,
WITH THE FLOWER PRINT.

1395
01:05:37,200 --> 01:05:39,470
- LOVELY.
- [MUTTERING]

1396
01:05:39,503 --> 01:05:40,972
...THE HUMAN EYE.

1397
01:05:41,005 --> 01:05:43,807
- OH, YOU JUST POP IT IN
AND SEE STUFF.
- FRANK?

1398
01:05:43,840 --> 01:05:46,610
OH, HI.
UH, I, UH, KILLED YOUR CAT.

1399
01:05:46,643 --> 01:05:48,578
I'M SORRY.

1400
01:05:50,113 --> 01:05:53,417
SHE'S UNCONSCIOUS,
BUT SHE'LL LIVE.

1401
01:05:53,450 --> 01:05:56,553
- NO.
- SHE WILL LIVE.

1402
01:05:56,587 --> 01:06:00,090
- NO.
- ANITA WON'T. SHE'S DEAD.

1403
01:06:00,123 --> 01:06:02,427
AW, NUTS. WAIT HERE.

1404
01:06:04,862 --> 01:06:08,298
NINA, DEAR,
COME ALONG WITH US NOW.

1405
01:06:08,332 --> 01:06:10,300
IT'S ALEXANDER'S RAGTIME BAND.

1406
01:06:10,333 --> 01:06:12,670
YOU'VE HAD A BAD SHOCK.

1407
01:06:12,703 --> 01:06:16,007
GET OUT OF HERE, BOTH OF YOU.

1408
01:06:16,040 --> 01:06:19,310
- WELL, IT'S MY HOUSE.
- SHE'S STAYING WITH ME.

1409
01:06:19,343 --> 01:06:20,978
THAT'S MARTIN BALSAM UP THERE.

1410
01:06:21,012 --> 01:06:22,613
- HMM?
- I SWEAR.

1411
01:06:24,582 --> 01:06:27,283
WHOA, LOOK AT HER RUN.
ZOOM.

1412
01:06:27,317 --> 01:06:29,287
[IMITATES CAR PASSING BY]

1413
01:06:33,357 --> 01:06:36,027
TIME ELAPSED.
JUST TAKE OUR WORD FOR IT.

1414
01:06:36,060 --> 01:06:38,028
♪♪ [HUMMING]

1415
01:06:38,062 --> 01:06:40,497
SO, HOW'S OUR LITTLE
SANDY DUNCAN TODAY, HMM?

1416
01:06:40,530 --> 01:06:41,698
OW.

1417
01:06:41,732 --> 01:06:44,702
WHY DON'T YOU
DO SOMETHING FOR HER?

1418
01:06:44,735 --> 01:06:47,170
I'VE DONE WHAT I CAN FOR NOW.

1419
01:06:47,203 --> 01:06:49,407
LATER, AN OPERATION
MIGHT BE POSSIBLE.

1420
01:06:49,440 --> 01:06:51,608
YOU KNOW, BEAUTY IS IN
THE EYE OF THE BEHOLDER-- OH!

1421
01:06:51,642 --> 01:06:53,777
I'M PRESERVING THE EYE.
LET ME SHOW YOU.

1422
01:06:53,810 --> 01:06:56,247
- COME OVER HERE.
- JEEZ, THEY'RE FUSING SPECIES
LEFT AND RIGHT,

1423
01:06:56,280 --> 01:06:59,217
AND THEY CAN'T
GIVE HER AN EYEBALL?

1424
01:06:59,250 --> 01:07:02,018
- IT'S A MARTINIZER.
- [ELECTRICITY ARCING]

1425
01:07:02,052 --> 01:07:05,588
THE CELLULAR STRUCTURE'S
BEING KEPT ALIVE
BY THESE ELECTRICAL VIBRATIONS.

1426
01:07:05,622 --> 01:07:08,625
- COOL, HUH?
- I USE THE SAME PRINCIPLE
IN KEEPING THAT HAND ALIVE.

1427
01:07:08,658 --> 01:07:11,662
EAT AT JOE'S. EAT AT JOE'S.
EAT AT JOE'S.

1428
01:07:11,695 --> 01:07:13,330
NINA'S A VERY LUCKY GIRL.

1429
01:07:13,363 --> 01:07:15,432
SHE'S GOT ME FOR A DOCTOR.

1430
01:07:15,465 --> 01:07:17,568
- YOU THINK THAT IRONICAL?
- "IRONICAL"?

1431
01:07:17,602 --> 01:07:20,470
- LET ME EXPLAIN.
- ABC-DEF-GHI-JKL-MNOP-
QRSTUV-WXYZ.

1432
01:07:20,503 --> 01:07:24,108
I'M THE ONLY MAN ALIVE TODAY
CAPABLE OF RESTORING
YOUR FRIEND'S SIGHT.

1433
01:07:24,142 --> 01:07:25,777
AND I'M VERY EXCITED ABOUT IT.

1434
01:07:25,810 --> 01:07:27,945
DR. ALEXIS CARREL,
WHO PIONEERED

1435
01:07:27,978 --> 01:07:29,880
THE TRANSPLANTING
OF VITAL HUMAN ORGANS--

1436
01:07:29,913 --> 01:07:32,082
DO YOU ALWAYS HAVE TO CLENCH
YOUR TEETH WHEN YOU TALK?

1437
01:07:32,115 --> 01:07:35,652
...KEPT AN ANIMAL'S HEART ALIVE
FOR MANY YEARS.

1438
01:07:35,685 --> 01:07:38,555
- BUT I'M BORING YOU.
- FOR THIS,
HE RECEIVED THE NOBEL PRIZE.

1439
01:07:38,588 --> 01:07:40,490
I GOT A PEOPLE'S CHOICE AWARD.

1440
01:07:40,523 --> 01:07:43,160
AND I, WHO HAVE
SO FAR SURPASSED HIS EFFORT--

1441
01:07:43,193 --> 01:07:46,697
SURELY YOU DON'T WANT
TO COMPARE YOURSELF
WITH DR. CARREL?

1442
01:07:46,730 --> 01:07:48,032
HE WAS HUMANE.

1443
01:07:48,065 --> 01:07:50,133
I, TOO,
FIGHT TO PRESERVE LIFE

1444
01:07:50,167 --> 01:07:52,903
AND TO FIND THE MEANS
TO IMPROVE THE LIVES
OF FUTURE GENERATIONS.

1445
01:07:52,937 --> 01:07:54,238
BUT I KILL PEOPLE.

1446
01:07:54,272 --> 01:07:56,573
YOUR VIEWPOINT
IS THAT NARROW, IGNORANT ONE

1447
01:07:56,607 --> 01:07:58,808
HELD BY
THE MEDICAL SOCIETY TODAY,

1448
01:07:58,842 --> 01:08:01,378
WHICH FORCES ME TO WORK
IN A PLACE LIKE THIS,

1449
01:08:01,412 --> 01:08:04,248
TO GIVE IN TO THE WHIMS
OF A FOOLISH OLD WOMAN,

1450
01:08:04,282 --> 01:08:07,417
BECAUSE SHE CAN SUPPLY ME
WITH THE FUNDS I NEED
TO CONTINUE MY WORK.

1451
01:08:07,450 --> 01:08:10,020
- WOW.
- YOU THINK I DON'T CRY?
I CRY.

1452
01:08:10,053 --> 01:08:12,490
[MOANING]

1453
01:08:12,523 --> 01:08:15,092
♪ SHE'S JUST
A POP-EYED OCULIST ♪

1454
01:08:15,125 --> 01:08:17,962
- NINA?
- YES, BEA?

1455
01:08:17,995 --> 01:08:20,965
I-- I CAN'T SEE. WHY--

1456
01:08:20,998 --> 01:08:23,467
WELL, YOU HAVE A DIAPER
ON YOUR FACE, DEAR.

1457
01:08:23,500 --> 01:08:26,970
- SOMETHING HAPPENED.
- DON'T THINK ABOUT IT NOW.

1458
01:08:27,003 --> 01:08:29,207
"DON'T THINK ABOUT IT"?

1459
01:08:29,240 --> 01:08:31,208
ARE YOU LISTENING?
THIS IS IMPORTANT.

1460
01:08:31,242 --> 01:08:32,375
YES?

1461
01:08:32,408 --> 01:08:35,045
WE MUST BE READY
IF A CHANCE COMES.

1462
01:08:35,078 --> 01:08:37,347
I REMEMBER NOW.
IT WAS ANITA.

1463
01:08:37,380 --> 01:08:39,217
- WHAT'S GOING ON?
- SHE--

1464
01:08:39,250 --> 01:08:42,052
OH, MY EYE! MY EYE!

1465
01:08:42,085 --> 01:08:45,188
- MY EYE! [SOBBING]
- OH, SHE'S GOT
PHYLLIS DILLER-ITIS.

1466
01:08:48,158 --> 01:08:50,527
OH, WHOOPS.
THAT WAS WINDOW CLEANER.
OH, SORRY.

1467
01:08:50,560 --> 01:08:52,730
BETTER LEAVE.
GIVE THIS A CHANCE
TO TAKE EFFECT.

1468
01:08:52,763 --> 01:08:54,665
[CRYING]

1469
01:08:54,698 --> 01:08:56,400
I'M A DOCTOR.
I'LL TAKE CARE OF HER.

1470
01:08:56,433 --> 01:08:57,735
[IMITATING DR. McCOY
FROM STAR TREK]
JIM.

1471
01:08:57,768 --> 01:09:00,337
I'M SURE YOU WILL
TAKE EXCELLENT CARE OF HER

1472
01:09:00,370 --> 01:09:03,773
UNTIL YOUR PLANS CALL
FOR SOMETHING ELSE.

1473
01:09:03,807 --> 01:09:07,010
OR AM I TO BE
THE NEXT ONE, DOCTOR?

1474
01:09:07,043 --> 01:09:10,113
OR SHOULD I SAY,
HERR DOKTOR?

1475
01:09:10,147 --> 01:09:11,848
- A SELZNICK--
- HEY. HEY.

1476
01:09:11,882 --> 01:09:13,350
OH.

1477
01:09:13,383 --> 01:09:15,818
[CROW]
GREYSTOKE: THE DESTRUCTION
OF JARED-SYN.

1478
01:09:15,852 --> 01:09:17,988
- [LAUGHING]
- THERE.

1479
01:09:18,022 --> 01:09:20,490
- GOT ALL THE CLOTHES?
- YES.

1480
01:09:20,523 --> 01:09:22,458
AND MADE MY HAIR APPOINTMENT?

1481
01:09:22,492 --> 01:09:25,062
I TOOK CARE OF EVERYTHING
ON YOUR LIST

1482
01:09:25,095 --> 01:09:26,763
WHILE YOU WERE TALKING
WITH THE LAWYER.

1483
01:09:26,797 --> 01:09:28,965
- DID YOU PICK UP
MY CANDY PANTS?
- HAIR APPOINTMENT--

1484
01:09:28,998 --> 01:09:31,335
MONDAY, 10:00 A.M.,
CHARLES OF THE RITZ--

1485
01:09:31,368 --> 01:09:34,338
- [IMITATING RICHARD NIXON]
I AM NOT A CROOK.
- ...UNDER NINA'S NAME.

1486
01:09:34,372 --> 01:09:35,438
♪♪ [IMITATES DRAMATIC FLOURISH]

1487
01:09:35,472 --> 01:09:38,075
I WANT NINA
TO MODEL THESE LATER,

1488
01:09:38,108 --> 01:09:40,010
AFTER I'VE RESTED.

1489
01:09:40,043 --> 01:09:41,645
YOU TELL HER.

1490
01:09:41,678 --> 01:09:43,880
YEAH, FINE, MRS. PYNCHON.

1491
01:09:43,913 --> 01:09:46,783
DO ANYTHING FOR YOU.

1492
01:09:46,817 --> 01:09:49,587
HMM, NOT ENOUGH VINEGAR
IN THE WATER.

1493
01:09:49,620 --> 01:09:52,188
STREAKS, HMM.

1494
01:09:52,222 --> 01:09:54,392
- THEY'RE BACK.
- WITH NEW OUTFITS!

1495
01:09:54,425 --> 01:09:56,460
I'LL HAVE TO LEAVE YOU NOW.

1496
01:09:56,493 --> 01:09:59,697
REMEMBER, I'M GOING TO TRY
TO GET US OUT OF HERE TONIGHT.

1497
01:09:59,730 --> 01:10:02,065
STAY ALIVE,
WHATEVER MAY OCCUR.

1498
01:10:02,098 --> 01:10:03,733
FORGET ABOUT ME.
I WON'T GO.

1499
01:10:03,767 --> 01:10:05,735
WELL, THAT'LL MAKE IT EASIER.

1500
01:10:05,768 --> 01:10:08,105
BEA, DON'T TALK LIKE THAT.

1501
01:10:08,138 --> 01:10:10,740
I'VE BEEN MEANING
TO TELL YOU THAT
THE WHOLE MOVIE.

1502
01:10:12,475 --> 01:10:15,412
UH, ISN'T SHE WEARING
HER HEADBAND A LITTLE LOW?

1503
01:10:19,148 --> 01:10:22,085
- SELZNICK INTER--
- [SHUSHING]

1504
01:10:22,118 --> 01:10:24,422
- MRS. MARSH DIDN'T REALIZE
HER NEW BODY HAD--
- [ROBOTS] AAH!

1505
01:10:24,455 --> 01:10:26,557
...SUCH A SATISFACTORY SHAPE.

1506
01:10:26,590 --> 01:10:28,858
PERHAPS NOT AS SPECTACULAR
AS THE ENGLISH GIRL,

1507
01:10:28,892 --> 01:10:31,095
- ...BUT IN EXCELLENT TASTE.
- WOW.

1508
01:10:31,128 --> 01:10:33,097
SHE COULDN'T HELP BEING AMUSED.

1509
01:10:33,130 --> 01:10:35,732
THE STUPID GIRL WAS NOT ONLY
MODELING MRS. MARCH'S
FUTURE WARDROBE...

1510
01:10:35,765 --> 01:10:37,400
[MIKE, ROBOTS
CHATTERING QUIETLY]

1511
01:10:37,433 --> 01:10:39,403
- IT'S A MOVIE FOR ME!
- NO.

1512
01:10:39,437 --> 01:10:43,807
SO FIRM, SO NICELY ROUNDED
IN PLACES MEN LIKE.

1513
01:10:58,955 --> 01:11:00,423
[MAGIC VOICE]
MIKE?

1514
01:11:00,457 --> 01:11:02,660
CROW? SERVO?

1515
01:11:02,693 --> 01:11:04,728
WHERE IS EVERYBODY?

1516
01:11:04,762 --> 01:11:07,130
SURE GETS LONELY
BEING MAGIC VOICE.

1517
01:11:07,163 --> 01:11:10,833
I WISH THERE WAS ANOTHER
DISEMBODIED VOICE AROUND HERE
I COULD TALK TO.

1518
01:11:10,867 --> 01:11:13,470
[FILM NARRATOR]
WELL, SOMETIMES IT'S CONVENIENT
TO HAVE A MAN,

1519
01:11:13,503 --> 01:11:16,107
ESPECIALLY WHEN HE COMES
CHEAPER THAN SERVANTS.

1520
01:11:16,140 --> 01:11:18,875
HEY, YOU'RE THE VOICE-OVER GUY
FROM TODAY'S MOVIE.

1521
01:11:18,908 --> 01:11:21,345
TELL ME, WHAT DO YOU LIKE?
WHAT'S YOUR FAVORITE HOBBY?

1522
01:11:21,378 --> 01:11:23,113
MAKING LOVE
TO AN 80-YEAR-OLD WOMAN

1523
01:11:23,147 --> 01:11:25,082
IN THE BODY
OF A 20-YEAR-OLD GIRL.

1524
01:11:25,115 --> 01:11:27,985
EW! HOW COULD YOU DO THAT?

1525
01:11:28,018 --> 01:11:32,222
SHE WAS QUITE HARMLESS
AND, AT TIMES, EVEN AMUSING.

1526
01:11:32,255 --> 01:11:34,925
YOU KNOW, I ONLY MET YOU
A FEW SECONDS AGO,

1527
01:11:34,958 --> 01:11:36,693
BUT YOU'RE REALLY YUCKY.

1528
01:11:36,727 --> 01:11:38,728
I CAN ONLY IMAGINE
WHAT YOU THINK OF ME.

1529
01:11:38,762 --> 01:11:42,933
SO FIRM, SO NICELY ROUNDED
IN PLACES MEN LIKE.

1530
01:11:42,967 --> 01:11:45,568
THAT'S IT.
GET LOST, LOSER.

1531
01:11:45,602 --> 01:11:48,072
JEEZ. FROM NOW ON,
I'M GONNA FORGET ABOUT ROMANCE

1532
01:11:48,105 --> 01:11:50,340
AND JUST GET LOST IN MY WORK.

1533
01:11:50,373 --> 01:11:54,010
COMMERCIAL SIGN IN FIVE,
FOUR, THREE, TWO--

1534
01:11:54,043 --> 01:11:56,247
COMMERCIAL SIGN NOW.
MEN!

1535
01:12:03,087 --> 01:12:06,190
- ♪♪ [HUMMING]
- YOU MIGHT HAVE KNOCKED
WHEN YOU CAME IN, VICTOR.

1536
01:12:06,223 --> 01:12:07,925
- I MIGHT HAVE, YEAH.
- I'M SORRY.

1537
01:12:07,958 --> 01:12:11,362
DON'T STOP YOUR STYLE SHOW
ON MY ACCOUNT.

1538
01:12:11,395 --> 01:12:16,032
DOES MY, UH...
DISTURB YOU?

1539
01:12:16,065 --> 01:12:18,568
- HETTY, THAT'S UNKIND.
- SHUT UP.

1540
01:12:18,602 --> 01:12:20,570
THE BLOOM IS DEFINITELY
OFF THE ROSE.

1541
01:12:20,603 --> 01:12:25,475
YOU SEE, IT'S HARD FOR A VAIN,
STUPID MAN TO REALIZE

1542
01:12:25,508 --> 01:12:29,312
THAT HE HOLDS NO ATTRACTION
FOR A LOVELY YOUNG GIRL.

1543
01:12:29,345 --> 01:12:31,715
- OOH, BURN.
- WELL, I CAN SEE WHERE
IT WOULD BE--

1544
01:12:31,748 --> 01:12:35,118
YOU'RE NOT NEEDED NOW, VICTOR.

1545
01:12:35,152 --> 01:12:39,790
CLOSE THE DOOR QUIETLY
WHEN YOU GO OUT.

1546
01:12:39,823 --> 01:12:42,458
I'M NOT GOING
TO BE NEEDED AT ALL.

1547
01:12:42,492 --> 01:12:46,230
- NOPE.
- THAT'S WHAT YOU'RE SAYING,
ISN'T IT?

1548
01:12:46,263 --> 01:12:48,565
- AFTER TOMORROW, WHEN--
- VICTOR!

1549
01:12:48,598 --> 01:12:52,068
- SIT!
- THAT'S ENOUGH!

1550
01:12:52,102 --> 01:12:54,070
- GET OUT!
- NOT IN FRONT
OF THE WHITE SLAVE.

1551
01:12:54,103 --> 01:12:56,005
IT'S THE WAY IT'S GOING TO BE
WHEN WHAT?

1552
01:12:56,038 --> 01:12:58,842
UH, WHEN WE HAVE THE PICNIC,
WHICH IS...
[CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY]

1553
01:12:58,875 --> 01:13:02,813
THROWN AWAY LIKE AN OLD SHOE.
POOR OLD VICTOR.

1554
01:13:02,847 --> 01:13:05,815
[MRS. MARCH]
DON'T ASK TIRESOME QUESTIONS.

1555
01:13:05,848 --> 01:13:08,485
- I COULD SNAP YOUR NECK.
- THAT WILL BE ENOUGH
FOR TONIGHT.

1556
01:13:08,518 --> 01:13:12,288
I WANT US BOTH TO GET SOME REST.
TRY TO SLEEP.

1557
01:13:12,322 --> 01:13:14,758
- BUT, MRS. MARCH--
- THAT'S AN ORDER!

1558
01:13:14,792 --> 01:13:16,927
DO AS I SAY!

1559
01:13:16,960 --> 01:13:19,497
YOU'RE GONNA PUT
YOUR BRAIN IN ME, AREN'T YOU?

1560
01:13:19,530 --> 01:13:21,998
I JUST KNOW IT.

1561
01:13:22,032 --> 01:13:23,833
[MOCK GRUNTING]

1562
01:13:23,867 --> 01:13:26,970
I SHOULD GET THE LARGER BOTTLES.
MORE ECONOMICAL.

1563
01:13:32,542 --> 01:13:34,578
VIC, HI.

1564
01:13:34,612 --> 01:13:37,347
THERE'S SOMEONE
WHO WANTS MONEY AT THE DOOR.

1565
01:13:39,783 --> 01:13:42,252
[SLURRED]
YOU'RE NOT LOOKING FOR ME,
ARE YOU?

1566
01:13:42,285 --> 01:13:45,255
WHY WOULD A PRETTY YOUNG GIRL
WANT TO BE AROUND AN OLD MAN?

1567
01:13:45,288 --> 01:13:47,257
[SLURRED GIBBERISH]

1568
01:13:47,290 --> 01:13:49,158
WHAT DID YOU TRY
TO TELL MRS. MARSH?

1569
01:13:49,192 --> 01:13:52,395
YOU DIDN'T HAVE TO SLEEP
WITH THE CRYPTKEEPER
EVERY NIGHT LIKE ME.

1570
01:13:52,428 --> 01:13:55,132
SO THAT'S WHAT YOU
PLANNED TO DO--

1571
01:13:55,165 --> 01:13:57,868
GET RID OF OLD VICTOR
ONCE YOU GET ALL THAT MONEY.

1572
01:13:57,902 --> 01:14:00,103
- I'M DRUNK.
- THE ONLY THING IS,

1573
01:14:00,137 --> 01:14:02,105
OF COURSE,
IT WON'T REALLY BE YOU.

1574
01:14:02,138 --> 01:14:04,808
WHAT WILL I DO
WITH A LITTLE IMPLANT NOW?

1575
01:14:04,842 --> 01:14:08,012
- OH!
- VICTOR, PLEASE TELL ME.

1576
01:14:08,045 --> 01:14:11,582
- TRY TO MAKE SENSE.
- I AM TELLING YOU.

1577
01:14:11,615 --> 01:14:14,450
TOMORROW, YOU'LL BE ONE OF
THE RICHEST WOMEN
IN THE WORLD.

1578
01:14:14,483 --> 01:14:16,453
YOU'RE GONNA BE OPRAH.

1579
01:14:16,487 --> 01:14:20,057
HERE'S A PRESS RELEASE.
IT'S IN THE MAILS NOW.

1580
01:14:20,090 --> 01:14:23,093
TO ALL THE MAJOR
NEWS SYNDICATES.

1581
01:14:23,127 --> 01:14:26,563
"ORPHAN GIRL SOLE HEIR
TO MARCH MILLIONS."

1582
01:14:26,597 --> 01:14:30,600
- AND BRAIN.
- "NINA RHODES IS A LUCKY STAR."

1583
01:14:30,633 --> 01:14:33,103
WELL, THIS IS
A TERRIBLE PRESS RELEASE.

1584
01:14:34,938 --> 01:14:36,907
I DON'T UNDERSTAND.

1585
01:14:36,940 --> 01:14:38,942
THE NEXT PRESS RELEASE
WILL BE:

1586
01:14:38,975 --> 01:14:42,478
"MARCH MANSION
DESTROYED BY FIRE.

1587
01:14:42,512 --> 01:14:45,282
"CINDERELLA GIRL, NINA RHODES,

1588
01:14:45,315 --> 01:14:47,183
SOLE SURVIVOR."

1589
01:14:47,217 --> 01:14:50,487
- ONLY IT WON'T BE YOU.
- IS THIS WHAT'S KNOWN
AS SINGING LIKE A CANARY?

1590
01:14:50,520 --> 01:14:53,323
- YES.
- IT'S A PITY TOO.

1591
01:14:53,357 --> 01:14:55,025
YOU'RE NICE THE WAY YOU ARE.

1592
01:14:55,058 --> 01:14:56,827
I'M DRUNK!

1593
01:14:59,262 --> 01:15:01,565
PLEASE DON'T LET IT HAPPEN.

1594
01:15:01,598 --> 01:15:04,233
YOU COULD HELP ME AND BEA
GET AWAY.

1595
01:15:04,267 --> 01:15:05,802
OKAY. I WILL.

1596
01:15:05,835 --> 01:15:07,905
WHEN YOU'RE A RICH WOMAN,

1597
01:15:07,938 --> 01:15:10,307
YOU WOULDN'T FORGET
AN OLD FRIEND,

1598
01:15:10,340 --> 01:15:12,375
A FRIEND WHO SAVED YOUR LIFE,
WOULD YOU?

1599
01:15:12,408 --> 01:15:14,845
UH, GIVE ME AN EXAMPLE.

1600
01:15:16,480 --> 01:15:19,448
- OH...
- OH, NO. HELP ME
TO THE BATHROOM.

1601
01:15:19,482 --> 01:15:21,685
GET OUT TO THE CAR
AND STAY THERE.

1602
01:15:21,718 --> 01:15:24,287
VICTOR, BEA TOO.
BEA MUST COME TOO.

1603
01:15:24,320 --> 01:15:26,457
- I'M SOBER NOW.
- ONE MINUTE.

1604
01:15:26,490 --> 01:15:28,125
HEY.

1605
01:15:28,158 --> 01:15:31,662
- SO, MIKE,
WHERE'S THE ATOMIC BRAIN?
- I DON'T KNOW.

1606
01:15:31,695 --> 01:15:34,063
DEAR HELOISE,

1607
01:15:34,097 --> 01:15:36,833
HERE'S A TIP FOR ORGANIZING
YOUR SPICE RACK.

1608
01:15:36,867 --> 01:15:39,670
HUH?

1609
01:15:39,703 --> 01:15:44,273
JAR LIDS
SCREWED ONTO A LAZY SUSAN
WILL ADEQUATELY SUFFICE.

1610
01:15:44,307 --> 01:15:45,775
SIGN THIS.

1611
01:15:45,808 --> 01:15:47,743
SIGN THE PEN?

1612
01:15:51,013 --> 01:15:52,482
HURRY.

1613
01:15:52,515 --> 01:15:54,685
OW, OW, OW, OW.
DON'T SIGN THE HAND.

1614
01:15:54,718 --> 01:15:56,052
OW!

1615
01:15:58,922 --> 01:16:01,057
OH, MY ULCER'S ACTING UP.

1616
01:16:01,090 --> 01:16:03,760
OH, OH.
LET'S SEE HERE.

1617
01:16:03,793 --> 01:16:05,995
"LICK ME, FAT BOY."
HEY, WAIT A MINUTE!

1618
01:16:09,598 --> 01:16:12,302
[FOREIGN ACCENT]
VERY INTERESTING.

1619
01:16:12,335 --> 01:16:14,003
♪♪ [HARPSICHORD]

1620
01:16:14,037 --> 01:16:16,005
THELONIOUS.

1621
01:16:16,038 --> 01:16:18,842
- LOOKS LIKE ROY SCHEIDER.
- [LAUGHS]

1622
01:16:25,282 --> 01:16:27,950
DEAR MRS. MARCH,
BY THE TIME I READ THIS,

1623
01:16:27,983 --> 01:16:30,120
YOU'LL BE DEAD.

1624
01:16:30,153 --> 01:16:32,655
I'M GOING TO KILL
TREVOR PINNOCK!

1625
01:16:32,688 --> 01:16:34,157
♪♪ [CONTINUES]

1626
01:16:34,190 --> 01:16:36,893
LORD, I KNOW I HAVEN'T BEEN
THE BEST GIGOLO,

1627
01:16:36,927 --> 01:16:39,195
BUT I'VE BEEN THE BEST GIGOLO
I KNOW HOW.

1628
01:16:39,228 --> 01:16:41,998
KNIT ONE, PURL DIE!

1629
01:16:43,200 --> 01:16:44,433
[STAMMERS]

1630
01:16:44,467 --> 01:16:45,868
OH, GOT A NEEDLE...

1631
01:16:45,902 --> 01:16:47,470
[MUTTERING]

1632
01:16:48,738 --> 01:16:51,040
OH, THAT WAS MY FAVORITE
DARNING NEEDLE.

1633
01:16:51,073 --> 01:16:52,542
DARN!

1634
01:16:52,575 --> 01:16:54,377
HI. I'M DARREN McGAVIN.

1635
01:16:54,410 --> 01:16:56,380
HEY, YOU COULD DO
A CHIN PUPPET ON HIM, MIKE.

1636
01:16:56,413 --> 01:16:59,382
- CHIN...
- EAT STEEL, LOVER BOY.

1637
01:16:59,415 --> 01:17:01,283
BEA, YOU'VE GOT
TO COME WITH ME.

1638
01:17:01,317 --> 01:17:03,620
NO. I WON'T GO.

1639
01:17:03,653 --> 01:17:06,490
I DON'T WANT TO GO ON
LIVING LIKE THIS.

1640
01:17:06,523 --> 01:17:08,025
BY THE WAY, I'M BEHIND YOU.

1641
01:17:08,058 --> 01:17:11,762
I'LL GET VICTOR TO HELP ME,
AND WE WILL CARRY YOU.

1642
01:17:11,795 --> 01:17:14,630
YEAH, WELL, ANYWAY,
IT'S SO COMFORTING
TO HAVE YOU HERE.

1643
01:17:14,663 --> 01:17:16,400
THANKS FOR STAYING.

1644
01:17:19,635 --> 01:17:22,105
- [SCREAMS]
- DOH!

1645
01:17:22,138 --> 01:17:25,108
NO, NO. DON'T BE ALARMED.
JUST DOING MY YOGA.

1646
01:17:25,142 --> 01:17:28,678
[MRS. MARCH]
WANT SOMETHING
FROM VICTOR, DEAR?

1647
01:17:28,712 --> 01:17:31,748
- SIT DOWN, MY DEAR.
- WHERE IS SHE?

1648
01:17:31,782 --> 01:17:35,152
I'M AFRAID YOU'RE WEARING
YOURSELF OUT WITH ALL THIS
RUSHING AROUND.

1649
01:17:35,185 --> 01:17:37,153
- AH.
- I DON'T LIKE THAT.

1650
01:17:37,187 --> 01:17:40,390
[NINA]
YOU REALIZE SHE'S MAD,
DON'T YOU, DR. FRANK?

1651
01:17:40,423 --> 01:17:42,692
- RELAX.
- [MRS. MARCH] HURRY, DOCTOR.

1652
01:17:44,160 --> 01:17:46,697
YOU'VE GOT SNOTOMS.

1653
01:17:46,730 --> 01:17:49,900
I'LL BE READY FOR YOU SHORTLY,
MRS. MARCH.

1654
01:17:49,933 --> 01:17:51,935
[MRS. MARCH]
I'LL BE WAITING.

1655
01:17:51,968 --> 01:17:54,403
- [IMITATING WHIRRING SOUND]
- BLOOP.

1656
01:17:54,437 --> 01:17:57,240
MRS. PARTRIDGE.

1657
01:17:57,273 --> 01:18:00,410
- I LIKE HER.
- OH. [MUTTERS]

1658
01:18:00,443 --> 01:18:04,413
WHAT ARE THE ODDS WE BOTH
GO DOWN WITH HIP POINTERS
ON THE SAME DAY?

1659
01:18:04,447 --> 01:18:06,817
FINALLY ABOUT TO HAPPEN.

1660
01:18:06,850 --> 01:18:08,985
WHAT'S ABOUT TO HAPPEN?

1661
01:18:10,720 --> 01:18:14,423
YOU DON'T KNOW
WHAT IT'S BEEN LIKE FOR ME,

1662
01:18:14,457 --> 01:18:17,760
LIVING WITH THIS UGLY BODY
OF MINE.

1663
01:18:17,793 --> 01:18:20,163
- OH, HERE COMES THE DIATRIBE.
- [SIGHS]

1664
01:18:20,197 --> 01:18:23,500
KNOWING THAT ANY ATTENTION
I RECEIVED

1665
01:18:23,533 --> 01:18:27,470
WAS NOT FOR ME
BUT MY MONEY.

1666
01:18:27,503 --> 01:18:30,373
- YEAH, AND YOUR BUNS OF STEEL.
- [CROW WHISPERING]

1667
01:18:30,407 --> 01:18:34,177
- WELL, NOBODY GOT ANY OF IT.
- [TOM SERVO WHISPERING]

1668
01:18:34,210 --> 01:18:35,578
NO.

1669
01:18:37,647 --> 01:18:39,548
WELL, LET'S HAVE AT IT THEN.

1670
01:18:39,582 --> 01:18:42,952
I'VE NEVER KNOW WHAT IT WAS LIKE
TO BE LOVED--

1671
01:18:42,985 --> 01:18:44,822
OH, GOD!
[SIGHS]

1672
01:18:44,855 --> 01:18:48,158
...FOR MYSELF ALONE.

1673
01:18:48,192 --> 01:18:50,993
WHY DID YOU KILL VICTOR,
MRS. MARCH?

1674
01:18:51,027 --> 01:18:54,563
- VICTOR?
- VICTOR? WHICH ONE WAS HE?

1675
01:18:54,597 --> 01:18:57,500
VICTOR WAS A FOOL!

1676
01:18:57,533 --> 01:19:01,037
OKAY. I WAS JUST WONDERING.

1677
01:19:01,070 --> 01:19:04,073
I'M A PRACTICAL WOMAN,
DR. FRANK.

1678
01:19:04,107 --> 01:19:06,142
NOW LOP MY HEAD OFF.

1679
01:19:06,175 --> 01:19:07,643
A BUSINESSWOMAN.

1680
01:19:07,677 --> 01:19:10,480
I'VE NEVER BEEN
A VERY PRACTICAL PERSON.

1681
01:19:10,513 --> 01:19:13,115
I SUPPOSE THAT MAKES ME
A FOOL, TOO, IN YOUR EYES.

1682
01:19:13,148 --> 01:19:15,952
- OF COURSE NOT!
- RELAX, MRS. MARCH.

1683
01:19:15,985 --> 01:19:18,622
NOW, NOW, NOW, NOW,
DON'T LEVITATE NOW.

1684
01:19:27,330 --> 01:19:31,167
NOW, LET'S MAKE SURE THERE'S
A NICE BIG AIR BUBBLE IN HERE.

1685
01:19:31,200 --> 01:19:33,470
- [GASPS]
- OH, THAT'S GOOD.

1686
01:19:33,503 --> 01:19:36,673
IT'S LIKE I'M KISSING GOD.
OH, YES. OH!

1687
01:19:36,707 --> 01:19:39,375
YOU'RE IN GOOD HANDS.

1688
01:19:39,408 --> 01:19:42,078
- SHE HAD GIZZARDS IN HER HEAD.
- [ELECTRICITY ARCING]

1689
01:19:42,112 --> 01:19:44,580
OH, I GOT A BRAIN
LEFT OVER NOW.

1690
01:19:45,982 --> 01:19:49,987
- SEE? HER CEREBELLUM--
ALL RUSTED HERE.
- YEAH.

1691
01:19:50,020 --> 01:19:53,957
- OH, IT'S GRISTLY THE CAT.
- MEOW.

1692
01:19:53,990 --> 01:19:56,358
- [ARCING CONTINUES]
- [LIQUID BUBBLING]

1693
01:19:56,392 --> 01:19:59,228
HALFWAY THROUGH THIS,
I HAVE NO IDEA WHAT I'M DOING.

1694
01:20:01,965 --> 01:20:04,067
[IMITATING LIQUID BUBBLING]

1695
01:20:05,135 --> 01:20:07,037
SO, ANYWAY, NINA,
AM I BORING YOU?

1696
01:20:07,070 --> 01:20:09,305
JUST TELL ME, WILL YOU? I...

1697
01:20:11,007 --> 01:20:13,743
YOU KNOW, GUYS,
I WANNA GO TO EGYPT.

1698
01:20:13,777 --> 01:20:15,412
SEE THE SIGHTS.

1699
01:20:15,445 --> 01:20:18,515
[DR. FRANK, MUFFLED SOUNDING]
WAKING UP, ARE YOU? GOOD.

1700
01:20:18,548 --> 01:20:22,718
- I WANNA TALK TO YOU.
- IS HE EATING A SANDWICH?

1701
01:20:22,752 --> 01:20:25,222
[IMITATING CHOMPING SOUNDS]

1702
01:20:25,255 --> 01:20:27,223
[SMACKS LIPS]

1703
01:20:27,257 --> 01:20:30,527
YOU SIGNED A PAPER MAKING VICTOR
YOUR LEGAL GUARDIAN.

1704
01:20:30,560 --> 01:20:33,297
THAT'S RIGHT, ISN'T IT?

1705
01:20:33,330 --> 01:20:36,700
- I DID SIGN SOMETHING,
DIDN'T I?
- MM-HMM.

1706
01:20:36,733 --> 01:20:40,903
- THAT WOULD PROBABLY WORK
AS WELL FOR ME.
- STOP.

1707
01:20:40,937 --> 01:20:43,072
WE COULD STAY HERE.

1708
01:20:43,105 --> 01:20:45,475
NONE OF THIS
WOULD HAVE TO BE DESTROYED.

1709
01:20:45,508 --> 01:20:47,543
WE'D GET A COUCH
AND MAYBE SOME PICTURES.

1710
01:20:47,577 --> 01:20:49,913
- YOU'RE DOING BETTER,
AREN'T YOU?
- [MEOWS]

1711
01:20:49,947 --> 01:20:52,582
WHY DON'T YOU TRY IT
ON YOUR OWN?

1712
01:20:52,615 --> 01:20:55,085
OH, WHY DON'T YOU HOP DOWN AND--
OH, YOU CAN'T.

1713
01:20:55,118 --> 01:20:58,755
I WANNA KNOW IF MRS. MARCH
DIDN'T INTEND BLOWING ME UP

1714
01:20:58,788 --> 01:21:00,757
ALONG WITH
ALL THE REST OF THIS.

1715
01:21:00,790 --> 01:21:02,658
HOW DOES THAT GUY
REACH HIS TIME CLOCK?

1716
01:21:02,692 --> 01:21:05,528
HE CAN'T EVEN PUNCH IN.
[GRUNTING]

1717
01:21:05,562 --> 01:21:07,530
YOU'RE A VERY WEALTHY WOMAN
NOW, NINA.

1718
01:21:07,563 --> 01:21:09,132
BUT YOU HAVE A PORPOISE BRAIN.

1719
01:21:09,165 --> 01:21:13,603
WHAT I MUST DECIDE IS
HOW TO KEEP YOU
AND YOUR FRIENDS AVAILABLE

1720
01:21:13,637 --> 01:21:16,272
WITH THE LEAST AMOUNT
OF NUISANCE TO MYSELF.

1721
01:21:17,573 --> 01:21:20,543
- I COULD KEEP YOU
UNDER SEDATION--
- TRUE.

1722
01:21:20,577 --> 01:21:22,345
...UNTIL YOUR SIGNATURE
WAS REQUIRED.

1723
01:21:22,378 --> 01:21:24,280
YOU MAKE THE CALL.

1724
01:21:24,313 --> 01:21:27,117
OR I COULD REPLACE YOUR BRAIN
WITH ONE MORE AMENABLE.

1725
01:21:27,150 --> 01:21:30,320
- YOU GOT ANYTHING
TO SAY ABOUT THAT?
- JUST JUMP IN ANYTIME.

1726
01:21:30,353 --> 01:21:33,188
WHAT ABOUT MRS. MARCH, DOCTOR?

1727
01:21:33,222 --> 01:21:35,325
MRS. MARCH NO LONGER
HAS A THING TO SAY.

1728
01:21:35,358 --> 01:21:38,060
- SHE DRINKS FROM A BOWL.
- DO YOU, MY DEAR?

1729
01:21:38,093 --> 01:21:42,065
SHE'S TOO BUSY LICKING HER BUTT.

1730
01:21:42,098 --> 01:21:45,335
COMPLETELY RECOVERED, I'D SAY.
HOW DO YOU FEEL?

1731
01:21:45,368 --> 01:21:47,103
- [SNARLS, HISSES]
- DON'T PATRONIZE ME!

1732
01:21:51,040 --> 01:21:52,508
I'M MAD.

1733
01:21:52,542 --> 01:21:55,978
I GUESS A TRANSPLANT
WOULD BE BETTER.
IT WON'T HURT.

1734
01:21:56,012 --> 01:21:58,315
AND THE PRICE IS REALLY NOT
AS BAD AS YOU THINK.

1735
01:21:58,348 --> 01:21:59,950
[ELECTRICITY ARCING]

1736
01:22:01,117 --> 01:22:02,418
♪♪ [WHISTLING]

1737
01:22:02,452 --> 01:22:05,388
DR. FRANK HAD ENJOYED
THIS TRANSPLANTATION--

1738
01:22:05,422 --> 01:22:09,092
MRS. MARCH'S BRAIN WINDING UP
IN THE BODY OF A CAT.

1739
01:22:09,125 --> 01:22:11,093
HEY, VOICE-OVER GUY,
I'M TRYING TO WORK.

1740
01:22:11,127 --> 01:22:14,197
POETIC JUSTICE TO THINK
OF AUTOCRATIC MRS. MARCH

1741
01:22:14,230 --> 01:22:17,733
SCAVENGING IN BACK-ALLEY
GARBAGE CANS FOR HER DINNER.

1742
01:22:17,767 --> 01:22:21,905
I THINK I GOT ANOTHER BRAIN
IN THE STOREROOM HERE.

1743
01:22:21,938 --> 01:22:25,375
- [DOOR THUDS LOUDLY]
- HUH?

1744
01:22:25,408 --> 01:22:27,377
[YOWLING SOFTLY]

1745
01:22:27,410 --> 01:22:29,912
BUT MRS. MARCH DOESN'T
TAKE THINGS LYING DOWN.

1746
01:22:29,945 --> 01:22:32,015
OH, NO, NO, NO, NO, NO.

1747
01:22:34,017 --> 01:22:36,920
[YOWLING CONTINUES]

1748
01:22:36,953 --> 01:22:39,222
HUH? THE HELL--

1749
01:22:45,595 --> 01:22:47,697
- IN A CAMEO APPEARANCE...
- [CHUCKLES]

1750
01:22:47,730 --> 01:22:50,333
NOW, SEE, THIS IS WHY
I DON'T LIKE CATS.

1751
01:22:50,367 --> 01:22:51,500
[LAUGHS]

1752
01:22:51,533 --> 01:22:54,137
THEY'LL BLOW UP
A NUCLEAR PILE ON YOU.

1753
01:22:54,170 --> 01:22:56,238
PLEASE, NO--
YOU FORGOT THE FABRIC SOFTENER.

1754
01:22:56,272 --> 01:22:57,373
- [DOOR RATTLING]
- [COUGHING]

1755
01:23:00,243 --> 01:23:02,712
MORE MILK EVERY NIGHT.
TUNA. LOTS OF TUNA.

1756
01:23:02,745 --> 01:23:04,213
COME ON. COME ON.

1757
01:23:04,247 --> 01:23:06,082
[POUNDING ON DOOR]

1758
01:23:08,885 --> 01:23:10,487
♪♪ [WHISTLING]

1759
01:23:10,520 --> 01:23:12,422
HE'S JUST IN A MACHINE SHED.

1760
01:23:12,455 --> 01:23:14,757
I'LL SHRINK IF I'M DRIED! OH!

1761
01:23:18,293 --> 01:23:20,763
WHOA. NINA, YOU RUN INTO
THE BED THERE?

1762
01:23:20,797 --> 01:23:23,667
YOU ALL RIGHT? NINA? NINA?

1763
01:23:26,970 --> 01:23:28,270
OOH-AAH!
[LAUGHS]

1764
01:23:28,303 --> 01:23:30,573
YABBA-DABBA-DOO.
[LAUGHS]

1765
01:23:30,607 --> 01:23:32,408
KICK ME.

1766
01:23:34,577 --> 01:23:37,647
OKAY, OKAY. MY IMPRESSION
OF THE SCALES OF JUSTICE LADY.

1767
01:23:37,680 --> 01:23:41,317
WHERE ARE MY SCALES? THANK YOU.
I'M THE SCALES OF JUSTICE LADY.

1768
01:23:41,350 --> 01:23:44,153
- WHOA! WAS SHE HIT
BY A METEORITE?
- WHOA.

1769
01:23:44,187 --> 01:23:47,623
[ELECTRICITY CONTINUES ARCING]

1770
01:23:47,657 --> 01:23:51,393
- OH, THAT'S WHAT HAPPENS WHEN
YOU DRINK IN A HOT TUB, FOLKS.
- YEP, YEP.

1771
01:23:53,963 --> 01:23:55,798
OH! OH!

1772
01:23:55,832 --> 01:23:59,468
RADIATION ON AN OPEN SORE.
JUST LIKE LEMON JUICE.

1773
01:23:59,502 --> 01:24:01,170
OH, WELL,
THANKS FOR RESCUING ME.

1774
01:24:01,203 --> 01:24:03,773
BUT YOU COULD PUT A SHEET
OVER THAT THING. EW.

1775
01:24:03,807 --> 01:24:06,175
♪♪ [IMITATING DRAMATIC
SOUNDTRACK MUSIC]

1776
01:24:06,208 --> 01:24:08,177
YOU'VE GOT JUST ENOUGH TIME
TO CHANGE YOUR PUMPS.

1777
01:24:08,210 --> 01:24:11,180
THEY'RE ALL WRONG.

1778
01:24:11,213 --> 01:24:14,317
OH, YOU KNOW,
AS LONG AS I'M HERE,
I'M GONNA GRAB MY EYE. OOH!

1779
01:24:14,350 --> 01:24:16,685
[CRIES OUT]

1780
01:24:16,718 --> 01:24:19,022
- ♪♪ [HUMMING]
- [RUMBLING]

1781
01:24:23,527 --> 01:24:25,962
♪ JOSHUA FIT THE BATTLE
OF JERICHO ♪

1782
01:24:25,995 --> 01:24:28,697
- ♪ JERICHO ♪
- ♪♪ [HUMMING]

1783
01:24:31,767 --> 01:24:35,172
- [GROWLING]
- ♪ IT'S MY HEART
THAT'S A-SUFFERIN' ♪

1784
01:24:37,140 --> 01:24:39,108
EW, HE DROOLED.

1785
01:24:39,142 --> 01:24:41,510
EHH. WHAT A DAY.

1786
01:24:41,543 --> 01:24:45,882
NOW SHE'LL STEP INTO A RATTRAP,
GET HIT BY LIGHTNING,
MEET THE HUDSON BROTHERS.

1787
01:24:45,915 --> 01:24:47,483
[LAUGHS]

1788
01:24:47,517 --> 01:24:49,952
WELL, THERE GOES THAT THING.

1789
01:24:52,855 --> 01:24:54,623
OH, NO. TARA.

1790
01:24:54,657 --> 01:24:58,027
MRS. MARCH DID NOT INTEND
TO LET HER MONEY
GET OUT OF SIGHT.

1791
01:24:58,060 --> 01:24:59,862
SHE WOULD FOLLOW THAT GIRL.

1792
01:24:59,895 --> 01:25:02,765
SOMETIME, SOMEPLACE,

1793
01:25:02,798 --> 01:25:04,400
REVENGE WOULD COME.

1794
01:25:04,433 --> 01:25:06,302
BUT THAT'S THE SUBJECT
OF THE SEQUEL.

1795
01:25:06,335 --> 01:25:09,572
IT'S IN DEVELOPMENT RIGHT NOW,
AND WE'VE GOT TO DO
A MEMO AND...

1796
01:25:11,207 --> 01:25:13,375
I SUGGEST
THEY PLACATE THE OLD WOMAN

1797
01:25:13,408 --> 01:25:15,845
WITH A LITTLE FANCY FEAST.

1798
01:25:15,878 --> 01:25:18,380
- [TOM SERVO SHOUTING IN GERMAN]
- [MIKE SHOUTS]

1799
01:25:18,413 --> 01:25:20,450
[IMITATING GUNFIRE]

1800
01:25:25,053 --> 01:25:27,523
[MIKE]
THE 400 BLOWS.

1801
01:25:27,557 --> 01:25:30,025
[YOWLS]

1802
01:25:30,058 --> 01:25:32,862
PLEASE LET ME DIE.

1803
01:25:32,895 --> 01:25:35,298
OH, SHAME ON YOU,
JOSEPH MASCELLLI.

1804
01:25:35,332 --> 01:25:39,102
BAD DIRECTOR! BAD!
[GRUNTING]

1805
01:25:39,135 --> 01:25:41,370
THE 7:00 NEWS.

1806
01:25:41,403 --> 01:25:43,472
JACK POLLEXFEN.

1807
01:25:45,342 --> 01:25:47,643
YES, MRS. DWIGGINS.
[CHUCKLES]

1808
01:25:47,677 --> 01:25:50,380
END THE MOVIE, MRS. DWIGGINS.

1809
01:25:52,048 --> 01:25:54,750
OH, HE CAME UP WITH...
♪♪ [HUMMING PART
OF SOUNDTRACK MUSIC]

1810
01:25:54,783 --> 01:25:57,253
♪♪ [ROBOTS JOIN IN]

1811
01:25:57,287 --> 01:26:01,490
FINE. FINE.
NO USE CALLING ATTENTION
TO YOURSELF.

1812
01:26:01,523 --> 01:26:02,992
JEEZ.

1813
01:26:04,993 --> 01:26:06,462
♪♪ [HUMMING SOUNDTRACK MUSIC]

1814
01:26:06,495 --> 01:26:08,063
I'M GONNA BE CHARITABLE
AND JUST SAY

1815
01:26:08,097 --> 01:26:10,800
I HOPE ALL THESE PEOPLE
WERE FORCED TO DO THIS MOVIE
AT GUNPOINT.

1816
01:26:10,833 --> 01:26:12,602
NO, THEY CHOSE TO DO THIS MOVIE.

1817
01:26:12,635 --> 01:26:14,003
ALL EXCEPT FOR XERXES THE CAT.

1818
01:26:14,037 --> 01:26:16,205
YOU KNOW, XERXES WENT ON TO
A LONG AND EXTINGUISHED CAREER.

1819
01:26:16,238 --> 01:26:18,273
HE WAS A FAVORITE
OF NICHOLAS RAY'S,
AND THEN HE APPEARS

1820
01:26:18,307 --> 01:26:19,975
COURTESY OF DAVID O. SELZNICK...

1821
01:26:35,592 --> 01:26:38,193
- ♪♪ [MIKE SINGING]
- MIKE! MIKE!

1822
01:26:38,227 --> 01:26:39,928
MI-MI-MI-MIKE!
[TRILLS]

1823
01:26:39,962 --> 01:26:41,932
- MIKE, MIKE, MIKE.
- YES, ELEANOR?

1824
01:26:41,965 --> 01:26:43,733
- READY?
- I WAS BORN READY.

1825
01:26:43,767 --> 01:26:45,768
OH, OKAY.
OH, KALOO KALAY.

1826
01:26:45,802 --> 01:26:47,570
- OKAY, TOM, HIT IT.
- READY.

1827
01:26:47,603 --> 01:26:48,905
[CLEARS THROAT]

1828
01:26:48,938 --> 01:26:51,140
DR. RICHARD KIMBLE
IS A FUGITIVE

1829
01:26:51,173 --> 01:26:52,575
ON THE RUN FROM THE LAW.

1830
01:26:52,608 --> 01:26:54,177
BUT IN ANOTHER PART
OF THE WORLD,

1831
01:26:54,210 --> 01:26:57,313
GREEN ACRES' HANK KIMBALL
IS ALSO ON THE RUN FROM THE LAW.

1832
01:26:57,347 --> 01:26:58,815
♪♪ [HUMMING]

1833
01:26:58,848 --> 01:27:01,550
AH, OH, UH, MR. NELSON,
UH, I'M ON THE RUN.

1834
01:27:01,583 --> 01:27:03,318
WELL, UH, NOT ACTUALLY
ON THE RUN.

1835
01:27:03,352 --> 01:27:05,722
I'M, UH, BEING PURSUED,
AND I'M WALKING QUICKLY.

1836
01:27:05,755 --> 01:27:07,823
YOU SEE,
I'M IN FLIGHT FROM THE LAW.

1837
01:27:07,857 --> 01:27:10,593
WELL, NOT THE WHOLE LAW.
UH, ACTUALLY,
JUST PARTS OF THE LAW.

1838
01:27:10,627 --> 01:27:12,762
WHEN I SAY "PARTS,"
I SHOULD REALLY SAY "MEN."

1839
01:27:12,795 --> 01:27:14,830
NOT TO SAY THERE AREN'T WOMEN
IN THE POLICE FORCE.

1840
01:27:14,863 --> 01:27:17,433
THERE ARE SOME WOMEN.
I'M JUST NOT SURE
OF THE RATIO.

1841
01:27:17,467 --> 01:27:19,268
I'M ALSO BEING FOLLOWED
BY A ONE-ARMED MAN,

1842
01:27:19,302 --> 01:27:21,070
OR A MAN WITH A PROSTHETIC ARM.

1843
01:27:21,103 --> 01:27:23,372
I'M SURE HE HAD TWO ARMS
WHEN HE WAS BORN.

1844
01:27:23,405 --> 01:27:25,575
WELL, THANKS VERY MUCH.
GOOD NIGHT.

1845
01:27:25,608 --> 01:27:26,977
- ♪♪ [HUMMING]
- BOY! MM!

1846
01:27:27,010 --> 01:27:28,143
- CROW BUDDY--
- WOW.

1847
01:27:28,177 --> 01:27:30,245
...YOU SET A STOOL DOWN
NEXT TO THAT PREMISE

1848
01:27:30,278 --> 01:27:32,415
AND JUST MILKED IT
FOR EVERYTHING IT WAS WORTH.

1849
01:27:32,448 --> 01:27:34,050
- MOO.
- WELL, THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

1850
01:27:34,083 --> 01:27:35,685
- GOOD JOB.
- OH.

1851
01:27:35,718 --> 01:27:37,120
OKAY.
WE GOT A BUNCH OF LETTERS.

1852
01:27:37,153 --> 01:27:39,855
- LETTERS. OH, I LOVE LETTERS.
- DELICIOUS LETTERS.

1853
01:27:39,888 --> 01:27:41,857
AND, UH-- WELL,
LET'S START WITH THIS ONE HERE.

1854
01:27:41,890 --> 01:27:43,860
THIS FIRST ONE'S
FROM ERIC HALLORAN.

1855
01:27:43,893 --> 01:27:47,297
- PUT THAT UP ON
STILL STORE THERE, CAMBOT.
- HI, ERIC.

1856
01:27:47,330 --> 01:27:49,165
ERIC SAYS,
"DEAR SATELLITE OF LOVE"--

1857
01:27:49,198 --> 01:27:52,102
- WHICH IS A GOOD START--
"I'M A 13-YEAR-OLD BOY, AND"--
- [MUTTERING]

1858
01:27:52,135 --> 01:27:53,737
- PLEASE. IT'S ANNOYING.
- SORRY.

1859
01:27:53,770 --> 01:27:55,505
EVERY TIME I READ THE PAPER--
"I'M WRITING TO SAY

1860
01:27:55,538 --> 01:27:58,040
"I REALLY ENJOY THE SHOW,
AND I REALLY THINK
IT'S A LAUGH RIOT.

1861
01:27:58,073 --> 01:28:00,543
- [LAUGHS]
- I'M ALSO WRITING
TO ASK A QUESTION." HERE WE GO.

1862
01:28:00,577 --> 01:28:04,047
- OKAY.
- "WHAT DOES THE 'K' STAND FOR
IN MST3K"?

1863
01:28:04,080 --> 01:28:05,982
UH, I GOT THIS ONE, MIKE.
[CLEARS THROAT]

1864
01:28:06,015 --> 01:28:08,317
ERIC, THE "K" STANDS FOR KARL.

1865
01:28:08,350 --> 01:28:10,587
KARL WAS THE MAN
WHO INVENTED LIGHTNING.

1866
01:28:10,620 --> 01:28:12,522
- THANK YOU VERY MUCH.
- LIGHTNING?

1867
01:28:12,555 --> 01:28:14,323
- YEAH. KARL.
- GOOD ANSWER.

1868
01:28:14,357 --> 01:28:16,058
ALL RIGHT.
WELL, LET'S MOVE ON HERE.

1869
01:28:16,092 --> 01:28:18,127
- OKAY.
- THIS ONE'S KIND
OF A SPECIAL, UH--

1870
01:28:18,160 --> 01:28:20,397
- CHECK THIS OUT. "JUST A LETTER
TO LET YOU KNOW"--
- LET ME SEE.

1871
01:28:20,430 --> 01:28:21,897
THIS ONE'S FROM ANNE FELDSTEIN,
BY THE WAY.

1872
01:28:21,930 --> 01:28:24,333
- WHY DON'T YOU PUT THAT UP?
- HI, ANNE.

1873
01:28:24,367 --> 01:28:26,935
ANNE, THANK YOU FOR WRITING.
"JUST A LETTER
TO LET YOU GUYS KNOW

1874
01:28:26,968 --> 01:28:28,805
- ...HOW MUCH
I LOVE YOUR SHOW"--
- THANK YOU.

1875
01:28:28,838 --> 01:28:30,773
..."AND HOW I ESPECIALLY LOVE
TOMMY-GUN SERVO."

1876
01:28:30,807 --> 01:28:34,443
- WOW.
- "HE IS MY FAVORITE,
AND I LOVE HIS SONGS.

1877
01:28:34,477 --> 01:28:36,245
"IF I COULD BE
ON THE SATELLITE OF LOVE,

1878
01:28:36,278 --> 01:28:38,313
I WOULD SIT AND TALK TO TOM
ALL DAY LONG."

1879
01:28:38,347 --> 01:28:41,217
- OH, ANNE. OH, SWEET ANNE.
- "DEVOTEDLY, ANNE FELDSTEIN."

1880
01:28:41,250 --> 01:28:43,652
- SMELL IT.
- WHO'S THAT FROM?

1881
01:28:43,685 --> 01:28:45,955
- UH, ANNE FELDSTEIN.
- OH, YEAH.

1882
01:28:45,988 --> 01:28:47,757
- FELDSTEIN. YEAH. YEAH.
- ANNE...

1883
01:28:47,790 --> 01:28:50,358
I GOT A BIG STACK OF LETTERS
FROM FELDSTEIN
DOWN IN MY LOCKER.

1884
01:28:50,392 --> 01:28:52,895
- WHAT?
- THAT'S RIGHT.
I GOT A BUNCH FROM HER TOO.

1885
01:28:52,928 --> 01:28:54,897
FINALLY GOT AROUND
TO WRITING YOU, HUH?

1886
01:28:54,930 --> 01:28:57,833
WELL, YOU TROLLOP,
YOU TART, ANNE.
[LAUGHS]

1887
01:28:57,867 --> 01:28:59,602
- HEY.
- THAT'S ANNE.

1888
01:28:59,635 --> 01:29:01,970
- I'M SORRY.
JUST A LITTLE BITTER HERE.
- WE'RE JUST KIDDING.

1889
01:29:02,003 --> 01:29:04,373
- UH, IF WE CAN CONTINUE ON
HERE, PLEASE?
- PLEASE DO.

1890
01:29:04,407 --> 01:29:06,375
- THIS IS FROM ERIC HANSEN.
- ERIC?

1891
01:29:06,408 --> 01:29:08,110
- ANOTHER ERIC.
- ANOTHER ERIC.

1892
01:29:08,143 --> 01:29:10,713
HANSEN, HALLORAN.
I SMELL A CONSPIRACY.

1893
01:29:10,747 --> 01:29:12,715
ANYWAY, PUT THAT LETTER UP.

1894
01:29:12,748 --> 01:29:14,550
- NEAT.
- AND I'LL SHOW YOU
A PICTURE TOO.

1895
01:29:14,583 --> 01:29:16,085
"DEAR LORDS OF LUNAR LAUGHTER"--

1896
01:29:16,118 --> 01:29:18,087
[LAUGHING]
THAT'S US.

1897
01:29:18,120 --> 01:29:20,355
"I AM ONE OF THE MILLIONS
OF FANS, OR MSTies,

1898
01:29:20,388 --> 01:29:23,192
"WHO ARE FORCED TO PUMP
MST3K INTO THEIR VEINS.

1899
01:29:23,225 --> 01:29:25,762
"SO ADDICTED AM I
THAT I HAVE CONSTRUCTED
A ROBOT COMPANION

1900
01:29:25,795 --> 01:29:29,065
"TO ASSIST ME IN ALLEVIATING
THE TRIBULATIONS
OF BAD CINEMATOGRAPHY.

1901
01:29:29,098 --> 01:29:32,402
"MY ROBOT,
OR MORE ACCURATELY, PUPPET,
PICTURED HERE WITH ME

1902
01:29:32,435 --> 01:29:36,238
IS A REPLICA OF TV'S
WISECRACKING CROW
BUILT OUT OF HOUSEHOLD GADGETS."

1903
01:29:36,272 --> 01:29:38,240
AND LET'S PUT
THE PICTURE UP THERE.

1904
01:29:38,273 --> 01:29:41,577
- LOOK AT THAT!
- NOW. THAT'S VERY FLATTERING.

1905
01:29:41,610 --> 01:29:43,245
BUT IT SHOULD BE GOOD,
BECAUSE IF YOU'LL NOTICE,

1906
01:29:43,278 --> 01:29:45,848
THAT'S NOT ERIC AT ALL,
THAT'S GEORGE LUCAS--

1907
01:29:45,882 --> 01:29:46,948
- WOW!
- WHAT?

1908
01:29:46,982 --> 01:29:48,317
...THX DEVELOPER.

1909
01:29:48,350 --> 01:29:50,520
LOOKIT. YOU CAN EVEN SEE
THE GRAYING TEMPLES AT THE SIDE.

1910
01:29:50,553 --> 01:29:53,022
- HOW ABOUT THAT?
- HE JUST SHAVED HIS BEARD
AND TRIED TO FOOL US.

1911
01:29:53,055 --> 01:29:55,157
- AW, GEORGE.
- NO GOOD, GEORGE LUCAS.

1912
01:29:55,190 --> 01:29:57,193
- THANK YOU.
- THAT'S FROM ERIC, ANYWAY.

1913
01:29:57,227 --> 01:30:00,228
- CLEVER, HUH?
- HEY, WHY DON'T YOU DO
THE ADDRESS FOR THE INFO CLUB?

1914
01:30:00,262 --> 01:30:03,132
OKAY. SEND YOUR TINCTURES
AND OTHER MISSIVES TO--

1915
01:30:03,165 --> 01:30:06,102
- LETTERS.
- THE MYSTERY SCIENCE THEATER
INFORMATION CLUB.

1916
01:30:06,135 --> 01:30:08,603
POST OFFICE BOX 5325,

1917
01:30:08,637 --> 01:30:11,507
HOPKINS, MINNESOTA, 55343.

1918
01:30:11,540 --> 01:30:15,377
- DO IT TODAY.
- WELL, I GUESS THAT'S IT.
WHAT DO YOU THINK, MAD GUYS?

1919
01:30:15,410 --> 01:30:17,913
I'M DR. FRANK, PHYSICIAN

1920
01:30:17,947 --> 01:30:20,448
AND BON VIVANT.
[CHUCKLING]

1921
01:30:20,482 --> 01:30:22,618
[DR. FORRESTER]
OH, DR. FRANK,

1922
01:30:22,652 --> 01:30:25,488
THERE'S A DR. FIST
HERE TO SEE YOU.

1923
01:30:25,522 --> 01:30:27,690
WELL, SEND HIM RIGHT IN--

1924
01:30:27,723 --> 01:30:30,493
HEY, WAIT. I'M NOT GONNA FALL
FOR THAT ONE AGAIN.

1925
01:30:30,527 --> 01:30:32,928
HE REALLY WANTS
TO CONSULT WITH YOU, DR. FRANK.

1926
01:30:32,962 --> 01:30:34,897
HE SAYS IT'S VERY IMPORTANT.

1927
01:30:34,930 --> 01:30:36,932
IMPORTANT? CONSULT?

1928
01:30:36,965 --> 01:30:38,700
WELL, I AM A DOCTOR AFTER ALL.

1929
01:30:38,733 --> 01:30:40,570
SEND HIM RIGHT IN.
COME IN.

1930
01:30:40,603 --> 01:30:42,805
[CHUCKLES]
WELL, HELLO, DR. FIST.

1931
01:30:42,838 --> 01:30:45,040
TELL ME, WHAT IS YOUR-- OH!

1932
01:30:46,108 --> 01:30:49,112
SOMETIMES IT'S JUST TOO EASY.

1933
01:31:54,343 --> 01:31:57,078
[SCREAMS]
